ahawlkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/everyday) (w:expel/drive out/drive away) (d:<a> and <hawlkhiat>, drive out, written as one word: that he or they drive out or expel; also of driving a vehicle away) (j:a/hawlkhiat) (r:zd:10696/zd:19671) (q:draft)
ahawlpa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:the driver/its driver/pilot) (d:<a> and <hawlpa> written as one word: the man who drives the vehicle or flies the aircraft just named) (j:a/hawlpa) (r:zd:11296/zd:17952) (q:draft)
ahawlpen = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:driver/the one driving) (d:<a>, <hawl>, drive, and <pen> written as one word: the one who was driving the vehicle, as the topic of the sentence) (j:a/hawl/pen) (r:zd:11472/zd:19530/zd:20056) (q:draft)
ahawlte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:driver/drivers/the one driving) (d:<a> and <hawlte> written as one word: the one or ones who drive the vehicle; said also of a single driver, as in {mawtaw ahawlte tutna}, the driver's seat) (j:a/hawlte) (r:zd:12904/zd:17952/zd:16511) (q:draft)
ahawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:distribute/share out/hand out) (d:<a> and <hawm>, divide, written as one word: he or it distributes, shares out) (j:a/hawm) (r:zd:21862/zd:15972) (q:draft)
ahawm = (i:2) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:empty/hollow) (d:<a> and <hawm>, empty, written as one word: empty, with nothing or nobody inside, or the empty one) (j:a/hawm) (r:zd:11296/zd:16820) (q:draft)
ahawmkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work) (w:distribute/give out) (d:<a> and <hawmkhia> written as one word: he or they distribute something, or the one who distributes it) (j:a/hawmkhia) (r:zd:14531/zd:12210) (q:draft)
ahawmkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/media) (w:distribute/give out/release) (d:<a> and <hawmkhiat> written as one word: he or they distribute or hand out something; also of a supplier of goods and of an artist who releases an album) (j:a/hawmkhiat) (r:zd:20466/zd:19373/zd:13086) (q:draft)
ahbel = (i:1) (t:ppm) (f:everyday) (w:as for in/in) (d:<ah>, in or at, with the particle <bel>, written as one word: marks a place or matter that is set against others, as for in; {Zogam ahbel} is in Zogam, for its part) (j:ah/bel) (r:zd:11401/zd:10821) (q:draft)
aheh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:be angry/get angry) (d:<a> and <heh> written as one word: he, she or they are angry, or the one who is angry; {aheh suak} is become furious) (j:a/heh) (r:zd:24736/zd:19526/zd:19033) (q:draft)
ahehpih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:pity/have mercy on) (d:<a> and <hehpih> written as one word: he pities, or the one who pities; {ahehpih huai} is pitiable) (j:a/hehpih) (r:zd:11619/zd:17372) (q:draft)
ahehpihhuai = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/social) (w:pitiable/pitiful/poor) (d:<a> and <hehpihhuai>, pitiable, written as one word: who is to be pitied; {ahehpihhuai mahmah} is very pitiable) (j:a/hehpihhuai) (r:zd:11619/zd:11058) (q:draft)
ahidiam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:is it/could it be) (d:<ahi>, it is, and the question word <diam> written as one word: closes a question or a doubt, is it so, could it be that) (j:ahi/diam) (r:zd:12504/zd:11256/zd:12776) (q:draft)
ahiding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:ought to be/will be/be likely) (d:<a>, <hi> and <ding> written as one word: what is to be or ought to be; {ahiding mah} is just as it should be, and {ahiding in ummawh} is suspect that it is) (j:a/hi/ding) (r:zd:15493/zd:19676/zd:16391) (q:draft)
ahih hangin = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:but) (d:<ahih>, being so, with <hangin>, although: although that is so; joins two statements that contrast) (r:1.6.8)
ahih mahbangin = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:as/since/being) (d:<ahih>, being so, and <mahbangin>, just as: placed after a noun phrase or clause, as befits one who is that, since it is so; {tua ahih mahbangin} at the head of a sentence is accordingly, that being so) (r:zd:17446/zd:12192) (q:draft)
ahih manun = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:because/since/as) (d:<ahih>, be so, and <manun>, because, the form used when the subject is plural: placed at the end of the clause that gives the reason, because they are or because they do) (r:zd:16340/zd:24320) (q:draft)
ahih nakleh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:whenever it is/as long as it is/when it comes to) (d:<ahih>, being so, and <nakleh>, as long as: placed after a noun or a clause, whenever it is that, provided that it is so) (r:zd:22059/zd:10893) (q:draft)
ahihang = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (j:ahih hangin) (r:zd:22658/zd:23212) (q:draft)
ahihangin = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (j:ahih hangin) (r:zd:12038/zd:22784/zd:25227) (q:draft)
ahihciang = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:since/as/because) (d:<ahih> and <ciang> written as one word, a short form of <ahihciangin>: placed at the end of a clause, since that is so) (j:ahih/ciang) (r:zd:16442/zd:12093) (q:draft)
ahihcianga = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:because/since/so) (d:<ahih> and <cianga> written as one word after a clause: that being so, because of that) (s:ahihciangin) (j:ahih/cianga) (r:zd:19357/zd:23112) (q:draft)
ahihding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:will be/would be/to be) (d:<ahih>, being so, and <ding>, will, written as one word: that it will be, that it should be, or that it may be; with <kisam> it is required to be, and with <patau> or <lamen> feared or hoped to be) (j:ahih/ding) (r:zd:11253/zd:13011/zd:12955) (q:draft)
ahihhang = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (j:ahih hangin) (r:zd:24595/zd:21040) (q:draft)
ahihhangin = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (j:ahih hangin) (r:zd:21989/zd:21369) (q:draft)
ahihi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:is/it is) (d:<ahi>, it is, and the sentence-final <hi> written as one word: closes a statement that says what something is) (j:ahi/hi) (r:ts:261/zd:25919/zd:25928) (q:draft)
ahihiam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:is it/what is) (d:<ahi> and <hiam> written as one word at the end of a question: is it so, and after <bang> what is it) (j:ahi/hiam) (r:zd:11020/zd:23901) (q:draft)
ahihkeh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:or/or else) (d:short form of {ahih kei leh}, if it is not so: or, joining two words or clauses as alternatives) (r:zd:20172/zd:17613/zd:23860) (q:draft)
ahihkei = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:or/otherwise/if not) (d:<ahih> and <kei>, not, written as one word, nearly always followed by <leh>: if it is not so, or else, or) (j:ahih/kei) (r:zd:12119/zd:25275) (q:draft)
ahihkeileh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:or/otherwise/if not) (d:<ahih>, <kei> and <leh> written as one word, if it is not so: between two words it means or, and at the start of a clause otherwise) (j:ahih/kei/leh) (r:zd:20924/zd:23863/zd:23797) (q:draft)
ahihleh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:if) (d:<ahih>, being so, with <leh>, if: if it is, if he is, after a noun or a clause) (s:hileh)
ahihmah = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:since it is/as it really is) (d:<ahih> and <mah> written as one word, followed by <bangin>: just as it is, since it really is so) (j:ahih/mah) (r:zd:16924/zd:21703/zd:17271) (q:draft)
ahihman = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:because/since) (d:<ahih>, being so, and the first part of <manin> written as one word, with <in> written apart: because it is so; {tua ahihman in} is therefore) (j:ahih/man) (r:zd:23943/zd:20179/zd:17120) (q:draft)
ahihmanin = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:because/since/therefore) (d:<ahih> and <manin> written as one word: because it is so; <tua ahihmanin> is therefore) (j:ahih/manin) (r:zd:21085/zd:21063) (q:draft)
ahihna kimu = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:it is seen that/it is evident that) (d:<ahihna>, the fact that it is so, and <kimu>, here be seen and not meet: placed after a clause, it is seen that this is so; mostly {ahihna kimu thei hi}, it can be seen that, closing a conclusion drawn from what was said) (r:zd:24064/zd:23492/zd:26026) (q:draft)
ahihna thu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/media) (w:the fact that/that it is so) (d:<ahihna>, its being so, and <thu>, matter: placed after a clause and before a verb of saying or announcing such as <gen> or <pulak>, it turns the clause into what is said, where English says that) (r:ts:3271/ts:12347) (q:draft)
ahihnak = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:if it is/as for/when it comes to) (d:<ahih>, being so, written together with the first part of <nakleh>, if: {ahihnak leh} is if it is, as long as it is, and after a noun as for, when it comes to) (b:ahih) (r:zd:15384/zd:15396/zd:11506) (q:draft)
ahihtawh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:since/as/because) (d:<ahih> it being so and <tawh> with, written as one word after a clause: since it is, with its being so, and for that reason) (j:ahih/tawh) (r:zd:13121/zd:16952/zd:15467) (q:draft)
ahihteh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:since/because/as it is) (d:<ahih>, it being so, and <teh> written as one word at the end of a clause: since that is so, giving the reason for what follows; {tua ahihteh} is that being so) (j:ahih/teh) (r:zd:16897/zd:16263) (q:draft)
ahihtheih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be possible/can be done) (d:<a> and <hihtheih> written as one word: what can be done; {ahihtheih leh} is if possible, and {ahihtheih bangin} or {ahihtheih zahin} is as far as possible) (j:a/hihtheih) (r:zd:11702/zd:13341/zd:19733) (q:draft)
ahikeh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:or/or else/otherwise) (d:short spoken form of {ahih kei leh}, if it is not so: joins two alternatives, or opens a sentence with otherwise) (r:zd:19139/zd:20117/zd:19065) (q:draft)
ahileh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (j:ahihleh) (r:zd:16820/zd:21027) (q:draft)
ahilo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:is not/not being) (d:<a> and <hilo>, is not, written as one word: that is not, what is not; {ahi le ahilo} is whether it is so or not) (j:a/hilo) (r:zd:22683/zd:15192) (q:draft)
ahimanin = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:because/since/therefore) (d:<ahih> and <manin> written as one word and without the h: because it is so; {tua ahimanin} is therefore) (j:ahih/manin) (r:zd:8422/zd:21551) (q:draft)
ahingin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:alive) (d:<a> and <hingin> written as one word: alive, while still living, said of a person or animal that is caught, found or rescued) (j:a/hingin) (r:zd:11099/zd:18154/zd:19860) (q:draft)
ahinglai = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/health) (w:still alive/alive) (d:<a> and <hinglai> written as one word: one that is still alive, while still alive) (j:a/hinglai) (r:zd:11927/zd:12277) (q:draft)
ahingtang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:alive/while still alive) (d:<ahing>, alive, with an ending that tells the state someone is in; with <in>, {ahingtang in} tells that something is done to a person or animal that is still alive, as buried alive or burnt alive) (b:ahing) (r:zd:12869/zd:12450) (q:draft)
ahingtangpi = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:alive/while still alive) (d:<ahing>, alive, with <tangpi> written as one word: while still living, said of one who is buried, burned or thrown to animals alive) (j:ahing/tangpi) (r:zd:11980/zd:12869) (q:draft)
ahiphial = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:even if/even though) (d:<ahi>, be, with <phial>, even if, written as one word and followed by <zongin> or {zong in}: even if it is, even if it were) (j:ahi/phial) (r:zd:14709/zd:14565/zd:25589) (q:draft)
ahitam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:is it I wonder) (d:<ahi>, it is, with the question ending {-tam} at the end of a question: is it, could it be; it gives the question a tone of wondering and is often followed by <maw>; compare <aitam>) (r:zd:20565/zd:21723/zd:22586) (q:draft)
ahithei = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:as far as possible/possible) (d:<a> and <hithei>, can be, written as one word: what is possible; {ahithei zahin} and {ahithei bangin} are as much as possible, as far as one can) (j:a/hithei) (r:zd:22282/zd:23935/zd:10742) (q:draft)
ahizong = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:but/however/nevertheless) (d:<ahi> and <zong> written as one word, mostly followed by <in>: even so, however; begins a sentence that goes against what was just said) (j:ahi/zong) (r:zd:22658/zd:25203/zd:15644) (q:draft)
ahizongin = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:but/however/even so) (d:<ahi> and <zongin> written as one word, mostly at the start of a sentence: although that is so, but) (j:ahi/zongin) (r:zd:21110/zd:20145/zd:13340) (q:draft)
ahkl = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday/media) (w:or/otherwise) (d:written abbreviation of {ahih kei leh}, if it is not so: or, or else) (j:ahih/kei/leh) (r:zd:24814/zd:24480) (q:draft)
ahoihlam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:good side/good direction) (d:<a> and <hoihlam> written as one word: the good side of a matter; {ahoihlam in} is in a good way, for good, and {ahoihlam ah} is toward the better) (j:a/hoihlam) (r:zd:20319/zd:23697/zd:24750) (q:draft)
ahoihlo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:bad/not good) (d:<a> and <hoihlo> written as one word: what is not good, the bad one; {ahoihlo in} is badly) (j:a/hoihlo) (r:zd:17295/zd:19603/zd:12727) (q:draft)
ahoihna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:advantage/good point/benefit/goodness) (d:<a> with <hoihna>, goodness, written as one word: the good in something, its advantage, set against {ahoihlohna} or {a siatna}, its harm) (j:a/hoihna) (r:zd:24157/zd:22650/zd:24068) (q:draft)
ahoihpen = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:the best/best) (d:<a> and <hoihpen>, best, written as one word: the best one, or best after a noun) (j:a/hoihpen) (r:zd:13179/zd:24317/zd:11734) (q:draft)
ahon = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:open) (d:<a> and <hon>, open, written as one word: he opens, the opening of) (j:a/hon) (r:zd:25115/zd:19679) (q:draft)
ahon = (i:2) (t:n) (f:social) (w:group/flock) (d:<a> with <hon>, group, written as one word; {ahon in} is as a group, together) (j:a/hon) (r:zd:11342/ts:9856) (q:draft)
ahong = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:<a> and <hong> written as one word before a verb: he, she, it or they, with the particle that turns the action toward the speaker, as in {ahong gen hi}, he told us) (j:a/hong) (r:zd:21626/zd:17444/zd:20627) (q:draft)
ahonkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:rescue/save) (d:<a> and <honkhia> written as one word: he rescues, the one who rescued; {nuntakna ahonkhia} is saved the life of) (j:a/honkhia) (r:zd:15562/zd:11126) (q:draft)
ahonkhiading = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/everyday) (w:to rescue/in order to save) (d:<a>, <honkhia>, rescue, and <ding>, will, written as one word; {ahonkhiading in} is in order to rescue them) (j:a/honkhia/ding) (r:zd:10968/zd:16595/zd:13022) (q:draft)
ahopih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:speak to/talk with) (d:<a> and <hopih> written as one word: he speaks to, the one he talks with) (j:a/hopih) (r:zd:12507/zd:24139/zd:21463) (q:draft)
ahotkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:rescue/save) (d:<a>, he or they, and <hotkhiat>, written as one word: he or they rescue someone, used before words such as <ciangin>, <sawm> and <nop>) (j:a/hotkhiat) (r:zd:20535/zd:11461) (q:draft)
ahu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body/nature) (w:his breath/its breath/vapour) (d:<a> and <hu>, breath, written as one word: his or her breath, breathing; of a thing its vapour, gas or blast) (j:a/hu) (r:zd:18046/zd:25433/zd:11860) (q:draft)
ahu = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:guard/protect/shield) (d:<a> written as one word with a verb meaning shield or protect, a different word from <hu> breath: the one who guards; {a nuntakna ahu ding galkap} is the soldiers who are to guard his life) (r:zd:21706/zd:25339) (q:draft, low confidence)
ahuaisia = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/media) (w:severe/terrible/serious) (d:<a> with <huaisia>, dreadful, written as one word: severe, the worst, said of fires, accidents and disasters) (s:lauhuai) (r:zd:18166/zd:17622/zd:15679) (q:draft)
ahuaisialua = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:health) (w:very serious/severe/critical) (d:<a>, <huaisia>, dreadful or serious, and <lua>, too much, written as one word; said of injuries, mostly in {ahuaisialua omlo}, there is none that is serious) (r:zd:12569/zd:12490/zd:17252) (q:draft)
ahuaisiapen = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:media/everyday) (w:worst/most terrible/deadliest) (d:<a>, <huaisia>, severe, and <pen>, here the mark of the highest degree, written as one word: the most terrible of its kind, said of accidents, fires, storms and attacks) (j:a/huaisia/pen) (r:zd:11856/zd:15368/zd:11956) (q:draft)
ahuam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:cover/include/take in) (d:<a> and <huam> written as one word: it covers or includes, or that which takes in the whole of something) (j:a/huam) (r:zd:26658/zd:24157) (q:draft)
ahuampi = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/education) (w:in general/overall/as a whole) (d:taking everything together, from <huam>, include; mostly as {ahuampi in}, in general, broadly) (r:zd:10729/zd:25132) (q:draft)
ahuh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:help) (d:<a> and <huh>, help, written as one word: he helps, the one who helps; {ahuh mi} is a helper) (j:a/huh) (r:zd:25601/zd:11400) (q:draft)
ahuhding = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/social) (w:to help/in order to help) (d:<a>, <huh>, help, and <ding> written as one word: to help him or them, usually followed by <in>; also the one who will help) (j:a/huh/ding) (r:zd:21563/zd:15657/zd:15435) (q:draft)
ahunhun = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:from time to time/periodically/now and then) (d:<a> and <hunhun> written as one word, usually followed by <in>: from time to time, each time as it comes) (j:a/hunhun) (r:zd:21563/zd:20667/zd:22981) (q:draft)
ahunlap = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time/everyday) (w:in time/timely) (d:<ahun> and <lap> written as one word, followed by <in>: catching the time, in time, before it is too late) (j:ahun/lap) (r:zd:16259/zd:16511) (q:draft)
ahunzui = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time/everyday) (w:as the time requires/from time to time/in due course) (d:<ahun>, the time, with <zui>, follow: according to the time or occasion, mostly as {ahunzui in}) (j:ahun/zui) (r:zd:13020/zd:22081/zd:23240) (q:draft)
ahzong = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:also in/also at/in as well) (d:<ah>, the marker of place, and <zong>, also, written as one word after a noun: in or at that place too) (j:ah/zong) (r:zd:11844/zd:19962/zd:17143) (q:draft)
AIDS = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health) (w:AIDS) (d:the disease AIDS, caused by the virus HIV; also said {AIDS natna}) (o:English) (r:zd:23697/zd:23512) (q:draft)
aih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (j:ahih) (r:zd:22981/zd:23081/zd:14730) (q:draft)
aih ciang = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:because/since/so) (d:<aih>, the spoken short form of <ahih>, being, with <ciang>: because it is so; placed at the end of a clause that gives the reason for what follows, in speech and in told stories; the full form is <ahihciangin>) (s:ahihciangin) (r:zd:22683/zd:24370/zd:15122) (q:draft)
aihteh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:since/seeing that/because) (d:placed after a clause to give it as the reason, often one that the speaker supposes or takes for granted, for what follows) (r:zd:22595/zd:15571) (q:draft, low confidence)
aikeh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:or/or else) (d:short written form of the spoken {ahih kei leh}, if it is not so: joins two alternatives) (r:zd:21033/zd:20584) (q:draft)
AirAsia = (i:1) (t:name) (f:travel) (w:AirAsia) (d:a low-cost airline of Malaysia) (r:zd:12785/zd:17301) (q:draft)
aircon = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/travel) (w:air conditioner/air conditioning) (d:machine that cools the air of a room or vehicle; {aircon bus} is an air-conditioned bus) (o:English) (r:zd:10935/zd:11759/zd:17299) (q:draft)
aircraft = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:aircraft/aeroplane) (d:an aeroplane, mostly in English phrases and beside the Zolai word <vanleng>) (s:vanleng) (o:English) (r:zd:12000/zd:14787) (q:draft, low confidence)
