apuam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/media) (w:identity/particulars) (d:found only in the pair <amin apuam>, his name and particulars: the full identity of a person, as in news reports where it has not been made known) (r:zd:11635/zd:15531/zd:23639) (q:draft)
apuan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:clothes/clothing) (d:<a> and <puan> written as one word: his, her or their clothes) (j:a/puan) (r:zd:26097/zd:22658/zd:12477) (q:draft)
apuansilh = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/body) (w:his clothes/her clothes/their clothes) (d:<a>, his, her or their, and <puansilh>, clothing, written as one word: the clothes that the person spoken of is wearing or owns) (j:a/puansilh) (r:zd:11938/zd:19902/zd:15443) (q:draft)
apuanteng = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:all his clothes/all her clothes) (d:<a> and <puanteng> written as one word: all the clothes a person has on; {apuanteng suahkhia} is take off all his clothes) (j:a/puanteng) (r:zd:16122/zd:11217) (q:draft)
apuk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/nature) (w:fell/fall down) (d:<a> and <puk>, fall, written as one word: it fell, or the one that fell; said here mostly of a tree falling over) (j:a/puk) (r:zd:18003/zd:18028/zd:19925) (q:draft)
apulak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media) (w:announce/report/make known) (d:<a> and <pulak>, make known, written as one word: he or they announced or reported, or the thing announced; often followed by <khia> or <khiatna>) (j:a/pulak) (r:zd:20764/zd:13059) (q:draft)
apulakkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/politics) (w:announce/declare/make public) (d:<a>, <pulak> and <khiat> written as one word: he or they announced or made known publicly) (j:a/pulak/khiat) (r:zd:22728/zd:16823) (q:draft)
apulakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/politics) (w:announcement/statement) (d:<a> and <pulakna> written as one word: his, her or their announcement; {apulakna ah} is in the statement they made, according to what they announced) (j:a/pulakna) (r:zd:11588/zd:21981) (q:draft)
apumpi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (w:body/whole body) (d:<a> and <pumpi> written as one word: his or her body, the whole body) (j:a/pumpi) (r:zd:12338/zd:14852) (q:draft)
apusuah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:come out/go out) (d:<a>, he or she, and <pusuah>, written as one word: he or she comes out of a place, used before <ciangin>, {khit teh} and similar words) (j:a/pusuah) (r:zd:17313/zd:14718) (q:draft)
apusuahkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:come out/go out) (d:<a>, <pusuah> and <khiat> written as one word: he, she or it comes out, mostly before <ciangin>, when, or <nadingin>, so that) (j:a/pusuah/khiat) (r:zd:17301/zd:15848/zd:21030) (q:draft)
apusuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:going out/coming out) (d:<a> and <pusuak> written as one word: that goes out or comes out, the one who went out) (j:a/pusuak) (r:zd:11786/zd:20663) (q:draft)
Arabic = (i:1) (t:name) (f:education/social) (w:Arabic) (d:the Arabic language and its writing, as in {Arabic kam} and {Arabic lai}; also said of an Arab person) (o:English) (r:zd:25947/zd:15071) (q:draft)
Arakan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:politics/travel) (w:Arakan/Rakhine) (d:the older name of Rakhine, the coastal state in the west of Myanmar, and of its people; {Arakan Army} is the armed group of that people) (r:ts:12002/zd:25094/ts:9781) (q:draft)
Area = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/politics) (w:area/district) (d:an area: a part of a town or country, mostly after its name or in an English compound, as in Washington D.C Area) (o:English) (r:zd:24041/zd:20655) (q:draft, low confidence)
