asiapa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:his teacher/their teacher/coach) (d:<a>, his, her or their, and <siapa>, male teacher, written as one word: the teacher, instructor or coach of the person spoken of) (j:a/siapa) (r:zd:20289/zd:20387) (q:draft)
asiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be ruined/break down/go bad) (d:<a> and <siat> written as one word: its being ruined, spoiled or out of order; {asiat leh} is if it is ruined and {asiat ma-in} before it goes bad) (j:a/siat) (r:zd:12357/zd:12121/zd:22658) (q:draft)
asiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:damage/breakdown/fault/bad side) (d:<a> and <siatna> written as one word: its being broken or out of order, the damage or fault of a thing; paired with <ahoihna>, the bad side of something) (j:a/siatna) (r:zd:11922/zd:25275/zd:15031) (q:draft)
asiding = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/health) (w:about to die/going to die) (d:<a>, <si>, die, and <ding>, will, written as one word: the one who is going to die; {asiding in} is expecting him to die, or so that he will die) (j:a/si/ding) (r:zd:18110/zd:22087/zd:25616) (q:draft)
asih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:die) (d:<a> and <sih> written as one word: he or she died, his or her death, the one who died; {asih ciangin} is when he died and {asih khit ciang} is after his death) (j:a/sih) (r:zd:11283/zd:15943/zd:23639) (q:draft)
asihkhit = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/family) (w:have died/after the death of) (d:<a> and <sihkhit> written as one word; {asihkhit ciangin} is after he or she died) (j:a/sihkhit) (r:zd:13024/zd:19191) (q:draft)
asihlawh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/health) (w:die as a result/lose one's life) (d:<a> and <sihlawh>, die because of something, written as one word: he, she or they died as a result, or the one who died as a result) (j:a/sihlawh) (r:zd:13236/zd:19127) (q:draft)
asihloh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:not die/survive) (d:<a>, <sih> and <loh> written as one word: his or her not dying; {asihloh hangin} is although he or she did not die) (j:a/sih/loh) (r:zd:17952/zd:14699/zd:18005) (q:draft)
asihma = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time/everyday) (w:before dying/before death) (d:<a>, <sih> and <ma> written as one word, mostly with <in>: before he or she died) (j:a/sih/ma) (r:zd:16867/zd:17083) (q:draft)
asihna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/media) (w:death/his death/her death) (d:<a> and <sihna>, death, written as one word: the death of the person spoken of; {asihna ahang} is the cause of death) (j:a/sihna) (r:zd:21332/zd:23404) (q:draft)
asihzawh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:after his death/since he died) (d:<a> and <sihzawh> written as one word: after he or she died; followed by a length of time, that long since the death) (j:a/sihzawh) (r:zd:11736/zd:11700) (q:draft)
asik = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:step on/tread/press with the foot) (d:<a> and <sik>, step on, written as one word: he steps on something; of a brake, press it, and of a bicycle, pedal it) (j:a/sik) (r:zd:17200/ts:3369) (q:draft)
asikhin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health/media) (w:already dead/have died) (d:<a> and <sikhin> written as one word: he has already died, or the one who is already dead) (j:a/sikhin) (r:zd:18046/zd:16849) (q:draft)
asilh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:home/everyday) (w:wear/wearing/what one wears) (d:<a> and <silh> written as one word: he or she wears, the one wearing, or the clothes one has on; {asilh leh ateen} is one's clothing) (j:a/silh) (r:zd:15537/zd:25926) (q:draft)
asilo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:survive/not die) (d:<a>, <si> and <lo> written as one word: who did not die, the survivor of an accident or attack) (j:a/si/lo) (r:zd:17472/zd:14528) (q:draft)
asim = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education/everyday) (w:read/who reads) (d:<a> and <sim>, read, written as one word: he or she reads, or before a noun the one who reads; {asim mi te} are those who read) (j:a/sim) (r:zd:22557/zd:21130/zd:11571) (q:draft)
asin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education) (w:learn/study) (d:<a> and <sin.1> written as one word: he or she learns, the one who learns, what is learned; {asin ding} is what there is to learn) (j:a/sin) (r:zd:16313/zd:19174/zd:24381) (q:draft)
asinu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/media) (w:the dead woman/the deceased) (d:<a> with <si>, die, and <nu>, woman, written as one word: the woman who died, said in reports of a death) (j:a/si/nu) (r:zd:18122/zd:11825) (q:draft)
asipa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/media) (w:the deceased/dead man) (d:<a> and <sipa> written as one word: the man who died, in news reports the man killed) (s:misipa) (j:a/sipa) (r:zd:11574/zd:12007/zd:19906) (q:draft)
asipen = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/everyday) (w:the dead/the one who died) (d:<a>, <si>, die, and the topic marker <pen> written as one word: as for the one or the ones who died) (j:a/si/pen) (r:zd:20562/zd:12811/zd:21563) (q:draft)
asisa = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/health) (w:dead/the dead one) (d:<a> and <sisa> written as one word: the one that has died; {asisa in} is dead, as in found dead or born dead) (j:a/sisa) (r:zd:16490/zd:15286/zd:11887) (q:draft)
asit = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:work/everyday) (w:genuine/real/original) (d:the real thing and not a copy or imitation, said of goods, documents and medicines; often {asit taktak}) (o:Burmese) (r:zd:12908/zd:12564/zd:11833) (q:draft)
asit = (i:2) (t:v) (f:work/politics) (w:examine/inspect/test) (d:<a> and <sit>, examine, written as one word: he or they examine, inspect or test, and those who were examined) (j:a/sit) (r:zd:12534/zd:11825/zd:24411) (q:draft)
asitcian = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/work) (w:inspect/examine carefully/investigate) (d:<a>, <sit>, examine, and <cian>, carefully, written as one word: he or they examine something closely, check it thoroughly) (j:a/sit/cian) (r:zd:14509/zd:15103) (q:draft)
asite = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/media) (w:the dead/those who died/the deceased) (d:<a> and <site> written as one word: the ones who died, in news the people killed in an accident or attack) (j:a/site) (r:zd:11752/zd:20703/zd:10842) (q:draft)
Assam = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:travel) (w:Assam) (d:a state in the north-east of India) (r:zd:24227/zd:20186) (q:draft)
assessment = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/education) (w:assessment/evaluation) (d:English word for a formal examination or evaluation of a person or thing, used with <kibawl>, be carried out; the Zolai word is <etcianna>) (o:English) (r:zd:15275) (q:draft, low confidence)
Assyria = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:religion) (j:Assiria) (r:zd:25099/zd:22159) (q:draft)
Astro = (i:1) (t:name) (f:media) (w:Astro) (d:a Malaysian satellite television company; {Astro Awani} is its news channel) (r:zd:19602) (q:draft, low confidence)
asuah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:family/everyday) (w:be born) (d:<a> and <suah> written as one word: he or she is born, before endings such as <ciangin> and <manin>) (j:a/suah) (r:zd:12567/zd:21848/zd:22923) (q:draft)
asuah = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:become) (d:<a> and <suah> written as one word: he becomes, it turns into, before endings such as {khit ciangin}) (j:a/suah) (r:zd:14728) (q:draft, low confidence)
asuahcil = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:family/health) (w:at birth/when newly born) (d:<a> <suah> <cil> written as one word: when he or she was just born; {asuahcil akipan} is from birth) (j:a/suah/cil) (r:zd:18248/zd:13117/zd:15435) (q:draft)
asuahkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:family/everyday) (w:be born/come out) (d:<a> and <suahkhiat> written as one word, before <laitak>, <khitciangin> and similar words: when or after it is born or comes out) (j:a/suahkhiat) (r:zd:13179/zd:14959) (q:draft)
asuahkhit = (i:1) (t:v) (f:family/health) (w:after being born/after giving birth) (d:<a> and <suahkhit> written as one word: once he or she has been born, or once she has given birth; mostly before <ciangin>) (j:a/suahkhit) (r:zd:16093/zd:12942/zd:17899) (q:draft)
asuahtak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:be released/get free/escape) (d:<a> and <suahtak> written as one word: his or her getting free; {asuahtak ciangin} is when he was released) (j:a/suahtak) (r:zd:10722/zd:21929) (q:draft)
asuahtaktheih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be able to escape/be able to go free) (d:<a>, <suahtak>, escape, and <theih>, be able, written as one word; mostly in {asuahtaktheih nadingin}, so that he or they could escape or be set free) (j:a/suahtak/theih) (r:zd:15851/zd:20625) (q:draft)
asuahzawh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time/family) (w:after birth/since being born) (d:<a> and <suahzawh> written as one word, with <suah> in the sense of be born: after he, she or it was born; a length of time follows, as {asuahzawh ni 6}, six days after birth) (j:a/suahzawh) (r:zd:12996/zd:14642/zd:16976) (q:draft)
asuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:become/be born) (d:<a> and <suak> written as one word: he becomes or the one who has become something; of birth, he was born or the one born in a place) (j:a/suak) (r:zd:21690/zd:23554/zd:17672) (q:draft)
asuakcil = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:family) (w:newborn/just born) (d:<a>, <suak>, be born, and <cil>, at first, written as one word, placed after the noun: {naungek asuakcil} is a newborn baby) (j:a/suak/cil) (r:zd:12014/zd:16767) (q:draft)
asuakkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:family/health) (w:be born/come out) (d:<a> and <suakkhia> written as one word: he or she is born; before a noun, the one that was born, as in {asuakkhia naungek}, the newborn baby) (j:a/suakkhia) (r:zd:15286/zd:13228) (q:draft)
asuakta = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:survive/escape/be free) (d:<a> and <suakta> written as one word: the one who survived or got away; before a noun, free) (j:a/suakta) (r:zd:18911/zd:12166) (q:draft)
asuamlum = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:murder/assassinate/kill) (d:<a> and <suamlum> written as one word: he or they attack and kill, the one who killed) (j:a/suamlum) (r:zd:11366/zd:16786) (q:draft)
asuan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:nature/work) (w:plant) (d:<a> and <suan>, plant, written as one word: he planted, the one who plants) (j:a/suan) (r:zd:11885/zd:16797) (q:draft)
asuan = (i:2) (t:n) (f:family) (w:his descendants/their descendants) (d:<a>, his or their, and <suan>, descendant, written as one word; mostly in the pair {asuan leh khak}, their descendants) (j:a/suan) (r:zd:25273) (q:draft)
asuang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/travel) (w:inside/in it) (d:<a> with <suang>, inside, written as one word; {asuang ah} is inside it, said of people in a vehicle) (j:a/suang) (r:zd:11646) (q:draft, low confidence)
asuhsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:snatch/rob of/take by force) (d:<a> with <suh>, take by force, and <sak>, written as one word: take a thing from a person by force, said of a purse, a phone or a car; also the one who does so) (j:a/suh/sak) (r:zd:14731/zd:14997) (q:draft)
asukham = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/everyday) (w:blow up/set off/smash) (d:<a> and <sukham>, break to pieces, written as one word; in the articles mostly of a bomb, {Bomb asukham}, the one who set off the bomb or the bombing itself, also of breaking up a group) (j:a/sukham) (r:zd:13089/zd:24731) (q:draft)
asukkhapsawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:plan to blow up/attempt to destroy) (d:<a>, <sukkhap>, smash, and <sawm>, intend, written as one word: who planned or tried to blow up or destroy something) (j:a/sukkhap/sawm) (r:zd:14711/zd:16932) (q:draft)
asum = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/everyday) (w:the money/his money) (d:<a> and <sum> written as one word: the money, his, her or their money; {asum in akituat ciangin} is when it is reckoned in money) (j:a/sum) (r:zd:25919/zd:15443/zd:19863) (q:draft)
asumbawm = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/work) (w:his purse/her purse/handbag) (d:<a> and <sumbawm> written as one word: his or her purse, wallet or handbag) (j:a/sumbawm) (r:zd:17741/zd:12261) (q:draft)
asun = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:by day/daytime) (d:<a> and <sun>, day, written as one word; {asun azan} is day and night, all the time) (j:a/sun) (r:zd:25148/zd:24948/zd:21843) (q:draft)
asun = (i:2) (t:v) (f:health) (w:be injected/be vaccinated) (d:<a> written together with <sun>, pierce or inject: one who has had an injection; {vaccine asun nai lo} is one who is not yet vaccinated) (j:a/sun) (r:zd:25042) (q:draft)
asung = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:its inside/inside it/the inside) (d:<a> and <sung> written as one word: the inside of the thing spoken of; {asung ah} is inside it) (j:a/sung) (r:zd:22658/zd:12337/zd:11409) (q:draft)
asungah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:inside it/in it) (d:<a>, its, and <sungah>, inside, written as one word: inside it, in the thing or place just named) (j:a/sungah) (r:zd:12733/zd:15274/zd:15602) (q:draft)
asunglam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/body) (w:inside/inner part/interior) (d:<a> and <sunglam> written as one word: its inside, the inner side or inner part of something) (j:a/sunglam) (r:zd:15059/zd:15255/zd:23016) (q:draft)
asungpan = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:from inside it/out of it) (d:<a>, its, with <sungpan>, from within, written as one word: from the inside of the thing named; {amau ii asungpan apiang} is born of themselves, their own child) (j:a/sungpan) (r:zd:12901/zd:14523) (q:draft)
Asylum = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:asylum) (d:protection that a country gives to a person who has fled another country; {Asylum ngen} is ask for asylum) (o:English) (r:zd:24029/zd:15080) (q:draft)
at = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:cut) (d:cut with a blade. {At khia} is cut off) (q:draft)
at = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work) (w:reap/harvest) (d:cut grain at harvest; {buh at} is to reap the grain, and {at} is set against <vawh>, sow) (s:anla) (a:vawh/tuh) (q:draft)
ata = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:his child/her child/their child) (d:<a>, his, her or their, and <ta>, child, written as one word) (j:a/ta) (r:zd:17945/zd:20244/zd:12402) (q:draft)
ataangpi = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:social/everyday) (w:general/common/overall) (d:of the whole or of most of a group, not of one part; {ataangpi-in} after a noun is in general, as a whole, for the most part) (r:zd:21079/zd:17860/zd:17901) (q:draft)
atai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:run/flee) (d:<a> and <tai>, run, written as one word: he runs or flees, the one who flees; of a bus, train or lorry, that runs in a place) (j:a/tai) (r:zd:16323/zd:25203) (q:draft)
ataiding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:will run/will operate) (d:<a>, <tai>, run, and <ding>, will, written as one word: that is to run, said of a boat, bus or train on its route) (j:a/tai/ding) (r:zd:17822/zd:12420) (q:draft)
ataih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:hit/strike/attack) (d:<a> with <taih>, strike against or attack: that hits, the one that hit; <damiah ataih> is one who commits a robbery, or a robbery was committed) (j:a/taih) (r:zd:12113/zd:14917) (q:draft, low confidence)
ataihkha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:hit/crash into/collide with) (d:<a> and <taihkha> written as one word: said of a vehicle that runs into a person, a tree or another vehicle; before a noun, the one that hit) (j:a/taihkha) (r:zd:17299/zd:17104/zd:15836) (q:draft)
ataihkhak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:hit/run into/knock down) (d:the prefix <a> with {taihkhak}, the form of <taihkha> used before a noun, <laitak> or <ciangin>: the one that a vehicle hit, or when it hit; said of a car, bus or ship running into a person or thing) (r:zd:17104/zd:11710/zd:19063) (q:draft)
ataikhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:flee/run away/escape) (d:<a> and <taikhia> written as one word: he or they fled, or the ones who fled) (j:a/taikhia) (r:zd:15043/zd:15214/zd:15795) (q:draft)
ataikhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:run away/flee/escape) (d:<a> and <taikhiat> written as one word: his or their running away, used before words such as <ciangin> and <khitciangin>) (j:a/taikhiat) (r:zd:16389/zd:11978) (q:draft)
atailaitak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:while running/while travelling) (d:<a>, <tai> and <laitak> written as one word: at the very time it was running, said mostly of a vehicle on its way) (j:a/tai/laitak) (r:zd:16346/zd:17239) (q:draft)
ataimang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:flee/run away/escape) (d:<a> and <taimang> written as one word: he fled, or the one who fled) (j:a/taimang) (r:zd:24297/zd:15641) (q:draft)
ataina = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:course/track/route) (d:<a> and <taina> written as one word: where it runs, as {ataina lampi}, the road it runs on, and {ataina Runway}, the runway an aircraft runs along; also a place to flee to) (j:a/taina) (r:zd:16851/zd:19807/zd:21509) (q:draft)
ataisim = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:run away/flee/escape/desert) (d:<a> and <taisim>, slip away, written as one word: who has run away or is fleeing, as a prisoner, a soldier who deserts or a person who leaves home) (j:a/taisim) (r:zd:14785/zd:16325/zd:22072) (q:draft)
ataklam = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:body) (w:right/right side) (d:<a> and <taklam> written as one word: the right one, his or her right; {akhut ataklam} is his right hand) (j:a/taklam) (r:zd:12490/zd:12623/zd:18063) (q:draft)
atakpi = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/media) (w:true/real/genuine) (d:<a> and <takpi> written as one word: what is true or real, the real thing; {atakpi himawk} is it is indeed true, and {atakpi in} is in reality) (j:a/takpi) (r:zd:16630/zd:14728/zd:12913) (q:draft)
atakpimah = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/media) (w:really true/true indeed/genuine) (d:<a>, <takpi>, truly, and <mah>, written as one word: it is really so; {atakpimah hi} confirms that a report is true) (j:a/takpi/mah) (r:zd:15651/zd:12603/zd:14539) (q:draft)
ataktak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:really/actually/real/in reality) (d:<a> and <taktak> written as one word: the real thing, what is truly so; {ataktak in} is in reality, actually, and {ataktak hilo} is not real, not true) (j:a/taktak) (r:zd:21703/zd:12500/zd:22557) (q:draft)
ataktakin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:in fact/actually/truly) (d:<a> and <taktakin> written as one word: in fact, the truth is, at the opening of a statement) (j:a/taktakin) (r:zd:22802/zd:15274) (q:draft)
atamman = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:work/everyday) (w:expensive/costly/high-priced) (d:<a>, <tam>, much, and <man>, price, written as one word: of high price; {atamman mahmah} is very expensive) (s:manpha) (j:a/tam/man) (r:zd:12132/zd:16408/zd:25919) (q:draft)
atamna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:great number/large amount/abundance) (d:<a> and <tamna> written as one word: the great number or amount of something, how much there is of it, or the place where it is most numerous) (j:a/tamna) (r:zd:24226/zd:17649) (q:draft)
atampen = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:the most/at most/the greatest number) (d:<a> and <tampen> written as one word: the most, the largest in number or amount; before a number, at most) (j:a/tampen) (r:zd:21042/zd:20363/zd:20093) (q:draft)
atampenpen = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:the most/the very most) (d:<a> with <tam>, many, and <penpen> written as one word: the greatest in number of all, the most) (j:a/tam/penpen) (r:zd:13000/zd:14686) (q:draft)
atamzaw = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:most/majority/the greater part) (d:<a> and <tamzaw> written as one word: the greater number, most of them; {atamzaw in} is mostly, for the most part) (j:a/tamzaw) (r:zd:26163/zd:22331/zd:16914) (q:draft)
atamzawte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:most/the majority/most of) (d:<a> and <tamzawte> written as one word, placed after a noun: most of them, the greater number, as in {mi atamzawte}, most people) (j:a/tamzawte) (r:zd:11409/zd:22037) (q:draft)
atamzawtham = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:most/the great majority/far more) (d:<a>, <tamzaw> and <tham> written as one word: by far the greater part, most of them; after <sangin>, far more than) (j:a/tamzaw/tham) (r:zd:12481/zd:15435) (q:draft)
atan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:class/grade/standard) (d:a school class or year: {atan 10} is the tenth standard and {atan kibatpih} is a classmate) (o:Burmese) (r:zd:22470) (q:draft, low confidence)
atan = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (d:<a> and <tan> written as one word, in several meanings of <tan>: abstain from a food; of a lamp or a light, shine; and with <lawh>, lose or miss out on something) (j:a/tan) (r:zd:12541/zd:25171) (q:draft, low confidence)
ataneu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:small child/young child) (d:<a> and <taneu> written as one word: his or her small child) (j:a/taneu) (r:zd:12475/zd:20490) (q:draft)
atang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/food) (w:grain/seed/single piece) (d:<a> and <tang> written as one word: its grain or seed, a single small round piece such as a tablet or a bullet; {a lom atang}, in bundles and in single pieces, is in great quantity) (j:a/tang) (r:ts:3641/zd:21954/zd:25397) (q:draft, low confidence)
atangek = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:her baby/his baby) (d:<a>, his or her, <ta>, child, and <ngek>, tiny, written as one word: his or her baby, an infant child) (j:a/ta/ngek) (r:zd:15485/zd:18128) (q:draft)
atangko = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/politics) (w:announce/proclaim/declare) (d:<a> and <tangko> written as one word: he announces, or what is announced) (j:a/tangko) (r:zd:19577/zd:21723) (q:draft)
atangthu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/education) (w:his story/its history) (d:<a>, his, her or its, and <tangthu>, story, written as one word: the story or history of a person or people) (j:a/tangthu) (r:zd:20125/zd:14795) (q:draft)
atangtun = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:be fulfilled/fulfil/accomplish/carry out) (d:<a> and <tangtun>, fulfil, written as one word: it is fulfilled or carried out, of an aim, a plan, a promise or a word) (j:a/tangtun) (r:zd:22719/zd:22331/zd:23742) (q:draft)
atangtung = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/religion) (w:come true/be fulfilled/succeed) (d:<a> and <tangtung> written as one word: it is fulfilled or carried through, said of a plan, a wish or a promise; with <sak>, bring it about) (j:a/tangtung) (r:zd:11133/zd:17760) (q:draft)
atano = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:his little child/her baby/their little child) (d:<a>, his, her or their, with <ta>, child, and the ending for little or young, written as one word: the small child or baby of the person spoken of) (r:zd:11782/zd:17049/zd:16073) (q:draft)
atansak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:body/everyday) (w:cut off/sever) (d:<a> and <tansak> written as one word: cut off a part of the body; with <ngawng>, neck, behead) (j:a/tansak) (r:zd:14543/zd:11562) (q:draft)
atanu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:his daughter/her daughter/their daughter) (d:<a> and <tanu> written as one word) (j:a/tanu) (r:zd:12585/zd:17709/zd:12196) (q:draft)
atapa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:his son/her son/their son) (d:<a> and <tapa> written as one word: his, her or their son) (j:a/tapa) (r:zd:11373/zd:16073/zd:19063) (q:draft)
atat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education) (w:keep writing/write regularly) (d:<at>, write, doubled and written as one word, mostly with <lai>: write again and again, go on writing) (b:at) (r:zd:21529/zd:16254) (q:draft, low confidence)
atate = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:his children/her children/their children) (d:<a> and <tate> written as one word: the children of the person spoken about) (j:a/tate) (r:zd:17936/zd:14954/zd:19571) (q:draft)
atatsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:smear on/rub on/wipe on) (d:<a> with <tatsak>, here rub or smear a thing on someone, written as one word; in the articles of poison smeared on the face of a person; also the one who smeared it) (j:a/tatsak) (r:zd:11440) (q:draft, low confidence)
ataw = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (w:buttocks/bottom/anus) (d:<a> and <taw> written as one word: the bottom or rear of the body of a person or animal) (j:a/taw) (r:zd:13334/zd:12616) (q:draft)
atawi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:hold/carry) (d:<a> and <tawi> written as one word: he holds or carries in the hand, or the one who holds, as in {laidal atawi}, one who holds a document) (j:a/tawi) (r:zd:12930/zd:17304) (q:draft)
atawl = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:be weary/toil) (d:<a> and <tawl> written as one word: the one who is tired; {agim atawl} is those who toiled and wore themselves out for a task) (j:a/tawl) (r:zd:11375/zd:14579) (q:draft)
atawm = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:few/the few/little) (d:<a> and <tawm>, few, written as one word: few, what is few; {atawm pen} is the least, at least) (j:a/tawm) (r:zd:17488/zd:22704) (q:draft)
atawmman = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:work) (w:cheap/low-priced/inexpensive) (d:<a>, <tawm>, little, and <man>, price, written as one word: of low price, cheap; {atawmman in} is cheaply) (j:a/tawm/man) (r:zd:17551/zd:20014) (q:draft)
atawmpen = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:at least/minimum) (d:<a> and <tawmpen> written as one word: the least, used before an amount for at least) (j:a/tawmpen) (r:zd:12564/zd:17102) (q:draft)
atawmzaw = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:less/fewer/the smaller number/minority) (d:<a> and <tawmzaw> written as one word: the lesser or fewer, what is less; of people, the smaller group or minority; {atawmzaw in} is less, to a smaller degree) (j:a/tawmzaw) (r:zd:20589/zd:15471/zd:17110) (q:draft)
atawng = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/media) (w:detail/small piece) (d:<a> and <tawng>, here a short piece, written as one word; used in {a neng atawng}, the small bits and pieces, that is the details, and {a neng atawng in}, in detail) (r:ts:9489/ts:3817/ts:10764) (q:draft, low confidence)
atawntung = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:forever/always/eternity) (d:<a> and <tawntung> written as one word: for all time, forever; often followed by <in> or <a>) (j:a/tawntung) (r:zd:21251/zd:23171) (q:draft)
atawp = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:end/the last) (d:<a> and <tawp> written as one word: the end of something; {atawp dong} is to the end) (j:a/tawp) (r:zd:19779/zd:14767) (q:draft)
