atawpna ah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:finally/in the end/at last/lastly) (d:<atawpna>, the end, and <ah>, the place marker: at the end; opens a sentence or clause that tells the last event or the last point of a talk or letter) (r:zd:20016/zd:25919) (q:draft)
ateek = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:family/everyday) (w:old/the old/grown old) (d:<a> and <teek> written as one word: the old, one who is old; {ateek dongin} is until he is old, and {ateek akhang} is old and young alike; with <te> after it, a woman's parents-in-law) (j:a/teek) (r:zd:26945/zd:16508) (q:draft)
