ateng = (i:2) (t:det) (f:everyday) (w:all/the whole of) (d:{a teng} written as one word after a noun or phrase: all of it, all of them, as in {anuai ateng}, all of the following) (r:zd:23974/zd:24946) (q:draft, low confidence)
atha = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (w:his strength/her strength/their strength) (d:<a>, his, her or their, and <tha>, strength, written as one word; {atha nem} is weak and {atha hat} is strong) (j:a/tha) (r:zd:19427/zd:22556/zd:15114) (q:draft)
athah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:kill/killing) (d:<a> and <thah> written as one word: his or their killing of someone; {athah laitak} is while killing) (j:a/thah) (r:zd:11038/zd:25584) (q:draft)
