athahlup = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:kill/be killed) (d:<a> and <thahlup> written as one word: he or she killed; before a noun, the one who was killed) (j:a/thahlup) (r:zd:17195/zd:15604) (q:draft)
athakkhat = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:a new/a new one) (d:<athak>, new, and <khat>, one, written as one word and placed after a noun: a new one, as {mawtaw athakkhat}, a new car) (j:athak/khat) (r:zd:14597/zd:14665/zd:16959) (q:draft)
athat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:who killed/killer) (d:<a> and <that> written as one word: the one who killed, placed before the person or the number of persons, as in {athat mi}, the killer) (j:a/that) (r:zd:16666/zd:11389) (q:draft)
athatlum = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:kill/he killed) (d:<a> and <thatlum> written as one word: he killed, the one who killed) (j:a/thatlum) (r:zd:15004/zd:17357) (q:draft)
athawh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:he rises/he gets up) (d:<a> and <thawh> written as one word: he or she gets up, his rising; {athawh ciangin} is when he got up) (j:a/thawh) (r:zd:15756/zd:22683/zd:23943) (q:draft)
athei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:know/the one who knows) (d:<a> and <thei> written as one word: the one who knows, those who know; {athei nailo te} is those who do not yet know) (j:a/thei) (r:zd:19676/zd:20440/zd:21262) (q:draft)
