atheih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:know/come to know) (d:<a> and <theih>, know, written as one word: {atheih ciangin} is when he or she learned of it, and {atheih huai thu} is a thing worth knowing) (j:a/theih) (r:zd:14622/zd:25042) (q:draft)
atheihkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:found out/discovered) (d:<a> and <theihkhiat> written as one word: he, she or they found out, what was found out) (j:a/theihkhiat) (r:zd:14738/zd:12841/zd:16932) (q:draft)
atheihloh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not know/be unaware) (d:<a>, <theih> and <loh> written as one word: that he does not know, what is not known; {atheihloh kaalin} is while one is unaware) (j:a/theih/loh) (r:zd:20193/zd:16803) (q:draft)
atheikha = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:one who knows/witness) (d:<a> and <theikha> written as one word: one who happens to know of it, anyone who knows) (j:a/theikha) (r:zd:12669/zd:18161) (q:draft)
atheilo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not know/be unaware) (d:<a>, <thei>, know, and <lo>, not, written as one word: does not know, or one who does not know) (j:a/thei/lo) (r:zd:20970/zd:11206/zd:11548) (q:draft)
athemneng = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:fragments/debris/wreckage/scraps) (d:<a>, <them> and <neng> written as one word: the small broken pieces of something, as the wreckage of an aeroplane or the splinters of a blast) (j:a/them/neng) (r:zd:12888/zd:11588/zd:17164) (q:draft)
