athuakkha = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/media) (w:victim/the one affected) (d:<a> and <thuakkha> written as one word: the one who has suffered something, a victim; with <te>, the victims) (j:a/thuakkha) (r:zd:11360/zd:15469/zd:11837) (q:draft)
athuaknu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/media) (w:female victim/the woman who suffered it) (d:<a>, <thuak>, suffer, and <nu>, woman, written as one word: the woman to whom the thing named before it was done) (j:a/thuak/nu) (r:zd:12429/zd:11990) (q:draft)
athuakpa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:victim/the one who suffered) (d:<a> and <thuakpa> written as one word, placed after the word for what was done: the man to whom it was done, as in {mat athuakpa}, the man who was arrested) (j:a/thuakpa) (r:zd:21030/zd:19868/zd:20492) (q:draft)
athuakte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/media) (w:victims/those who suffer/sufferers) (d:<a> and <thuakte> written as one word, placed after what was suffered: those who underwent it, as in {kapliam athuakte}, those wounded by shooting, and {hih natna athuakte}, those who have this disease) (j:a/thuakte) (r:zd:24014/zd:15000) (q:draft)
athugen = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/religion) (w:what he says/his speech/his words) (d:<a>, his or her, and <thugen>, written as one word: what a person says or said, a speech or sermon; {athugen ding} is what he is going to speak about) (j:a/thugen) (r:zd:22550/zd:17305) (q:draft)
athuk = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/nature) (w:deep) (d:<a> and <thuk>, deep, written as one word: deep, that is deep; after a measure it says how deep, as {pi 20 athuk}, twenty feet deep) (j:a/thuk) (r:zd:12355/zd:12450/zd:17673) (q:draft)
athuk = (i:2) (t:adj) (f:food) (w:sour) (d:<a> and <thuk>, sour, written as one word: sour, that which is sour) (j:a/thuk) (r:zd:22775) (q:draft, low confidence)
athukim = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:agree/one who agrees) (d:<a> and <thukim> written as one word: he or they agree, or those who agree) (j:a/thukim) (r:zd:21050/zd:23982/zd:17291) (q:draft)
athum = (i:1) (t:num) (f:everyday) (w:the three/all three/third) (d:<a> and <thum>, three, written as one word: {athum un} is all three of them, {athum veina} is the third time) (j:a/thum) (r:zd:12311/zd:25351) (q:draft)
athum = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:beg/plead) (d:<a> and <thum>, plead, written as one word: he begs or pleads) (j:a/thum) (r:zd:22550) (q:draft, low confidence)
athumna = (i:1) (t:num) (f:everyday) (w:third/the third/thirdly) (d:<a> and <thumna> written as one word: the third one, or thirdly in a list of points) (j:a/thumna) (r:zd:25203/zd:21042/zd:14865) (q:draft)
