avaikhak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/food) (w:order/instruct/ask for) (d:<a> and <vaikhak> written as one word: what he or she ordered or instructed; in an eating place, the food ordered) (j:a/vaikhak) (r:zd:12696/zd:12754) (q:draft)
avak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:wander/roam/go about) (d:<a> and <vak>, here walk about, written as one word: who goes about, wandering from place to place) (s:vakthap) (j:a/vak) (r:zd:12874/zd:18292) (q:draft)
avak = (i:2) (t:v) (f:family/food) (w:feed/support/provide for) (d:<a> and <vak>, another spelling of <vaak>, feed, written as one word: he or she feeds and supports someone) (j:a/vak) (r:zd:17372/zd:15199) (q:draft, low confidence)
