avakvak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:wander about/go around/roam) (d:<a> with <vak> said twice, written as one word; <vak> here means walk about: one who keeps going around from place to place, as beggars do) (j:a/vak) (r:zd:18292/zd:12728) (q:draft)
aval = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:exceed/be more than/be over) (d:<a> and <val>, exceed, written as one word: after a number or measure, more than it; {aval in} is to excess) (j:a/val) (r:zd:16686/zd:22658) (q:draft)
avang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:hole/opening/gap) (d:<a> and <vang>, opening, written as one word: a hole or opening in something) (j:a/vang) (r:zd:21025/zd:13262) (q:draft)
avang = (i:2) (t:n) (f:social) (w:power/standing/prestige) (d:<a> and <vang>, power, written as one word: his or their power, influence or standing; {avang liatna} is his great power) (j:a/vang) (r:zd:23843) (q:draft, low confidence)
avanlak = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/everyday) (w:luggage/belongings/baggage) (d:<a>, his or her, <van>, goods, and <lak>, midst, written as one word: among his things, mostly {avanlak ah}, in his luggage, of what is found in the bags of a traveller) (j:a/van/lak) (r:zd:12274/zd:15296) (q:draft)
avansung = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/everyday) (w:inside of the bag/in the luggage) (d:{a van} his or her goods or baggage and <sung> inside, written as one word: the inside of a person's bag or luggage, mostly with <ah>) (r:zd:14613/zd:12138/zd:18286) (q:draft)
avanteng = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/home) (w:all his belongings/luggage) (d:<a>, his or her, <van>, goods, and <teng>, here all, written as one word: all of a person's belongings or luggage) (j:a/van/teng) (r:zd:11407/zd:12761/zd:15560) (q:draft)
avanzat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/work) (w:belongings/tools/equipment) (d:<a>, <van>, things, and <zat>, use, written as one word: the things or tools that someone uses, or the thing he used) (j:a/van/zat) (r:zd:16713/zd:14950) (q:draft)
avei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health) (w:suffer from/be ill with) (d:<a> written together with <vei>, suffer from an illness: one who has the illness named before it) (j:a/vei) (r:zd:25131/zd:21517) (q:draft)
avei = (i:2) (t:v) (f:social/religion) (w:care deeply for/have a burden for) (d:<a> written together with <vei>, feel the weight of: one who cares deeply for a land, a people or a cause) (j:a/vei) (r:zd:16686/zd:22972/zd:24376) (q:draft)
aveilam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body/everyday) (w:left side/the left) (d:<a> and <veilam> written as one word: the left side of a person or thing, his left; after a body part, the left one) (j:a/veilam) (r:zd:15512/zd:19562) (q:draft)
aveina = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/religion) (w:concern/burden/care) (d:<a> with <veina> in the sense of feeling for someone: the deep concern or burden that someone feels for a people, a country or God, often paired with love as {a it aveina}) (j:a/veina) (r:zd:23171/zd:24376/zd:17574) (q:draft)
avek = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:all/altogether/everyone) (d:<a> with <vek>, all, written as one word and followed by <in>, or by <un> for people: all of it, all of them) (j:a/vek) (r:zd:24064/zd:12525/zd:15186) (q:draft)
