Bahmaw = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:politics/travel) (w:Bhamo) (d:town in Kachin State, Myanmar) (r:ts:8689/ts:9743) (q:draft)
Bahrain = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:politics) (w:Bahrain) (d:island country in the Persian Gulf) (r:zd:10924) (q:draft)
Bahru = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel) (w:Johor Bahru) (d:second word of the name Johor Bahru, the city at the southern end of Malaysia opposite Singapore) (r:zd:12950/zd:17832) (q:draft)
baht = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:baht) (d:the money unit of Thailand, written after or before the amount) (o:Thai) (r:zd:17649/zd:13334) (q:draft)
baih = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/time) (w:early/soon/quickly) (d:placed after a verb: early, soon or quickly; {tho baih} is rise early) (s:tungin/pak) (q:draft)
baih = (i:2) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:easy) (d:not hard to do; {baih zaw} means easier) (s:ol) (a:haksa/hak) (q:draft)
Baihlamtak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:easily/with ease) (d:<baihlam>, easy, with <tak>, which makes an adverb of manner: in an easy way; found here in the book title {Baihlamtak a Nalianpi Sepna}, doing great work easily) (s:baihlam-a) (r:zd:21110) (q:draft, low confidence)
baihlo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:not easy/difficult/hard) (d:<baih>, easy, and <lo>, not, written as one word) (j:baih/lo) (r:zd:20572/zd:21848) (q:draft)
baihtak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:easily/readily/without difficulty) (d:<baih> and <tak> written as one word, mostly as {baihtak in}: easily, without trouble or delay) (j:baih/tak) (r:zd:24047/zd:21259/zd:23655) (q:draft)
bail = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:bail) (d:money or a pledge on which an arrested person is set free until the trial; {bail tawh khahkhia} is release on bail) (o:English) (r:zd:15499/zd:13209/zd:12546) (q:draft)
Balai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:police station) (d:Malay word for a hall or station, used by Zomi in Malaysia for a police station, in full {Balai Polis}, usually with the name of the place) (o:Malay) (r:zd:23629) (q:draft, low confidence)
balance = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/politics) (w:balance) (d:a state in which things are of equal weight or in the right proportion; also used as a verb, be or keep in balance) (o:English) (r:zd:23780) (q:draft, low confidence)
Balcony = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:balcony) (d:a platform with a railing on the outside of an upper floor of a building) (o:English) (r:zd:12240/zd:16673) (q:draft)
