haikhat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food) (w:one cup/a cup of/a glass of) (d:<hai>, cup, and <khat>, one, written as one word after the name of a drink or other thing measured: one cup of it) (j:hai/khat) (r:zd:24276/zd:22650/zd:17015) (q:draft)
hakai = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (f:food/nature) (w:yam) (d:a root crop eaten as food, a yam; {sing hakai} is cassava) (r:zd:9133) (q:draft, low confidence)
Hakha = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel/politics) (w:Hakha/Haka) (d:capital town of Chin State in Myanmar, and the Chin people and language of that area) (r:zd:19293/zd:16035/zd:21408) (q:draft)
haksa = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:hard/difficult) (d:Hard to do, to bear or to understand; {nasep haksa} is hard labour, and {thu-haksa} is a riddle or hard saying) (s:hak) (a:baih/ol) (q:draft)
haksa sa = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:find hard/find difficult) (d:<haksa>, difficult, followed by <sa> used as a verb, feel or deem, not the word for hot or meat: feel that something is hard to do; the thing found hard stands before it with <ding>, as {cih ding haksa sa}, find it hard to say) (r:zd:23297/zd:24011/zd:20329) (q:draft)
Hall = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/home) (w:hall) (d:a large room or building for meetings, worship and feasts; mostly after its name, as in ZAM Hall) (o:English) (r:zd:17126/zd:22935/zd:17574) (q:draft)
Halloween = (i:1) (t:name) (f:social) (w:Halloween) (d:festival kept on the evening of 31 October) (r:zd:16012/zd:16232/zd:24691) (q:draft)
halta = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time/everyday) (w:every/at intervals of) (d:placed after a number with a unit of time or count: once in every so many, at intervals of that length; {kha 6 halta} is every six months) (r:zd:21025/zd:18893/ts:301) (q:draft)
