hamsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (j:haksa) (r:ts:6447/zd:12600/zd:14903) (q:draft)
hamsa sa = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:find difficult/find hard) (d:<hamsa>, difficult, and <sa>, here the verb feel or consider, not hot: to find something hard; the thing found hard stands before it, usually a verb with <ding>) (r:zd:22171/zd:15681/zd:22757) (q:draft)
hamsapi = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:very difficult/very hard) (d:<hamsa>, difficult, with the augmentative <pi>: very hard or troublesome; {hamsapi in} is with great difficulty) (b:hamsa) (r:zd:23428/zd:20418) (q:draft)
hamsat = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:hard/difficult/hardship) (d:form of <hamsa>, hard or in difficulty, used before a noun and in dependent clauses; also as a noun, hardship) (s:haksat) (r:zd:25253/zd:21130/zd:16254) (q:draft)
hamsatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:hardship/difficulty/trouble) (d:<hamsat>, a form of <hamsa>, hard, with the noun ending <na>: what is hard to bear or to do) (s:haksatna) (b:hamsa) (r:ts:3125/zd:23067/zd:14942) (q:draft)
hamtangding = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/social) (w:must without fail/be sure to) (d:<hamtang>, without fail, and the particle <ding> written as one word after a verb: it must be done without fail, said of a rule or firm advice) (j:hamtang/ding) (r:zd:11759/zd:11590/zd:20343) (q:draft)
hamtangh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:without fail/surely/necessarily) (d:another spelling of <hamtang>; placed after a verb in present-day writing it says that the thing surely happens or must be done without fail) (j:hamtang) (r:zd:19166/zd:22412) (q:draft)
hamtangin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:without fail/be sure to) (d:<hamtang>, without fail, with the <in> that ends a command, written as one word at the end of an instruction: be sure to do it; after <kei>, on no account do it) (j:hamtang/in) (r:zd:21664/zd:23538) (q:draft)
hanciam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:try/strive/make an effort) (d:make an effort to do or reach something; it often follows a purpose clause with <dingin> or <nadingin>) (s:hahkat/hamciam) (r:20.2.2) (q:draft)
hanciamding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:will try/will strive) (d:<hanciam> and <ding> written as one word: will make an effort, is to strive) (j:hanciam/ding) (r:zd:20263/zd:23443/zd:19868) (q:draft)
hanciampih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:help to achieve/work hard for/strive with) (d:<hanciam>, strive, with <pih>, together with or for: make an effort for someone or for a cause, help someone to reach something) (b:hanciam) (r:zd:19593/zd:12470/zd:10742) (q:draft)
hanciamtak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/work) (w:diligently/with effort/earnestly) (d:<hanciam>, strive, with <tak>, which makes an adverb of manner, mostly as {hanciamtak in}: with real effort, trying hard) (j:hanciam/tak) (r:zd:20860/zd:24276) (q:draft)
Handbag = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:handbag) (d:a woman's bag for money and small things, in the articles usually written with a capital) (s:sumbawm) (o:English) (r:zd:12901/zd:16676) (q:draft)
Handphone = (i:1) (t:n) (f:it) (w:mobile phone/cell phone/handphone) (d:a mobile telephone, the word used in Malaysian and Singaporean English) (o:English) (r:zd:11874/zd:20227) (q:draft)
hangaa = (i:1) (t:prep) (f:everyday) (w:because of/due to) (d:<hang>, reason, and <aa> written as one word, placed after a noun or clause: because of it, the same as <hangin> after a noun) (j:hang/aa) (r:zd:23787/zd:23988) (q:draft)
hangh = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:we) (d:sentence-final marker for a first person plural subject that includes the hearer, used in place of <i> before the verb and <hi> after it, as {hi hangh}, we are; also written <hang>; compare <ung>) (r:zd:19147/zd:23731/zd:14755) (q:draft)
hanghi = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:is because of/is due to) (d:<hang> and <hi> written as one word, after a noun or clause: it is because of that) (j:hang/hi) (r:zd:21876/zd:12990) (q:draft)
hanghiam = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:why/for what reason) (d:<hang> and <hiam> written as one word, after <bang>, what: {bang hanghiam} asks why, and {bang hanghiam cih leh} introduces the reason, because) (j:hang/hiam) (r:zd:18241/zd:20763) (q:draft)
hanginzong = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:even though/even because of) (d:<hangin> and <zong> written as one word: after a verb, even though; after a noun, even because of it, or because of it too) (j:hangin/zong) (r:zd:17547/zd:19109/zd:15300) (q:draft)
hangmah = (i:1) (t:prep) (f:everyday) (w:because of/precisely because of) (d:<hang> reason and the emphatic <mah> written as one word after a noun or <tua>: for that very reason; {tua hangmah in} is for that very reason) (j:hang/mah) (r:zd:24531/zd:25224) (q:draft)
hangpen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:the reason is) (d:<hang>, reason, and the topic marker <pen>, written as one word; {a hangpen} introduces the reason for what was just said) (j:hang/pen) (r:zd:24320) (q:draft)
hangsanna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:courage/bravery/boldness) (d:<hangsan>, brave, with the noun suffix <na>) (s:hanna/ngamna) (b:hangsan) (r:zd:17958/zd:25165/zd:16441) (q:draft)
hangsantak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:bravely/boldly/courageously) (d:<hangsan> and <tak> written as one word, mostly followed by <in>: bravely, with courage) (j:hangsan/tak) (r:zd:21085/zd:11619/zd:25678) (q:draft)
hangtawh = (i:1) (t:prep) (f:everyday/media) (w:because of/on account of/due to) (d:<hang> and <tawh> written as one word after a noun: because of it, on account of it; frequent in news reports for the reason of an arrest or a charge) (j:hang/tawh) (r:zd:17731/zd:15431/zd:12708) (q:draft)
Hangzhou = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel/media) (w:Hangzhou) (d:a city in the east of China) (r:zd:14812) (q:draft)
hanlungciam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:strive/make an effort) (d:poetic word, apparently a fuller form of <hanciam>, strive; known from the Zomi motto {Zomi te lung kituak, hanlungciam khangto diam}) (r:zd:16087) (q:draft, low confidence)
hanmual = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/religion) (w:cemetery/graveyard/burial ground) (d:<han>, grave, with <mual>, hill: the place where the dead of a community are buried) (r:zd:17375/ts:2009) (q:draft)
hanmualah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:religion/social) (w:at the cemetery/to the cemetery) (d:<hanmual>, cemetery, from <han>, grave, and <mual>, hill, with the place marker <ah>: at or to the burial ground) (j:hanmual/ah) (r:zd:21522/zd:21987) (q:draft)
hansanna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:courage/bravery/boldness/daring) (d:courage, also in the bad sense of rash daring; {hansan} is another spelling of <hangsan>, brave, here with the noun suffix <na>) (b:hangsan) (r:zd:21876/zd:19783/zd:17271) (q:draft)
hardware = (i:1) (t:n) (f:it) (w:hardware/equipment) (d:the machines and physical parts of a computer or network, as against software; also in English shop and company names for building materials) (o:English) (r:ts:7156) (q:draft, low confidence)
Harvard = (i:1) (t:name) (f:education) (w:Harvard) (d:Harvard University in the United States) (r:zd:9233/zd:9212) (q:draft)
hat = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/body) (w:strong/mighty/powerful) (d:strong, said of a person, an arm, an enemy, the wind or a city; often with <tha>, strength, as in {a tha hat}, his strength is great; after a verb it means do something fast or much, as in {tai hat}, run fast) (s:thahat/vanglian) (a:thanem) (r:19.24.8) (q:draft)
Hatamas = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel) (w:Sri Hartamas) (d:Sri Hartamas, a district of Kuala Lumpur in Malaysia, home of a Zomi church fellowship) (r:zd:19430) (q:draft, low confidence)
