hatlo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/body) (w:not strong/weak) (d:<hat> and <lo> written as one word: not strong, weak; after a verb, not doing it much or often) (j:hat/lo) (r:zd:19271/zd:21081) (q:draft)
hatmahmah = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/nature) (w:very strong/very fast) (d:<hat> and <mahmah> written as one word: very strong, of wind, faith or an animal; of movement, very fast) (j:hat/mahmah) (r:zd:13138/zd:20906) (q:draft)
hatsaklua = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:go too fast/speed) (d:<hatsak>, make strong or fast, with <lua>, too much, written as one word: of a vehicle or its driver, go too fast, the usual cause given for road accidents) (j:hatsak/lua) (r:zd:17100/zd:18005/zd:13233) (q:draft)
hatsatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:suffering/harsh treatment/affliction/abuse) (d:hard and cruel things that a person has to bear, often done by others; {hatsatna thuak} is to suffer it) (s:gimna) (r:zd:19750/zd:22556) (q:draft)
hattak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/travel) (w:fast/at high speed/hard) (d:<hat>, strong, and <tak> written as one word, mostly followed by <in>: with force, and of a vehicle at high speed) (j:hat/tak) (r:zd:15836/zd:17100/zd:18005) (q:draft)
hau = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/work) (w:rich/wealthy) (d:rich, or as a verb be rich; after a noun it means have much of it, as in {sum hau}, rich in money) (s:sumhau) (a:zawng) (q:draft)
hausa upa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:village headman/village elders/local leaders) (d:<hausa>, chief, and <upa>, elder: the headman and elders of a village or quarter, the local leadership, also the office of headman itself; stands after <khuasung> or <vengsung> and takes <te> for the persons) (r:zd:25126/zd:22758) (q:draft, low confidence)
hausa upate = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:chief and elders/village authorities) (d:<hausa>, chief or headman, and <upate>, elders, said as a pair: the headman and the elders of a village as the body that rules it and judges its cases; often after <khua>, village) (r:zd:20176/zd:25114) (q:draft)
Hawaii = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:travel) (w:Hawaii) (d:group of islands in the Pacific Ocean that is a state of the United States) (r:zd:25916/zd:14559/zd:19262) (q:draft)
hawh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/travel) (w:visit/call on/go to see) (d:go to see a person or a place) (s:veh) (q:draft)
