hawhtohna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/travel) (w:going up to visit/visiting) (d:<hawh>, visit, with <tohna>, going up, written as one word; paired with <hawhsuk> as {hawhsuk hawhtohna}, going down and up on visits, going here and there to see people) (j:hawh/tohna) (r:zd:22652) (q:draft)
hawih = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (j:hoih) (r:zd:19210/zd:19166) (q:draft)
hawihna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/body) (w:build/form/appearance) (d:the shape, build or good appearance of a body, a building or a road; the meaning is inferred from few sentences) (r:zd:20545/zd:21458) (q:draft, low confidence)
hawlgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:drive recklessly/drive wildly) (d:<hawl>, drive, and <gawp>, violently, written as one word: drive a vehicle fast and without care) (j:hawl/gawp) (r:zd:15953/zd:17353) (q:draft)
hawlkhiading = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:will drive out/will expel) (d:<hawlkhia>, drive out, with <ding>, will, written as one word; after <ki> it is passive, {ki hawlkhiading}, will be expelled or deported) (j:hawlkhia/ding) (r:zd:11746/zd:16323) (q:draft)
hawm = (i:2) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:empty/hollow) (d:with nothing inside: empty or hollow, and of ears of grain thin; {khut hawm guak} is empty-handed) (s:awng/hawmguak) (a:dim) (q:draft)
hawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:divide/distribute/share) (d:give each person a part of something: divide land, goods or spoil among people, or share what one has with others) (s:khen/sehkhen) (r:45.12.13) (q:draft)
hawmkhiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/work) (w:distribution/giving out/release) (d:<hawmkhiat>, distribute, with the noun suffix <na>: the giving out of something to many people, as money, water, electricity or news; of a book, its release) (b:hawmkhia) (r:zd:24396/zd:16014/zd:24060) (q:draft)
hawmsiam = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:social) (w:generous/good at sharing) (d:<hawm>, share out, with <siam>, skilled: sharing what one has freely and fairly; also to share out well, as in {nasep hawmsiam}, divide the work well. The proverb {hawmsiam nungta, nebum si} says that the one who shares lives and the one who eats alone dies) (r:zd:22171/zd:22391) (q:draft)
hawmthawhna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:criticism/fault-finding/disparagement) (d:finding fault with what others do and counting it as too little; named together with <gensiatna> and <phunsanna>) (b:hawmthawh) (r:zd:25354/zd:16424) (q:draft)
hawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food) (w:sip/drink) (d:drink a liquid in small mouthfuls, said of tea, hot water or soup: {niangtui hawp} is drink tea) (r:zd:22858/zd:24276) (q:draft)
he = (i:1) (t:intj) (f:everyday) (w:yes/uh-huh) (d:a short word of assent in speech: yes; most other uses in the articles are the English pronoun inside English text) (r:zd:19518/zd:23249) (q:draft, low confidence)
Headquarters = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/work) (w:headquarters/head office) (d:the main office of an army, a police force, a company or an organisation, mostly after its English name) (s:zumpi) (o:English) (r:zd:11536/ts:3168) (q:draft)
Heathrow = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel) (w:Heathrow) (d:the main international airport of London, in England) (r:zd:12632/zd:17711) (q:draft)
Hebrew = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (f:religion) (j:Hebru) (r:zd:19111/zd:24377/zd:17509) (q:draft)
Hebrews = (i:1) (t:name) (f:religion) (j:Hebru) (r:zd:9241/ts:9862) (q:draft)
heel = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/family) (w:court/woo) (d:of a young man: visit a young woman and seek her as wife; also go to a place again and again) (r:zd:16803/zd:19419/zd:8389) (q:draft)
heh = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/social) (w:angry) (d:feeling anger; the person one is angry with is followed by <tungah>)
hehmahmah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:be very angry/be furious) (d:<heh> and <mahmah> written as one word: be very angry) (j:heh/mahmah) (r:zd:13028/zd:13005/zd:17123) (q:draft)
hehnem tahen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:religion/social) (w:may he comfort) (d:<hehnem>, comfort, and <tahen>, the word of a wish: formula of condolence at the end of a death notice, with {Topa'n} or another name of God as subject and <hong> before it, may the Lord comfort you or us) (r:zd:17463/zd:20263) (q:draft)
hehnemsiampa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:Comforter/skilled comforter) (d:<hehnem>, comfort, and <siampa>, the one skilled at it, written as one word: the one who knows how to comfort, said of the Holy Spirit in messages of condolence) (s:hehnempa) (j:hehnem/siampa) (r:zd:25091/zd:24150) (q:draft)
Heilei = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua) (f:travel) (w:Heilei) (d:a Zomi village in Chin State, Myanmar, listed among the villages where the Teizang dialect is spoken) (r:zd:19952) (q:draft)
hekna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:accusation/charge) (d:<hek>, accuse, with the noun ending <na>: a charge brought against someone; {hekna thuak} is the one accused) (b:hek) (r:zd:9124) (q:draft, low confidence)
Helicopter = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:helicopter) (o:English) (r:zd:11621/zd:25346) (q:draft)
helkha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:be included/be mixed in/be involved) (d:<hel>, mix in, and <kha>, happen to, written as one word; nearly always after <ki>: come to be included in a group, or get mixed into something) (j:hel/kha) (r:zd:19239/zd:19550/zd:14720) (q:draft)
hello = (i:1) (t:intj) (f:everyday/social) (w:hello) (d:word of greeting at the start of a conversation, a letter or a phone call) (o:English) (r:zd:16337/zd:12342) (q:draft)
hello = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not be included/be left out) (d:<hel>, include, with <lo>, not, written as one word; mostly as {ki hello}, is not included) (j:hel/lo) (r:zd:21931/zd:21706) (q:draft)
Helmet = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/home) (w:helmet/crash helmet) (d:a hard protective hat, in the news mostly that of a motorcycle rider; often written with a capital and beside <lukhu>) (s:lukhu) (o:English) (r:zd:15913/zd:19353/zd:12994) (q:draft)
hemkhiading = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/everyday) (w:will remove/to evacuate/to deport/to clear away) (d:<hemkhia>, remove, and the future marker <ding> written as one word; of people, with <ki>: be evacuated or sent out of a place) (j:hemkhia/ding) (r:zd:12422/zd:11623) (q:draft)
hemkhiapah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:remove at once/evacuate immediately) (d:<hemkhia>, move away or remove, and <pah>, at once, written as one word) (j:hemkhia/pah) (r:zd:15101/zd:16947/zd:15924) (q:draft)
hemkhiasak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/travel) (w:evacuate/move out/remove) (d:<hemkhia>, remove, with the causative ending {-sak}: make people leave a place; {ki hemkhiasak} is be evacuated, be moved out) (b:hemkhia) (r:zd:12040/zd:17777/zd:19514) (q:draft)
hemkhiathei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:be able to remove/be able to take out) (d:<hemkhia>, remove, and <thei>, be able, written as one word: manage to take out or bring away a person or a thing, as people from a burning vehicle or a bomb from a building) (j:hemkhia/thei) (r:zd:17800/zd:11081) (q:draft)
hen aw = (i:1) (t:part) (f:religion/social) (w:may it be/oh may) (d:<hen>, let or may, and <aw>, the calling word oh: closes a sentence as a heartfelt wish, oh may it be so; used in traditional songs, blessings and prayers, after the verb and often after <ta>) (r:zd:12023/zd:16038) (q:draft)
Henan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:travel) (w:Henan) (d:a province in central China) (r:zd:17701/zd:12355) (q:draft)
heng = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:health/body) (w:decayed/worm-eaten) (d:of a tooth: decayed, eaten hollow; {ha heng} is a decayed tooth and {lung heng} is worm-eaten) (r:zd:21120/zd:9133) (q:draft, low confidence)
hento = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:push up into/thrust in/insert) (d:push or stick something up into an opening or a narrow space; the ending is <to>, upward) (r:zd:17402/zd:14748) (q:draft, low confidence)
Hepatitis = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health) (w:hepatitis) (d:the liver disease hepatitis, named with its type as in {Hepatitis B}) (o:English) (r:zd:17834) (q:draft)
hepkhiatding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:will be removed/to remove) (d:<hepkhiat>, remove, and the future marker <ding> written as one word: to be removed, will remove or clear away) (j:hepkhiat/ding) (r:zd:13155/zd:12442) (q:draft)
hepkhiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/politics) (w:removal/taking away/clearing out) (d:<hepkhiat>, remove, with the noun suffix {-na}: the removing of a thing or the sending away of people) (b:hepkhiat) (r:zd:21142/zd:12422) (q:draft)
Hero = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/media) (w:hero) (d:a person who is admired and looked up to) (s:galhang) (o:English) (r:zd:24739) (q:draft, low confidence)
Heroin = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/politics) (w:heroin) (d:the illegal drug heroin, in reports of drug seizures) (o:English) (r:zd:14748/zd:11348) (q:draft)
hethet = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:at all/in the least) (d:<het> said twice for force: before a negative, not at all; after a verb of change without a negative it appears to mean steadily, more and more) (b:het) (r:zd:11882/zd:21178) (q:draft)
hetloding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:will not at all/must never) (d:<hetlo>, not at all, and <ding>, will, written as one word after a verb: will certainly not, and of a duty, must on no account) (j:hetlo/ding) (r:zd:11251/zd:23943/zd:19562) (q:draft)
hetlohding = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:must never/should not at all) (d:<hetloh>, not at all, with <ding>, written as one word after a verb: the action must not happen at all; {koihkhak hetlohding} is must never be left) (j:hetloh/ding) (r:zd:15317/zd:20440/zd:11590) (q:draft)
hi mah = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:yes) (d:it is so, said in agreement) (r:zai:yes) (q:draft)
hiaa = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:being/and so) (d:<hi> and the linking <a> written as one word: is and, being; {tua hiaa} is that being so, therefore, and {na hiaa} is whether you are) (j:hi/a) (r:zd:20747/zd:21502/zd:23972) (q:draft)
hiah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/travel) (w:here) (d:in or at this place; {Hiah om ing}, here I am, is the answer of someone who is called) (s:hihlai-ah) (a:tuasan)
hiai = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (d:after a verb, usually doubled as {hiai-hiai}: steadily, more and more, of something that goes on little by little) (r:zd:21626/zd:12313) (q:draft, low confidence)
hiai = (i:2) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:this) (d:this, in writing close to Paite, where Tedim Zolai has <hih>; {hiai hun} is this time or this programme) (r:zd:12074) (q:draft, low confidence)
hiaihiai = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:gradually/steadily/more and more) (d:placed after a verb to show that a change goes on step by step: {kiam hiaihiai} is keep decreasing) (s:semsem) (r:zd:23765/ts:3369/zd:15274) (q:draft)
hiam = (i:3) (t:adj) (f:everyday/home) (w:sharp) (d:having a keen edge, of a knife or blade; the opposite of <mawl>, blunt) (r:zai:bluntness) (q:draft, low confidence)
hiam cihleh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:because/the reason is/namely) (d:<hiam>, the word that ends a question, and <cihleh>, if one says: closes a question that the speaker then answers; {banghang hiam cihleh}, if one asks why, is because, for, and the answer often ends in {ahih man hi}; after another question word it means as for what or how, it is this) (r:zd:14927/zd:23297) (q:draft)
hiam cihpen = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday/media) (w:as to whether/the question of) (d:the question word <hiam>, whether or which, with <cihpen>, as for what is said: closes an indirect question and makes it the topic, as to whether or what or who; a verb of knowing, saying or inquiring follows, often negated) (r:zd:15425/zd:12099/zd:19303) (q:draft)
hiamcih = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:whether/what/why) (d:the question particle <hiam> with <cih>, saying, written as one word: closes a question that is reported or thought about, what, why or whether something is; {banghang hiamcih leh}, if one asks why, means because) (j:hiam/cih) (r:zd:21706/zd:19915/zd:18924) (q:draft)
hiamvan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:weapon/arms) (d:<hiam>, sharp, with <van>, goods: a weapon, any tool for wounding or killing; often named together with <galvan>) (s:galvan) (r:zd:15374/zd:17069/zd:12257) (q:draft)
Hiangzing = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua) (f:travel) (w:Hiangzing) (d:village near Taingen on the road between Kalaymyo and Tedim) (r:zd:19358/zd:20972/ts:5513) (q:draft)
hiaulo = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:hardly/not really/not at all) (d:<hiau> and <lo> written as one word after a verb: not really, hardly or not at all so) (j:hiau/lo) (r:zd:22396/zd:22448/zd:21866) (q:draft, low confidence)
hibang = (i:1) (t:det) (f:everyday) (w:such/like this/this kind of) (d:a short form of <hih>, this, with <bang>, like, written as one word: like this, of this kind; {hibang in} and {hibang dan in} are in this way) (j:hih/bang) (r:zd:16897/zd:21869/zd:23487) (q:draft)
hibangdan = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:like this/of this kind/such) (d:<hih>, this, <bang>, like, and <dan>, manner, written as one word in a shortened spelling: in this way, of this kind; before a noun, such) (j:hih/bang/dan) (r:zd:16391/zd:19550) (q:draft)
hibangin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:like this/in this way/as follows/thus) (d:<hih>, this, and <bangin>, in the way of, written as one word: in this way; before a verb of saying it introduces the words that follow) (s:hibang) (j:hih/bangin) (r:zd:23670/zd:22122/zd:15384) (q:draft)
hibilbel = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:happen to be/be just then) (d:<hi>, be, with <bilbel>, as it happened, written as one word: it just happened to be so, as things turned out) (b:hi) (r:zd:15051/zd:15949/zd:18157) (q:draft, low confidence)
hici bang = (i:1) (t:det) (f:everyday) (w:such/this kind of/like this) (d:<hici>, like this, and <bang>, like: placed before a noun, such a one or this kind of, pointing to what was just described) (r:zd:24814/zd:22623/zd:24356) (q:draft)
hiciang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:this far/up to here/to this point) (d:<hi>, here a short form of <hih>, this, with <ciang>, up to: as far as this, to this point or extent; {hiciang tung} is reach this far) (r:zd:19589/zd:19556/zd:22171) (q:draft)
hicibanga = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:like this/in this way/thus) (d:<hici>, like this, and <banga>, in the manner of, written as one word before a verb: in this way, so suddenly as this) (j:hici/banga) (r:zd:21369/zd:13178) (q:draft)
hicih = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:the sentence ending <hi> and <cih> written as one word, closing a statement that is reported, known or thought: that it is so; {om hicih phawk in} is remember that there is) (j:hi/cih) (r:zd:21083/zd:25932/zd:21989) (q:draft)
hicih = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:like this/in this way) (d:do or be like this; paired with {huacih}, like that) (s:hici) (r:zd:24130/zd:17675) (q:draft, low confidence)
hidan = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:like this/this way/such) (d:{hih dan} written as one word with the final h dropped: this manner, like this; before a noun, such a, and alone, such a thing) (j:hih/dan) (r:zd:25601/zd:17687/zd:24082) (q:draft)
hiden = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:always be/be constantly) (d:<hi>, be, and <den>, always, written as one word: it is always so, it keeps being so) (j:hi/den) (r:zd:14507/zd:10731/zd:10892) (q:draft)
hiding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:will be/must be/probably is) (d:<hi>, be, and the marker <ding> for what is to come, written as one word: will be, is to be, or is probably) (j:hi/ding) (r:zd:20328/zd:21856/zd:12822) (q:draft)
hiding cihi = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:media) (w:it is said to be likely/is believed to be/reportedly) (d:<hiding>, will be or probably is, and <cihi>, he said or it is said: closes a news sentence and marks what stands before it as the guess of the source, not an established fact) (r:zd:17834/zd:11889) (q:draft)
hiding hiven = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:it must be/presumably/I suppose) (d:<hiding>, it will be, and <hiven>, it is so after all: closes a clause that gives the speaker's guess at the reason or circumstance of what is told next, it must be that, presumably) (r:zd:26097/zd:19779) (q:draft)
hiding kici = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:media) (w:is said to be/is believed to be/is thought to be) (d:<hiding>, probably is, and <kici>, be said: closes a news statement that reports what people suppose and is not confirmed, it is said that it probably is; <hi> may follow) (r:zd:15435/zd:17375) (q:draft)
hidinga = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:will be) (d:<hi> and <dinga> written as one word: it will be so, and; closes one clause about what is to be and links it to the next) (j:hi/dinga) (r:zd:23487/zd:20968) (q:draft)
hidinghi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:will be/must be) (d:<hi>, <ding> and a second <hi> that ends the sentence, written as one word: it will be; in reports, it is probably so, it must be) (j:hi/ding) (r:zd:11062/zd:16772) (q:draft)
hidinghiam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:could it be/might be) (d:<hi>, <ding> and <hiam> written as one word: a question or doubt about what may be so, could it be that, whether it might be; often before {cihpen kitheician nailo hi}, it is not yet known) (j:hi/ding/hiam) (r:zd:20302/zd:12208/zd:11283) (q:draft)
hidingin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:to be/as being) (d:<hi> and <dingin> written as one word: that it is or will be so, mostly before a verb of believing or supposing such as <um> and <ummawh>) (j:hi/dingin) (r:zd:21829/zd:23298) (q:draft)
Highway = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:highway/expressway) (d:a main road for fast traffic between towns) (s:lamlian) (o:English) (r:zd:13332/zd:20406/zd:19036) (q:draft)
higige = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:always be/be constantly) (d:<hi>, be, and <gige>, always, written as one word: it is always so, it remains so) (j:hi/gige) (r:zd:11364/zd:16580) (q:draft)
hih = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:this) (d:points to a person or thing near the speaker or just mentioned; before a noun it means this or these, and {hih bangin} is in this way) (a:tua) (r:43.8.4)
hih = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:do) (r:zai:do) (q:draft)
hihang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:we are) (d:<hi>, be, and <hang>, here the verb ending for we including the hearer, written as one word at the end of a sentence: we are; after <ding>, we shall) (j:hi/hang) (r:zd:23057/zd:20860/zd:20329) (q:draft)
hihangh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (j:hihang) (r:zd:15874/zd:16336) (q:draft)
hihbang = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:like this/such/as follows) (d:<hih> and <bang> written as one word: of this kind; before <in>, in this way) (j:hih/bang) (r:zd:22992/zd:16849/zd:14718) (q:draft)
hihbangaa = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:like this/in this way/thus) (d:<hih>, <bang> and <aa> written as one word, where <aa> stands for the adverb ending more often written <in>: in this way, like this) (j:hih/bang/aa) (r:zd:20545/zd:19239) (q:draft)
hihbangdan = (i:1) (t:det) (f:everyday) (w:this kind of/such/like this) (d:<hih>, <bang> and <dan> written as one word: of this kind, in this way; before a noun it means such a) (j:hih/bang/dan) (r:zd:11803/zd:16946/zd:19567) (q:draft)
hihbangin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:like this/in this way/thus) (d:<hih> and <bangin> written as one word: in this way, like this; it points to what has just been told or to the words that follow) (j:hih/bangin) (r:zd:23670/zd:17841/zd:24276) (q:draft)
hihciang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:this far/to this point/to this extent) (d:<hih>, this, and <ciang>, as far as, written as one word: up to this point or level, often with <tung>, reach, or followed by <dong>) (j:hih/ciang) (r:zd:11103/zd:20091/zd:21219) (q:draft)
hihdan = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:like this/in this way/thus) (d:<hih>, this, with <dan>, manner, written as one word: this way, like this; {hihdan in} introduces what is said or done) (j:hih/dan) (r:zd:21607/zd:16216/zd:25223) (q:draft)
hihding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:to be/to do) (d:<hih> and <ding> written as one word: to be something, or what is to be done; {hihding kisam} is it is necessary to be) (j:hih/ding) (r:zd:21085/zd:21235/zd:11346) (q:draft)
hihetlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be not at all/be by no means) (d:<hi>, be, with <hetlo>, not at all, written as one word: it is not that at all) (j:hi/hetlo) (r:zd:12072/zd:15759/zd:25228) (q:draft)
hihhang = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:because of this/because it is/although it is) (d:<hih> and <hang>, reason, written as one word. {Hihhang in} is because of this; {a hihhang}, with <hih> the form of <hi>, be, is because it is so or although it is so, and alone it opens a sentence as even so) (j:hih/hang) (r:zd:15848/zd:16022/zd:25221) (q:draft)
hihhangin = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:however/although/even though) (d:the form <hih> of the verb be with <hangin>, written as one word after <a> or <na>: {a hihhangin} is although it is so, however, and {na hihhangin} is although you are) (j:hih/hangin) (r:zd:17883/zd:22988/zd:22171) (q:draft)
hihhun = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:time) (w:this time/this period) (d:<hih>, this, and <hun>, time, written as one word; {hihhun sungah} is during this time) (j:hih/hun) (r:zd:12708/zd:14826) (q:draft)
hihi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:is/am/are) (d:<hi>, be, written as one word with the sentence-final <hi> that follows it, after <a>, <ka>, <na> or <i>: {a hihi} is it is, {ka hihi} I am) (r:zd:20892/zd:21417/zd:24064) (q:draft)
hihiam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:is it/are/is) (d:<hi> and <hiam> written as one word: the verb to be at the end of a question, as in {bang hihiam}, what is it, and {na hihiam}, are you) (j:hi/hiam) (r:zd:10857/zd:21989/zd:24427) (q:draft)
hihkei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not be so) (d:<hih> and <kei> written as one word, <hih> being the form of <hi>, be, used before <leh>: {a hihkei leh} is if it is not so, otherwise, or else) (j:hih/kei) (r:zd:20195/zd:21012) (q:draft)
hihkeileh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:or/or else/otherwise) (d:<hih>, be so, with <kei>, not, and <leh>, if, written as one word and used after <a> as {a hihkeileh}: if it is not so, and so or, between two things of which one is chosen) (j:hih/kei/leh) (r:zd:21083/zd:21155) (q:draft)
hihleh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:if it is/as for) (d:<hih>, here the form of <hi> before an ending, with <leh>, written as one word after <a>, <na> or <ih>: if it is, if you are; after a noun or pronoun also as for; the same as <ahihleh>) (j:hih/leh) (r:zd:19969/zd:22742) (q:draft)
hihmah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:indeed be/truly be) (d:<hih>, here the form of <hi>, be, used before a following word, with emphatic <mah>, written as one word; {a hihmah bangin} is just as it really is, in keeping with what it is) (r:zd:17309/zd:17655) (q:draft, low confidence)
hihman = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:because/since) (d:<hih>, here the form of <hi>, be, with <man>, here reason, written as one word; stands after <a>, <i>, <ka> or <na> at the end of a clause, often followed by <in>: because it is, because we are; the same as {ahih manin}) (j:hih/man) (r:zd:23572/zd:21662/zd:11206) (q:draft)
hihmanin = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:because/since) (d:<hih>, here the form of <hi>, be, with <manin>, because, written as one word; stands after <a>, <i>, <ka> or <na> at the end of a clause: because it is, because I am; the same as {ahih manin}) (j:hih/manin) (r:zd:20892/zd:23212/zd:20896) (q:draft)
hihmawhna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/everyday) (w:worry/anxiety/concern) (d:used after <lung>, heart, as {lung hihmawhna}: worry or concern about what may happen; <hihmawh> with the noun ending <na>) (s:lunghihmawhna) (b:hihmawh) (r:zd:20633/zd:17896/zd:20895) (q:draft)
hihmun = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:this place/here) (d:<hih>, this, and <mun>, place, written as one word: this place; {hihmun ah} is here, at this point) (j:hih/mun) (r:zd:24289/zd:20477/zd:24593) (q:draft)
hihna taktak = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:true identity/real self/true nature) (d:<hihna>, the fact of being, and <taktak>, real: what a person or a people really is, as against how others see them; it follows a possessor, as in {i hihna taktak}, what we really are) (r:zd:13076/zd:25139/zd:16060) (q:draft)
hihnu = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:she/her/this woman) (d:<hih>, this, with <nu> marking a woman: this woman, she, said of a woman who is present or being spoken about) (s:tuanu)
hihpa = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:he/him/this man) (d:<hih>, this, with <pa> marking a man: this man, he, said of a man who is present or being spoken about) (s:tuapa) (r:1.5.29)
hihpen = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:this) (d:<hih>, this, with the topic marker <pen>, written as one word: this, as the thing spoken about) (j:hih/pen) (r:zd:21219/zd:20092/zd:16665) (q:draft)
hihtawh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/media) (w:with this/including this) (d:<hih> and <tawh> written as one word: with this, counting this one; {hihtawh kisai in} is concerning this) (j:hih/tawh) (r:zd:12645/zd:14606) (q:draft)
hihteng = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:all these/these) (d:<hih>, this, with <teng>, here in its sense of all of, written as one word: all these, the things just named or about to be named) (j:hih/teng) (r:zd:22203/zd:25180/zd:23332) (q:draft)
hihthu = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:this matter/this) (d:<hih>, this, and <thu>, matter or word, written as one word: this matter, what has just been told) (j:hih/thu) (r:ts:3366/zd:24314/zd:21869) (q:draft)
hihtuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:seem to be/appear to be/apparently be) (d:a form of <hi>, be, joined with <tuak> and written as one word at the end of a statement: it seems, it appears that; the writer passes on or infers something without stating it as certain) (r:zd:12327/zd:17945/zd:17856) (q:draft, low confidence)
hihtuaklo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:seem not to be/probably not be) (d:<hihtuak>, seem to be, with <lo>, not, written as one word: it does not seem to be, it is probably not) (j:hihtuak/lo) (r:zd:13072/zd:15732/zd:15788) (q:draft)
hihvai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/media) (w:this matter/this affair/this case) (d:<hih>, this, and <vai>, matter, written as one word; {hihvai tawh kisai in} is concerning this matter) (j:hih/vai) (r:zd:17547/zd:15951/zd:13243) (q:draft)
hihvaitawh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:media/everyday) (w:with this matter) (d:<hih>, this, <vai>, matter, and <tawh>, with, written as one word; used in {hihvaitawh kisai in}, concerning this matter) (j:hih/vai/tawh) (r:zd:18244/zd:17188) (q:draft)
hihzahliang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:to this extent/as much as this/on this scale) (d:<hihzah>, this much, and <liang>, even, written as one word, usually with <in>: to such a degree as this, often of something never seen before) (j:hihzah/liang) (r:zd:20173/zd:17802) (q:draft)
hii = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (j:hi) (r:zd:24417/zd:21626) (q:draft, low confidence)
hiin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:being/is and) (d:<hi>, be, and <in> written as one word: being so, is this and, closing one clause and linking it to the next) (j:hi/in) (r:zd:20900/zd:21027) (q:draft)
hiithiat = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (j:hithiat) (r:zd:21780/zd:21117) (q:draft)
Hijack = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/politics) (w:hijack) (d:seize a plane or vehicle by force; used with other words, as {ki Hijack}, be hijacked, and {Hijack bawl}, carry out a hijacking) (o:English) (r:zd:11827/zd:12108) (q:draft)
hik = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (f:nature/health) (w:louse/head louse/lice) (d:a louse, the small insect that lives in hair and clothing) (r:zd:21690) (q:draft)
hik = (i:2) (t:n) (f:health) (w:germ/virus) (d:the germ or virus that causes a disease; {natna hik} is a disease germ) (r:zd:19858/zd:19846) (q:draft)
hik = (i:3) (t:adj) (f:body/health) (w:numb) (d:without feeling, of the body or a limb; {khe hik} is the feet go numb) (r:zd:16287/zd:12541) (q:draft, low confidence)
hikei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:is not/be not) (d:<hi>, be, and <kei>, not, written as one word: it is not so; {tua hikei leh} is if not, otherwise) (j:hi/kei) (r:zd:20808/zd:20545/zd:25447) (q:draft)
hikhading = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:probably be/may be) (d:<hikha>, may be, and <ding>, will, written as one word: it is probably so, it must be; a guess of the writer) (j:hikha/ding) (r:zd:15754/zd:16834) (q:draft)
hikhinlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not all be/not wholly be) (d:<hikhin> and <lo> written as one word: not be so in every case, not all or not wholly so, often after <khempeuh>, all) (j:hikhin/lo) (r:zd:17177/zd:14892/zd:19340) (q:draft)
hikhinta = (i:1) (t:v) (f:time/everyday) (w:have already been/have become) (d:<hi> and <khinta> written as one word: it already is, it has now come to be, said mostly of a length of time or a number that has been reached) (j:hi/khinta) (r:zd:20050/zd:15924/zd:20562) (q:draft)
hilai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:still is/is still) (d:<hi> joined with the word for still, as in {om lai}, still there: is still so, remains) (j:hi/lai) (r:zd:24118/ts:3164) (q:draft)
hilai = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:here/this place) (d:<hih>, this, joined with the word for place or midst, as in {hih lai munah}: here, this place) (j:hih/lai) (r:zd:24310) (q:draft, low confidence)
hile = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:if/if it were) (d:<hi>, be, and <le>, if, written as one word and followed by the ending for the person, as {hile hang}, if we were, and {hile uh}, if they were) (s:hileh) (j:hi/le) (r:zd:17971/zd:23733) (q:draft)
hilecin = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:if you are/if you were) (d:<hi>, be, and <lecin>, if you, written as one word: if you are or were, if it were so with you) (j:hi/lecin) (r:zd:14613/zd:19709) (q:draft)
hileh kilawm = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:it seems that/apparently/it looks as if) (d:<hileh>, if it were, and <kilawm>, fitting: closes a statement that the speaker judges likely but does not know for sure, it seems that or presumably; stands after the verb and before the sentence-final <hi>) (r:zd:16897/zd:12998/zd:21945) (q:draft)
hilehang = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:if we were/if we could) (d:<hi>, be, and <lehang>, if we, written as one word after a verb or adjective: if we were so, if we did so, supposing that we) (j:hi/lehang) (r:zd:22312/zd:17339) (q:draft)
hileuleu = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (d:<hi>, be, with <leuleu>, in turn, written as one word: is in its turn, is again, on the other hand is) (j:hi/leuleu) (r:zd:24282/zd:17854) (q:draft)
hilh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/education) (w:teach/instruct) (d:teach or instruct someone, show how a thing is done) (s:thuhilh/sinsak) (a:sin) (q:draft)
hilhcian = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education/everyday) (w:explain/expound/make clear) (d:<hilh>, teach, with <cian>, clearly: explain a matter fully so that it is understood; of the Bible, expound) (r:zd:19976/zd:25475/zd:21656) (q:draft)
hilhcianna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education/media) (w:explanation/clarification) (d:<hilh>, teach, with <cian>, clearly, and the noun ending {-na}: an explanation that makes a matter clear) (r:zd:23989/zd:11702/zd:22950) (q:draft)
hilhlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education/everyday) (w:not teach/not tell) (d:<hilh>, teach, with <lo>, not, written as one word: not teach, without teaching) (j:hilh/lo) (r:zd:20964/zd:19465/zd:20970) (q:draft)
hiliang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:is even/amounts to) (d:<hi>, is, with <liang>, even, written as one word: it is as much as that, it even is; said with surprise at a number or degree) (j:hi/liang) (r:zd:19775/zd:20526/zd:11581) (q:draft)
hilo = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:not/no) (d:is not, the negative of <hi>, be, written as one word; as a reply it means no, it is not so) (b:hi) (q:draft)
hiloding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:will not be/is probably not) (d:<hilo> and <ding> written as one word: will not be, or in reports, is probably not, is thought not to be) (j:hilo/ding) (r:zd:12761/zd:11545) (q:draft)
hilohi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:is not/be not) (d:<hilo>, is not, with the sentence ending <hi>, written as one word: it is not, it is not so) (j:hilo/hi) (r:zd:24231/zd:17437/zd:23551) (q:draft)
hiloin = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:not being/and not/but) (d:<hilo> and <in> written as one word: it is not that, but; <bek hiloin> is not only) (j:hilo/in) (r:zd:24392/zd:25464/zd:23512) (q:draft)
hilozaw = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not be but rather/rather than being) (d:<hilo>, is not, and <zaw>, rather, written as one word, mostly as {hilozaw in}: it is not this but rather what follows) (j:hilo/zaw) (r:zd:16415/zd:17166) (q:draft)
himah ta = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:although/even though/even so) (d:<hi>, be, with the emphatic <mah> and <ta>, here the particle of a reached state and not the noun child: always followed by <leh>, <lehang> or {se leh}, and placed after a clause, although that is so; at the head of a sentence, even so) (s:himahleh) (r:zd:24502/zd:19662) (q:draft)
himah taleh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:although/even so/however) (d:<Himah>, it is indeed so, and <taleh>, even if: although that is so; placed after a clause it means although, and after a comma or at the start of a clause it means even so, however) (s:himahleh/ahizongin) (r:zd:11917/zd:25015/zd:11262) (q:draft)
himahleh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:but/although/however) (d:<hi>, <mah> and <leh> written as one word, placed after a clause: although that is so, but) (j:hi/mah/leh) (r:zd:12565/zd:14709) (q:draft)
himai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:just is/simply is) (d:<hi>, be, and <mai>, here a particle meaning just or simply and not the noun face, written as one word: it simply is so, there is nothing more to it; often with a tone of resignation or wonder) (r:zd:11259/zd:25477/zd:23037) (q:draft, low confidence)
himawhna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/health) (w:anxiety/worry) (d:used after <lung>, heart: {lung himawhna} is worry or anxiety, the same as <lunghimawhna>) (s:lunghimawhna) (b:himawh) (r:zd:24481/zd:10777) (q:draft)
himawkleh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:if indeed/if it should be) (d:<himawk> and <leh>, if, written as one word: if it should really be so, supposing that it were) (j:himawk/leh) (r:zd:14901/zd:18054) (q:draft)
himhim = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:at all/whatsoever/in itself) (d:placed after a noun or verb for emphasis: any at all, the thing as such; with a negative, not at all, by no means) (r:zd:23830/zd:25601/zd:22775) (q:draft)
hina = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:first part of <hinapi>, although, when that word is written apart as {hina pi-in} or {hina pi'n}: although it is so, even though being) (r:zd:11197/zd:19577) (q:draft)
hinai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be yet) (d:<hi> be and <nai> yet written as one word; used with a negative, {hinai lo} or {hinai kei}: is not yet) (j:hi/nai) (r:zd:24047/zd:11206) (q:draft)
hinawn = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be any longer) (d:<hi>, be, and <nawn>, any more, written as one word before <lo>: {hinawn lo} is no longer) (j:hi/nawn) (r:zd:21356/zd:20825/zd:24068) (q:draft)
hinawnlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be no longer/be not any more) (d:<hi>, be, and <nawnlo>, no longer, written as one word: is no longer what is named before it) (j:hi/nawnlo) (r:zd:19464/zd:20752/zd:23037) (q:draft)
Hindi = (i:1) (t:name) (f:social/education) (w:Hindi) (d:the Hindi language of India; {Hindi te} are the people who speak it) (r:zd:19875/zd:14965/ts:3506) (q:draft)
Hindu = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (f:religion) (w:Hindu) (d:a follower of Hinduism, the main religion of India, or of that religion; {Hindu biakna} is the Hindu religion and {Hindu te} are the Hindus) (r:zd:17577/zd:15884) (q:draft)
hingel = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:surely be/must be) (d:<hi>, be, and <ngel>, surely, written as one word: it surely is so, said of what the speaker supposes; {hingel ding hi} is it must be so) (j:hi/ngel) (r:zd:17409/zd:25173) (q:draft, low confidence)
hingtang = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:alive/living) (d:in a living state, not dead; {a hingtang in}, also written <hingtangin>, is alive, while still living, and {hingtang kipiakna} is a living offering of oneself) (b:hing) (r:zd:25749/zd:22650) (q:draft)
hipah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be just/be simply/be at once) (d:<hi>, be, and <pah>, at once, written as one word: it is simply that, it follows at once that it is so; {cihna hipah hi} is that is just what it means) (j:hi/pah) (r:zd:22641/zd:24320/zd:22701) (q:draft, low confidence)
hipan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be only/be just/be so far) (d:<hi>, be, written as one word with <pan>, here just, so far: is only this much as yet; mostly after an age, number or amount with <bek>, only, as in {kum 28 bek hipan hi}, is only 28 years old) (j:hi/pan) (r:zd:11782/zd:14597/zd:12307) (q:draft)
hipen = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:this) (d:<hih>, this, with the topic marker <pen>, written as one word at the start of a sentence: this, as for this) (j:hih/pen) (r:zd:16820/zd:21083) (q:draft)
hipen = (i:2) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:<hi>, be, with <pen> written as one word at the end of a clause: it is, is it) (j:hi/pen) (r:zd:19441/zd:16442) (q:draft, low confidence)
hipeuh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be so/be indeed) (d:<hi>, be, and <peuh> written as one word: {tua hipeuh leh} is if only that is so, in that case, and {hipeuh mah lo} is it is not so at all) (j:hi/peuh) (r:zd:11714/zd:25515/zd:11197) (q:draft)
hipeuhmah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (d:<hi> and <peuhmah> written as one word, found before <lo>: {hipeuhmah lo hi} is it is not necessarily so, it is by no means so) (j:hi/peuhmah) (r:zd:20315/zd:23554) (q:draft, low confidence)
hipeuhmahlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be not at all/be by no means) (d:<hi>, <peuhmah> and <lo> written as one word: is not at all, is by no means; a strong negative of <hi>, be) (j:hi/peuhmah/lo) (r:zd:19305/zd:11941/zd:15994) (q:draft)
hiphadiak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be mainly/be especially/be chiefly) (d:<hi> and <phadiak> written as one word at the end of a statement: it is mainly, it is above all) (j:hi/phadiak) (r:zd:15465/zd:15089/zd:11997) (q:draft)
hiphial = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be indeed/even if it is) (d:<hi>, be, with <phial>, written as one word: before {mah leh}, <taleh> or <zongin> it means even if it is so, and at the end of a sentence it is indeed so) (j:hi/phial) (r:zd:20083/zd:23057/zd:25242) (q:draft)
hiphot = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be so for now/be so far) (d:<hi>, the closing word of a statement, and <phot>, for the time being, written as one word at the end of a sentence: that is how it stands for now, so far) (j:hi/phot) (r:ts:5513/ts:8728/zd:16119) (q:draft, low confidence)
hipi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be the main one/be chiefly) (d:<hi>, be, with <pi>, great or chief, mostly as {hipi pen hi}: is the chief one, is mainly that; said of the main cause or the main example) (j:hi/pi) (r:zd:23338/zd:18086) (q:draft, low confidence)
hisam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be really/be exactly) (d:<hi>, be, with a softening particle, written as one word; mostly negative, {hisam lo hi} or {hisam kei}: it is not really so, it is not exactly that) (r:zd:24068/zd:25158/zd:25923) (q:draft)
hisamlo = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:is not really/is not at all) (d:<hi>, be, with <sam> and <lo>, not, written as one word: a stronger <hilo>, it is not really so, it is by no means so; <sam> here strengthens the negative and is not the verb call) (j:hi/sam/lo) (r:zd:22056/zd:15260/zd:16404) (q:draft)
hisawnsawn = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media) (w:turn out to be/happen to be) (d:<hi>, be, and <sawnsawn> written as one word: closes a statement in news reports that adds what someone or something proved to be: is in fact, turned out to be) (j:hi/sawnsawn) (r:zd:11731/zd:15456/zd:19562) (q:draft, low confidence)
historian = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:historian) (d:a person who studies and writes history; used beside the Zolai {tangthukan}) (o:English) (r:zd:23329) (q:draft, low confidence)
hitakpi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be truly so/really be/be indeed) (d:<hi> and <takpi> written as one word: it truly is so, be really the case) (j:hi/takpi) (r:zd:21670/zd:14750/zd:14805) (q:draft)
hitam = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:is it/is it so) (d:<hi>, be, with the question word <tam>, written as one word at the end of a question, often followed by <maw>: is it, could it be; {a takpi mah a hitam} is is it really so) (r:zd:22586/zd:23022) (q:draft, low confidence)
hiteh = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:<hi> and the second person ending <teh> written as one word, closing a statement about the person spoken to: you are, you will) (j:hi/teh) (r:zd:17271/zd:16245/zd:10746) (q:draft)
hiteng = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:all these/these/all this) (d:{hih teng} shortened and written as one word: these, all of the things or persons just named or about to be named) (r:zd:19654/zd:24276/zd:19953) (q:draft, low confidence)
hitheilo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be impossible/cannot be) (d:<hithei> and <lo> written as one word: it cannot be, it is not possible; {a hitheilo ding} is what cannot happen) (j:hithei/lo) (r:zd:19166/zd:23803/zd:14861) (q:draft)
hithu = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:this matter/this) (d:<hih>, this, with <thu>, matter, written as one word: this matter, the thing just spoken of) (j:hih/thu) (r:zd:24230/zd:25678/zd:23363) (q:draft)
hitota = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:has now reached/has come to be/is already) (d:<hi>, be, with <to>, on and on, and <ta>, now, written as one word: has by now come to be, has reached a number or a point in time) (j:hi/to/ta) (r:zd:12941/zd:14869/zd:12715) (q:draft)
hituan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be necessarily/be really) (d:<hi>, be, and the particle <tuan> written as one word, before a negative: {hituan lo hi} is it is not necessarily so, it does not follow that) (j:hi/tuan) (r:zd:12507/zd:26838) (q:draft)
hituanlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:is not necessarily/is not for all that) (d:<hi>, <tuan> and <lo> written as one word: it is not so in spite of what might be expected, it does not follow that it is) (j:hi/tuan/lo) (r:zd:20850/zd:23198/zd:12460) (q:draft)
hivai = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/media) (w:this matter/this affair) (d:<hih>, this, and <vai>, matter, written as one word without the final h of <hih>, also written <hihvai>: the matter just spoken of) (j:hih/vai) (r:zd:24495/zd:11623) (q:draft)
hive = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be indeed) (d:<hi> and <ve> written as one word: it is so indeed, an emphatic statement, usually followed by a person ending such as <hang>, <ungh> or <maw>) (j:hi/ve) (r:zd:21590/zd:16457) (q:draft, low confidence)
hiveh = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:<hi> with the exclamatory <veh> written as one word, at the end of a sentence and mostly followed by <aw> or <e>: it surely is, it must be, said with feeling or as a supposition) (j:hi/veh) (r:ts:2963/zd:14498) (q:draft, low confidence)
hiveh aw = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:<hiveh>, it surely is, and the exclamatory <aw>: ends a sentence that the speaker utters with feeling, as an exclamation or a supposition, it really is, it must be, you know) (r:zd:24327/ts:2963) (q:draft, low confidence)
hiven = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:after all/indeed) (d:<hi>, be, with the sentence-final <ven>, written as one word: ends a statement that the speaker treats as plain or as known to the hearer, it is so after all, you see) (j:hi/ven) (r:zd:15883/zd:25686/ts:3446) (q:draft, low confidence)
hiveng = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:<hi>, <ve> and <ing> written as one word: sentence ending of the first person singular that stresses the statement, I am indeed, I do; {ding hiveng} is I surely will) (j:hi/ve/ing) (r:zd:24132/zd:12998/zd:25562) (q:draft)
hizahta = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:so much/to this extent/so greatly) (d:<hizah>, this much, with the ending <ta>, compare <zahta>: to such an extent as this; usually followed by <a>, <aa> or <in>) (b:hizah) (r:zd:9445/zd:21066/zd:19295) (q:draft)
hizel = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be again/keep being) (d:<hi> and <zel> written as one word at the end of a statement: it is so again, it is always so) (j:hi/zel) (r:zd:21221/zd:15883) (q:draft, low confidence)
hizen = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:really be/simply be) (d:<hi>, be, and the emphatic <zen> written as one word: it really is so, it is simply that) (j:hi/zen) (r:zd:12998/zd:11409) (q:draft)
hizenzen = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:really be/be exactly) (d:<hi> and <zenzen> written as one word: really be so; mostly with <lo>, as in {hizenzen lo hi}, it is not really so, not exactly, and with <leh>, if it should really be) (j:hi/zenzen) (r:zd:11019/zd:24220/zd:15274) (q:draft)
hizenzenlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not really be/not necessarily be) (d:<hi>, <zenzen> and <lo> written as one word: is not really so, is not necessarily the case) (j:hi/zenzen/lo) (r:zd:11587/zd:12938) (q:draft)
hiziau = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:simply be/just be) (d:<hi>, be, and <ziau> written as one word before the final <hi>: it is simply so, it is just that and nothing more) (j:hi/ziau) (r:zd:17313/zd:19774/zd:20905) (q:draft)
hizong = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:even if/whether/however) (d:<hi>, be, and <zong>, also, written as one word: even if it is, whether it is; {a hizong} at the start of a sentence is however, even so) (j:hi/zong) (r:zd:23972/zd:20800) (q:draft)
hizongin = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:but/however/whether) (d:<hi>, be, and <zongin>, although, written as one word after <a>: {a hizongin} at the head of a sentence is but or however, after <bangbang> it is whatever the case, and after each of several nouns it is whether this or that) (j:hi/zongin) (r:zd:21869/zd:20142/zd:22584) (q:draft)
Hlaingthaya = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel) (w:Hlaingthaya/Hlaing Tharyar) (d:township in the west of Yangon, Myanmar) (r:zd:17917) (q:draft)
Hlotdaw = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:parliament/legislature/assembly) (d:a house of parliament of Myanmar or of one of its states, as in {Chin State Hlotdaw}) (o:Burmese, hluttaw) (r:zd:22586) (q:draft)
Hlutdaw = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:parliament/assembly/legislature) (d:the parliament of Myanmar or of one of its states, as in {State Hlutdaw}) (o:Burmese, hluttaw) (r:zd:10861/zd:24736) (q:draft)
Hluttaw = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:parliament/legislature) (d:the parliament of Myanmar or of one of its states and regions; {Pyithu Hluttaw} is the lower house and {Amyotha Hluttaw} the upper house) (o:Burmese) (r:zd:15565/zd:15743) (q:draft)
Hmar = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (f:social) (w:Hmar) (d:a people related to the Zomi and Mizo, living in Mizoram, Manipur and Assam in India) (r:zd:14867) (q:draft)
hoih = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:good/fine) (d:good in quality or in character, also fine or beautiful; {hoih lo} is not good) (s:pha) (a:gilo/hoihlo/siat) (r:25.3.25)
hoih kisa = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:think it good/find it best/be in favour) (d:<hoih>, good, and <kisa>, be felt or considered: it is thought good, used to give an opinion or a recommendation; the thing judged stands before it, often a clause ending in <ding>, it is thought good to do so; of a person it is think oneself good) (r:zd:25212/zd:11076) (q:draft)
hoihding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:would be good/will be good) (d:<hoih>, good, and <ding> written as one word: it will or would be good, often after a clause with <leh> or <leng>, if) (j:hoih/ding) (r:zd:12715/zd:21869/zd:25470) (q:draft)
hoihhetlo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/health) (w:not good at all/very bad) (d:<hoih> and <hetlo> written as one word: not good at all) (j:hoih/hetlo) (r:zd:20764/zd:16346/zd:14879) (q:draft)
hoihhi = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:is good/it is good) (d:<hoih>, good, and <hi.2> written as one word at the end of a sentence: is good; after a verb with <ding> it is good to do so) (j:hoih/hi) (r:zd:11472/zd:17651/zd:16321) (q:draft)
hoihlai = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:still good/still sound) (d:<hoih>, good, and <lai>, here in its sense of still, written as one word: still good, still in good condition) (j:hoih/lai) (r:zd:12998/zd:16754) (q:draft)
hoihlo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:bad/not good) (d:<hoih>, good, with the negative <lo>, written as one word: not good, bad) (s:gilo/siat) (a:hoih) (b:hoih) (q:draft)
hoihloh = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:not good/bad) (d:<hoih>, good, with the negative <loh> written as one word, the form used before endings such as <na>, <man> and <hangin>; {a hoihloh na} is the bad side of something) (s:hoihlo) (j:hoih/loh) (r:zd:12998/zd:22444) (q:draft)
hoihmahmah = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:very good/excellent) (d:<hoih>, good, with <mahmah>, very, written as one word) (j:hoih/mahmah) (r:zd:22451/zd:25909) (q:draft)
Hokkaido = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:travel) (w:Hokkaido) (d:the northernmost of the main islands of Japan, and the region of that name) (r:zd:15781/zd:17551) (q:draft)
holiday = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time/work) (w:holiday/day off) (d:a day or time free from work, a public holiday or a holiday trip; English word used in Zolai sentences) (o:English) (r:zd:23400/zd:16204) (q:draft, low confidence)
holim = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:converse/chat/talk together) (d:talk with someone in a friendly, unhurried way; the person talked with is marked by <tawh>, and {ki holim} is talk with one another) (s:kiho) (r:zd:25562/zd:20334/zd:17060) (q:draft)
holimna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/media) (w:conversation/talk/discussion/chat) (d:a talking together, a conversation or discussion, in news also an interview with someone; {holimna nei} is hold a talk; built on <ho>, talk) (r:zd:20587/zd:22680/ts:5105) (q:draft)
Hollywood = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:media) (w:Hollywood) (d:district of Los Angeles in the United States, and the American film industry that has its home there) (r:zd:11796/zd:10722) (q:draft)
Homalin = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel/politics) (w:Homalin) (d:town and township in Sagaing Region, Myanmar) (r:ts:2942/ts:5326) (q:draft)
hon = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/home) (w:open) (d:open a door, a gate, a book or the eyes; before <sak> it is written with an apostrophe) (a:khaksak/kalh) (r:20.18.16) (q:draft)
hon hun = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/time) (w:opening hours/opening time) (d:<hon>, open, and <hun>, time: the hours when an office, clinic or school is open, or the time when it opens; the place stands before it, as in {zum hon hun}, office hours) (r:zd:20418/zd:24234) (q:draft)
Honda = (i:1) (t:name) (f:travel) (w:Honda) (d:a Japanese make of car and motorcycle) (o:Japanese) (r:zd:17100/zd:15568) (q:draft)
hong nusiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:family/social) (w:pass away/die/leave us) (d:<hong>, towards us, and <nusiat>, a form of <nusia>, leave behind: said of a relative or respected person who has died, he or she has left us; this form stands before words such as <laitakin>, <teh>, <dan> and <dahpihna>) (r:zd:25178/zd:21925) (q:draft)
hong nusiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/family) (w:passing/death/decease) (d:<hong>, toward us, and <nusiatna>, leaving behind: his or her leaving us, a gentle word for the death of a person in notices of mourning and condolence; the name or kin term of the dead stands before it and <hangin>, because of, usually after it) (r:zd:22938/zd:21550) (q:draft)
hong sihsan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/family) (w:pass away/leave us in death) (d:the prefix <hong>, toward us, and <sihsan>, die leaving behind: to die and leave us; the usual wording of a death notice, and said of a relative who has died) (r:zd:10672/zd:21233) (q:draft)
hong zatsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:religion) (w:use us/use you) (d:<hong>, towards us or you, and <zatsak>, put to use: said of God using a person in his service; in the blessing {Topa'n hong zatsak semsem tahen}, may the Lord use you more and more) (r:zd:23155/zd:15951) (q:draft)
hongbawl = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:make/do) (d:<hong> and <bawl> written as one word: make or do, with the action directed toward the speaker or the person addressed, as when God made us) (j:hong/bawl) (r:zd:20202/zd:17933/zd:21922) (q:draft)
hongbei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:come to an end/pass/run out) (d:<hong> and <bei> written as one word: come to an end, pass away, be used up) (j:hong/bei) (r:zd:15956/zd:23035/zd:24593) (q:draft)
hongci = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:say to me/tell us) (d:<hong>, toward the speaker, and <ci>, say, written as one word after the words quoted: said to me or to us) (j:hong/ci) (r:zd:13190/zd:24029/zd:15662) (q:draft)
hongciah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:come home/come back/return) (d:<hong>, toward the speaker, and <ciah>, go home, written as one word: come back home) (j:hong/ciah) (r:zd:21389/zd:18050/zd:13350) (q:draft)
hongcih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:say to me/say to us/tell) (d:<hong> and <cih> written as one word: what someone says to the speaker, used before words such as <ciangin>) (j:hong/cih) (r:zd:17187/zd:10874/zd:12329) (q:draft)
hongdawn = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/everyday) (w:come to meet/come to fetch/welcome) (d:<hong> and <dawn>, meet, written as one word: come to meet or welcome someone, come to fetch someone) (j:hong/dawn) (r:zd:18152/zd:10973) (q:draft)
hongdawn = (i:2) (t:v) (f:food) (w:come to drink) (d:<hong> and <dawn>, drink, written as one word: come and drink) (j:hong/dawn) (r:zd:25915) (q:draft, low confidence)
honggen = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:tell/say to) (d:<hong> and <gen> written as one word: tell or say something to the speaker or to us; in a request, tell me) (j:hong/gen) (r:zd:23191/zd:16924/zd:12564) (q:draft)
honghawh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/travel) (w:come to visit/visit) (d:<hong> and <hawh>, visit, written as one word: come to see the speaker or the place spoken of) (j:hong/hawh) (r:zd:18071/zd:11401) (q:draft)
honghilh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/education) (w:teach us/show us/tell us) (d:<hong> and <hilh> written as one word: teach, show or tell something to the speaker or to us) (j:hong/hilh) (r:zd:22644/zd:25275/zd:21869) (q:draft)
honghuh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:help me/help us/help you) (d:<hong>, the marker of an action toward the speaker or the one spoken to, and <huh>, help, written as one word; {honghuh un} is the cry help us) (j:hong/huh) (r:zd:15243/zd:13022/zd:24604) (q:draft)
hongit = (i:1) (t:v) (f:family/religion) (w:love you/love me/love us) (d:<hong>, marking an action toward the speaker or the one spoken to, and <it>, love, written as one word: loves you, me or us; {hongit ing} is I love you) (j:hong/it) (r:zd:21011/zd:21355/zd:19518) (q:draft)
hongkem = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/religion) (w:look after/protect/keep) (d:<hong> and <kem> written as one word: look after or protect us or me) (j:hong/kem) (r:zd:15422/zd:22287/ts:3366) (q:draft)
hongkha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/social) (w:see off/escort/send on the way) (d:<hong>, toward the speaker, with <kha>, here send off, written as one word: see travellers off, accompany or send them on their way; said also of God bringing someone safely along) (j:hong/kha) (r:zd:13181/zd:11110/zd:13262) (q:draft)
hongkhak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:send/send here) (d:<hong>, toward the speaker, and <khak>, send, written as one word: send a letter, a picture or money to me or to us) (j:hong/khak) (r:zd:17120/zd:20896) (q:draft)
hongkhak = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:block/hold back/hinder) (d:<hong> and <khak>, shut, written as one word: shut in, block or hold back a person) (j:hong/khak) (r:zd:21989/zd:23784) (q:draft, low confidence)
hongkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/home) (w:open/open up/lay open) (d:<hon>, open, with <khia>, out: open a door or a closed thing, and bring a hidden matter into the open) (r:zd:18020/zd:24414) (q:draft)
hongkhia = (i:2) (t:v) (f:religion) (w:rescue/deliver) (d:<hon>, save, with <khia>, out: bring someone out of danger or death) (r:zd:9434) (q:draft, low confidence)
hongki = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:<hong> and the verb prefix <ki> written as one word and apart from the verb that follows: {hongki zasak} is it was reported to us, {hongki phallo} is we are not allowed) (j:hong/ki) (r:zd:15602/zd:20300/zd:15118) (q:draft)
hongkibawl = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:be made/be lodged) (d:<hong> and <kibawl> written as one word: has been made, said in news of a police report or a complaint that has been lodged) (j:hong/kibawl) (r:zd:15884/zd:19958) (q:draft)
hongkik = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:reopen/open again) (d:<hong>, here the form of <hon>, open, with <kik>, again, written as one word: open again a road, an office or a place that was closed; {ki hongkik} is be reopened) (j:hon/kik) (r:zd:11936/zd:17622/zd:25589) (q:draft)
hongkipan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:begin/start) (d:<hong> and <kipan> written as one word: something begins, or someone begins to do something) (j:hong/kipan) (r:zd:15775/zd:16257) (q:draft)
hongkipia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be given to us/be given to me) (d:<hong>, toward the speaker, and <kipia>, be given, written as one word: be given to me, to us or to you) (j:hong/kipia) (r:zd:12674/zd:16349/zd:14885) (q:draft)
hongkipuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:be brought/be sent/be taken) (d:<hong> and <kipuak> written as one word: be carried or sent to the place spoken of, as the injured to a hospital) (j:hong/kipuak) (r:zd:14697/zd:16045/zd:17538) (q:draft)
hongkisam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/it) (w:be called/receive a call) (d:<hong> toward the speaker and <kisam> be called, written as one word: a call came in, we were called or summoned) (j:hong/kisam) (r:zd:17432/zd:13213/zd:12515) (q:draft)
Hongkong = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city/land) (f:travel/politics) (w:Hong Kong) (d:city and territory on the south coast of China) (r:zd:17546/zd:10919) (q:draft)
hongla = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:take/take up) (d:<hong> written as one word with <la>, take, the base form of <lak>: take, said of something that comes toward the speaker or the matter in hand; {pan hongla} is take part and {mun hongla} take a place) (j:hong/la) (r:zd:11228/zd:23992/zd:25616) (q:draft)
honglak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/education) (w:show/point out/reveal) (d:<hong> and <lak>, show, written as one word: shows to us or to you; {lam honglak} is show the way) (j:hong/lak) (r:zd:23554/zd:23843/zd:17120) (q:draft)
honglut = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:come in/enter/arrive in) (d:<hong> and <lut> written as one word: enter toward the speaker or the place spoken of) (j:hong/lut) (r:zd:16617/zd:12794/zd:15084) (q:draft)
hongmu = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:see us/see me/look upon) (d:<hong> and <mu> written as one word: see, with the action directed toward the speaker, see us or me; {hongmu khia} is find out) (j:hong/mu) (r:zd:14709/zd:15362) (q:draft)
hongna = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday/social) (d:<hong>, marking an action toward the speaker, and the preverbal particle <na>, written as one word before a verb, mostly in requests: {hongna maisak in} is please forgive me, {hongna telsiam un} is please understand us) (j:hong/na) (r:zd:15651/zd:24545) (q:draft, low confidence)
hongnei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:have/hold/give) (d:<hong> and <nei> written as one word: have or hold toward the speaker or the public, as a talk, a meeting or a feeling) (j:hong/nei) (r:zd:11447/zd:12196/zd:16508) (q:draft)
hongneih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/religion) (w:hold/have/come to have) (d:<hong> and <neih> written as one word: hold a prayer or a meeting for or with the speaker's side, as in {thungetna hongneih pih}, or come to have something) (j:hong/neih) (r:zd:15622/zd:14587) (q:draft)
hongngah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:get/receive/obtain) (d:<hong> and <ngah> written as one word: come to receive or win something, with the action seen as coming toward the speaker or his people) (j:hong/ngah) (r:zd:15874/zd:8668) (q:draft)
hongnusia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/family) (w:pass away/leave us) (d:<hong> and <nusia> written as one word: has left us, the usual wording of a death notice; {in hongnusia} after a name is has passed away) (j:hong/nusia) (r:zd:17838/zd:12557) (q:draft)
hongom = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:come to be/arise/appear/be present) (d:<hong> and <om> written as one word: come into being, arise, come to be there; of people, come and be present) (j:hong/om) (r:zd:15941/zd:19427/zd:14579) (q:draft)
hongpai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:come) (d:<hong>, toward the speaker, and <pai>, go, written as one word: come, come here) (j:hong/pai) (r:zd:17325/zd:11953/zd:14899) (q:draft)
hongpaiding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:will come) (d:<hong>, <pai>, come, and <ding>, will, written as one word: will come, the one who is to come) (j:hong/pai/ding) (r:zd:14954/zd:20289/zd:22416) (q:draft)
hongpia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/religion) (w:give us/give me/grant) (d:<hong> and <pia> written as one word: give to the speaker or to the people addressed, give us, give you; common in blessings, as in <thupha hongpia>, bless us) (j:hong/pia) (r:zd:17022/zd:21085/zd:20035) (q:draft)
hongpiak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/religion) (w:give/gave/given) (d:<hong> and <piak> written as one word: give to the speaker or to us; the form used before a noun, as in {Pasian hongpiak thupha}, the blessing God has given us) (j:hong/piak) (r:zd:19593/zd:16498/zd:11508) (q:draft)
hongpiaksak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:religion/everyday) (w:grant/give to us/bestow) (d:<hong>, toward the speaker, and <piaksak> written as one word: give or grant to us or to one of ours; common in blessings, as in {thupha hongpiaksak}) (j:hong/piaksak) (r:zd:11011/zd:23035/zd:13066) (q:draft)
hongpian = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:come into being/arise/come about) (d:<hong> and <pian> written as one word: come into existence, arise or happen) (j:hong/pian) (r:zd:24657/zd:15695/zd:22293) (q:draft)
hongpiang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:happen/come about/arise) (d:<hong> and <piang> written as one word: come into being, happen or appear among those spoken of; {hongpiang khia} is come forth) (j:hong/piang) (r:zd:19683/zd:21876/zd:23860) (q:draft)
hongpuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:bring here/deliver to us/send here) (d:<hong> and <puak> written as one word: bring or send something or someone to the speaker or to the place spoken of) (j:hong/puak) (r:zd:16073/zd:13078/zd:16455) (q:draft)
hongsa = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:consider/regard as/find) (d:<hong>, toward the speaker or hearer, and <sa>, here feel or consider, written as one word after a describing word: people find me, us or you so, as in {lamdang hongsa}, be surprised at us) (j:hong/sa) (r:zd:14606/zd:16893) (q:draft)
hongsam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:call/invite) (d:<hong>, toward the speaker, and <sam>, call, written as one word: call or invite me or us; also call us by a name) (j:hong/sam) (r:zd:22350/zd:24029) (q:draft)
hongsawl = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/religion) (w:send/command) (d:<hong> and <sawl> written as one word: send here or send to us, and tell us to do something) (j:hong/sawl) (r:zd:19523/zd:25225/zd:17478) (q:draft)
hongsem = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:work/do/come to work) (d:<hong> and <sem> written as one word: do work toward or for the speaker or the person spoken to, set to work) (j:hong/sem) (r:zd:21340/zd:20871/zd:10951) (q:draft)
hongsep = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/politics) (w:take office/serve as/come to do) (d:<hong> and <sep> written as one word: come to do a work or hold a post, as in {President hongsep ciangin}, when he became President) (j:hong/sep) (r:zd:20850/zd:19801) (q:draft)
hongsuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:become/turn out/come to be) (d:<hong> and <suak> written as one word: become or come to be, said of what comes about for the speaker or the people spoken of, also arise or come out; with <sak>, cause to become) (j:hong/suak) (r:zd:21837/zd:12196/zd:24016) (q:draft)
hongtam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:become many/increase/grow in number) (d:<hong> and <tam>, many, written as one word: become many or more, increase) (j:hong/tam) (r:zd:20531/zd:11510/zd:12051) (q:draft)
hongtan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:ransom me/redeem us/bail out) (d:<hong>, towards the speaker, and <tan>, redeem, written as one word: pay to get me or us released) (j:hong/tan) (r:zd:19320) (q:draft)
hongtan = (i:2) (t:v) (f:nature/religion) (w:shine on us/dawn) (d:<hong>, towards the speaker, with <tan>, here shine, which the lexicon writes <taang>: light shines on us or breaks) (j:hong/tan) (r:zd:10793/zd:20670) (q:draft, low confidence)
hongthei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:know/come to know) (d:<hong> and <thei> written as one word: know or come to know, said toward the speaker or of something learned; {nang pen hongthei lo} is they do not know you) (j:hong/thei) (r:zd:19983/zd:24502) (q:draft)
hongthei = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/home) (w:can be opened/be able to open) (d:<hong>, here open, a form of <hon>, with <thei>, able: can open or can be opened, said of a lock, a door or a safe) (j:hong/thei) (r:zd:22862/zd:19754) (q:draft, low confidence)
hongtun = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:arrive/come/reach) (d:<hong> and <tun> written as one word: arrive here or come to the people spoken of, said of persons, times and events; the form used before <ding>, <ciangin>, <ma> and other endings) (j:hong/tun) (r:zd:22479/zd:24955/zd:23943) (q:draft)
hongtung = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:arrive/come/reach here) (d:<hong> and <tung> written as one word: arrive here, come to where the speaker is; also of a feeling or a blessing that comes upon someone) (j:hong/tung) (r:zd:21389/zd:15103/zd:12168) (q:draft)
hongtungding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:time) (w:will come/coming/upcoming) (d:<hong>, <tung> and <ding.1> written as one word: will arrive; before a date or an event, the coming or next one) (j:hong/tung/ding) (r:zd:21334/zd:22377/zd:11209) (q:draft)
hongzasak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/media) (w:inform us/let us know/report to) (d:<hong>, towards the speaker, and <zasak>, inform, written as one word: let us or me know, report to us; {hongzasak un} is please inform us) (j:hong/zasak) (r:zd:21328/zd:13020/zd:21248) (q:draft)
hongzin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:visit/come on a visit) (d:<hong>, toward the speaker, and <zin>, travel, written as one word: come here on a journey or visit) (j:hong/zin) (r:zd:11401/zd:16488/zd:12919) (q:draft)
hongzui = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:follow/come along with) (d:<hong>, toward the speaker or us, and <zui>, follow, written as one word: follow me or us, come after) (j:hong/zui) (r:zd:20997/zd:24593) (q:draft)
honkhatin = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/social) (w:a group of) (d:<honkhat> and <in> written as one word, after a noun: a group of them, as the ones who do the action) (j:honkhat/in) (r:zd:17974/zd:15777/zd:11265) (q:draft)
honkhattawh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:with a number of/with a quantity of) (d:<honkhat>, a group or lot, and <tawh>, with, written as one word after a noun: together with a number or quantity of the thing named) (j:honkhat/tawh) (r:zd:17069/zd:16729) (q:draft)
honkhatzong = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:a number also/some as well) (d:<honkhat> and <zong> written as one word, after a noun: a number of them also, a quantity of it as well) (j:honkhat/zong) (r:zd:19318/zd:19289) (q:draft)
honkhiathei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:can rescue/be able to save) (d:<honkhia>, rescue, and <thei>, be able, written as one word; with <ki> before it, could be rescued) (j:honkhia/thei) (r:zd:20387/zd:24276) (q:draft)
honpawi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:opening ceremony/inauguration) (d:<hon>, open, with <pawi>, festival: the ceremony at which a building, a school, a shop or an event is opened) (r:zd:15617/zd:14897/zd:12048) (q:draft)
honpikhat = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:a great many/a large amount of/a mass of) (d:<honpi> and <khat> written as one word, placed after a noun: a great quantity or number of it) (j:honpi/khat) (r:zd:11841/zd:17790) (q:draft)
hopihna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/everyday) (w:greeting/salutation) (d:words spoken to greet someone) (b:hopih) (q:draft)
hormone = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/body) (w:hormone) (o:English) (r:zd:22187/zd:20640/zd:20448) (q:draft)
Horn = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:horn/car horn) (d:the horn of a car, lorry or train, sounded as a warning; {horn tum} is sound the horn) (o:English) (r:zd:21015/zd:18303/zd:22686) (q:draft)
Hospital = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health) (w:hospital) (d:a hospital, in the articles mostly after the name of one; the Zolai word used beside it is <zato>) (o:English) (r:zd:16434/zd:19745/zd:12132) (q:draft)
Hospitals = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health) (w:hospital) (d:the English plural used as a Zolai noun for hospitals, often followed by <te> or <tuamtuam>) (o:English) (r:zd:11899/zd:11265) (q:draft)
host = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/work) (w:host/presenter) (d:the person who presents a television programme, also the one who receives guests at an event or a restaurant) (o:English) (r:zd:25603/zd:12311) (q:draft, low confidence)
Hostage = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/media) (w:hostage) (d:a person held captive to force a demand; {Hostage in man} is take as a hostage) (o:English) (r:zd:12860/zd:11642/zd:14848) (q:draft)
Hostel = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/education) (w:hostel/dormitory) (d:a house where students or workers lodge) (o:English) (r:zd:18234/zd:15255/zd:15461) (q:draft)
Hotel = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/work) (w:hotel) (d:a building where travellers pay to stay, often after its name) (o:English) (r:zd:15296/zd:12168/zd:12487) (q:draft)
hotkhiattheih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be able to rescue/can be saved) (d:<hotkhiat>, rescue, and <theih>, be able, written as one word; {hotkhiattheih nadingin} is in order to be able to rescue) (j:hotkhiat/theih) (r:zd:17265/zd:15928) (q:draft)
hotline = (i:1) (t:n) (f:it/social) (w:hotline/helpline) (d:a telephone number of an organisation that can be called for urgent help or information) (o:English) (r:zd:20418/zd:25415) (q:draft)
Hotpot = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food) (w:hotpot) (d:a meal cooked at the table in a pot of boiling broth; {hotpot ansai} is a hotpot restaurant) (o:English) (r:zd:16817/zd:15425) (q:draft)
hotspot = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/it/media) (w:hotspot) (d:a place where a disease or crime is concentrated; with Wifi, a place with wireless internet access) (o:English) (r:zd:24413/zd:15445) (q:draft)
Hougang = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel) (w:Hougang) (d:residential town in the north-east of Singapore, with a station of the same name) (r:zd:12031/zd:20514) (q:draft)
Houston = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel) (w:Houston) (d:city in the state of Texas in the United States, where a Zomi community lives) (r:zd:21042) (q:draft)
Hpakant = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel/work) (w:Hpakant) (d:a town and township in Kachin State, Myanmar, known for its jade mines) (r:zd:17428/zd:19543) (q:draft)
Htee = (i:1) (t:name) (f:politics) (w:Pyu Saw Htee) (d:last word of the Burmese name Pyu Saw Htee, the militia groups that fight on the side of the Myanmar military; also found in Burmese place names) (o:Burmese) (r:zd:26620/ts:1101) (q:draft)
hua = (i:1) (t:det) (f:everyday) (w:that/yonder/that over there) (d:points to something far from both speaker and hearer; {hua lai-ah} and {hua lamah} mean over there, in contrast with <hih>, this) (s:hia) (r:19.104.26) (q:draft)
huahna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/social) (j:hauhna) (r:zd:20264/zd:20443) (q:draft, low confidence)
huaihi = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:the suffix <huai>, worthy of, and the sentence ending <hi> written as one word after a verb: it is worth doing, one ought to do it, as {kidop huaihi}, one should be careful) (j:huai/hi) (r:zd:19676/zd:18011/zd:20899) (q:draft)
huailo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:not worth/not advisable/not fit to) (d:the suffix <huai>, worthy of, with the negative <lo>, written as one word after a verb: not worth doing, not to be done, as {pai huailo}, not advisable to go, and {deih huailo}, not desirable) (j:huai/lo) (r:zd:23394/zd:12867) (q:draft)
huailua = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:very much worth/exceedingly) (d:<huai> and <lua> written as one word after a verb: very much worth doing, or causing that feeling to a great degree, as in {lau huailua}, very much to be feared) (j:huai/lua) (r:zd:21271/zd:22371/zd:14947) (q:draft)
huaisia = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:health/nature/media) (w:serious/severe/critical/grave) (d:of an injury, a fire, a flood or an accident: very bad, severe; of an injured person, in a serious condition; often with <mahmah> or <phadiak>) (r:zd:14638/zd:16952/zd:16367) (q:draft)
huaisialua = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:nature/media) (w:too fierce/very severe) (d:<huaisia>, severe, and <lua>, too much, written as one word: very fierce, out of control, in the articles always of a fire; mostly followed by <mahmah>) (j:huaisia/lua) (r:zd:20428/zd:14692/zd:11236) (q:draft)
huaisiam = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:social) (w:caring/protective/good at holding people together) (d:good at gathering people in and looking after them, said of a leader who cares for all and keeps them together; frequent in songs; the second part is <siam>, skilled) (r:zd:24199/zd:24313) (q:draft, low confidence)
huaitak = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:<huai>, causing a feeling, with <tak>, which makes an adverb, written as one word after a verb of feeling: in a way that causes it; {khasiat huaitak in} is sadly, {lungkim huaitak in} contentedly, {cikziat huaitak in} disgustingly) (j:huai/tak) (r:zd:15679/zd:19174) (q:draft)
hual = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature) (w:wave) (d:a wave of water, usually as {tui hual}; also a wave of change or of a sickness that sweeps over a land) (s:tuihual) (r:zd:24067/ts:4827) (q:draft)
Hualngo = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (f:social) (w:Hualngo) (d:a people of the Falam area of Chin State who are related to the Lusei or Mizo, and the area where they live) (r:zd:25097/zd:15525) (q:draft)
hualpi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature/social) (w:wave/great wave/billow) (d:<hual>, wave, with <pi>, great: a great wave, as in <tuihual>; in articles mostly a wave of events, of change or of sickness, as {pulnatna hualpi}, a wave of epidemic) (r:zd:25242/zd:21974) (q:draft)
huam sungah = (i:1) (t:prep) (f:politics/travel) (w:within the area of/in the territory of) (d:<huam>, take in or cover, and <sungah>, inside: placed after the name of a town, township or other unit, inside the area that it covers) (r:zd:24170/zd:16728) (q:draft)
huamkim = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/social) (w:comprehensive/all-inclusive/inclusive) (d:<huam>, include, with <kim>, all: taking in everyone or everything, covering the whole) (b:huam) (r:zd:20410/zd:24392) (q:draft)
huampi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/education) (w:whole/overall view/generality) (d:the whole of a matter taken together, not its details; mostly as {a huampi in}, on the whole, in general, and {a huampi a etna}, an overview) (r:zd:23479/zd:24039/zd:21706) (q:draft)
huamsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/it) (w:make include/extend to/cover) (d:<huam>, take in, with the causative <sak>: make something take in or cover an area or a group, count as included) (j:huam/sak) (r:zd:20093/ts:12519) (q:draft)
huan = (i:3) (t:v) (f:everyday/food) (w:cook) (r:zai:cook) (q:draft)
huatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/everyday) (w:hatred/hate/loathing) (d:<huat>, hate, with the noun suffix <na>: hatred, strong dislike of a person or people) (s:muhdahna) (b:huat) (r:zd:12306/zd:8667) (q:draft)
Huawei = (i:1) (t:name) (f:it/work) (w:Huawei) (d:Chinese company that makes phones and telecommunication equipment) (r:zd:14531) (q:draft)
Hubei = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:travel/politics) (w:Hubei) (d:province in central China; Wuhan is its capital) (r:zd:23822/zd:17949) (q:draft)
huh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:help) (d:do something for someone so that things go better for them; {hong huh in} is the cry help me) (s:panpih) (a:nawngkaisak) (r:19.118.13)
huhding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:will help/to help) (d:<huh>, help, and <ding>, will, written as one word: will help, in order to help; also the one who will help or the help to be given) (j:huh/ding) (r:zd:20066/zd:25928/zd:8668) (q:draft)
huhna sum = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/social) (w:aid money/relief fund/donation/financial aid) (d:<huhna>, help, and <sum>, money: money given or collected to help people in need, and aid paid by a government or an organization) (r:zd:22334/zd:20513/zd:24236) (q:draft)
huhnading = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:social) (w:in order to help/for helping) (d:<huh> help and <nading> for, written as one word: for the help or relief of the people named before it) (j:huh/nading) (r:zd:15907/zd:14975/zd:15116) (q:draft)
huih siangtho = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature/health) (w:fresh air/clean air) (d:<huih>, air, and <siangtho>, here clean and pure, not holy: fresh, unpolluted air, also said of oxygen; often with the verb <diik>, breathe in) (r:zd:11571/zd:20778/zd:23729) (q:draft)
huihdik = (i:1) (t:v) (f:body/health) (w:breathe/inhale/take a breath) (d:<huih>, air, with a short spelling of <diik>, draw in: breathe; also as a noun, breathing, as in {huihdik haksa}, difficulty in breathing) (s:naak) (r:zd:23848/zd:21807/zd:21616) (q:draft)
huihdikna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/body) (w:breathing/respiration) (d:{huih dik}, breathe in air, with the noun ending <na>: breathing; {huihdikna lampi} is the airway) (r:zd:20195/zd:21796) (q:draft)
huihkhi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature) (w:breeze/wind/air) (d:the moving air, a breeze; also used in songs and as a figure, as in {kikhelna huihkhi}, the wind of change) (s:huih) (r:zd:22784/zd:11494) (q:draft)
huihnun = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature/social) (w:wind/blowing of the wind) (d:<huih>, wind, and <nun>, blow, written as one word: the blowing of the wind; <huihnun zia>, the way the wind blows, is the climate or trend of a country or of its politics) (j:huih/nun) (r:zd:24677/zd:23538) (q:draft)
huihnun zia = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:climate/prevailing conditions/trend) (d:<huihnun>, the blowing of the wind, and <zia>, manner: the way the wind blows, that is the conditions and mood prevailing in a country or in its politics; also written {huih nun zia}) (r:zd:23538/zd:24677) (q:draft)
huihpi guahpi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature) (w:storm/rainstorm/cyclone) (d:<huihpi>, strong wind, and <guahpi>, heavy rain: a pair that names one storm of wind and rain; in news also a cyclone or typhoon) (r:zd:12811/zd:11725) (q:draft)
Hulu = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel) (w:Hulu) (d:Malay word for the upper part of a river, the first part of the names of districts in Malaysia such as Hulu Selangor, Hulu Terengganu and Hulu Langat) (o:Malay) (r:zd:15356/zd:11162) (q:draft)
humbit = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:protect/defend/shield/guard) (d:<hum>, cover or shield, with <bit>, safe: keep someone or something safe from danger or attack) (s:dal/huu) (r:zd:10952/zd:11072) (q:draft)
humbitna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/social) (w:protection/safeguarding/defence) (d:the act of shielding someone or something so that it is safe, from <hum> and <bitna>) (r:zd:22620/zd:10683/zd:20349) (q:draft)
humop = (i:1) (t:v) (f:religion) (w:inspire/be inspired) (d:of God or the Holy Spirit and the Scriptures: inspire, breathe out; {Pasian humop} is inspired by God, and with {-na} it is inspiration) (r:zd:24064/zd:22470) (q:draft)
hun = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:time/period/season) (d:a point or stretch of time; {tua hun lai takin} means at that time, and {hun sung} means during a period)
hun awng = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time/everyday) (w:free time/spare time/leisure) (d:<hun>, time, and <awng>, here in the sense be empty or vacant: time that is not taken up by work, free time; mostly with <ngah>, get, or <nei>, have, {hun awng ngah} is to get free time) (r:zd:20060/zd:17177/ts:3375) (q:draft)
hun nunung = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion/time) (w:last days/end times/last time) (d:<hun>, time, and <nunung>, last: the last time; in church writing the end times before the return of Christ, often with <ah>, in; after the name of a person it means the last days of that person) (r:zd:9434/zd:19679) (q:draft)
hunbawl = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion/social) (w:service/ceremony/programme) (d:<hun>, time, and <bawl>, make, written as one word: a service or programme that is held, as in {sihvui hunbawl}, a funeral service; also the holding of it) (j:hun/bawl) (r:zd:15846/zd:22388/zd:11712) (q:draft)
hunbawl = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:around/about the time of) (d:after a length of time, <hun> with <bawl>, about: around that time, roughly; {kum 8 hunbawl akipan} is since about eight years ago) (r:zd:14684) (q:draft, low confidence)
hunbawlna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/religion) (w:service/ceremony/programme) (d:<hun>, time, with <bawlna>, doing: a service or ceremony that is held, such as a funeral or thanksgiving service) (r:zd:11757/zd:10745) (q:draft)
hunbei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:time) (w:take time/spend time) (d:<hun>, time, with <bei>, be used up: time is spent; after a length of time it says how long something takes, and {a hunbei} is the time spent) (j:hun/bei) (r:zd:20387/zd:17862) (q:draft)
hunbit = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:work/religion) (w:full-time) (d:<hun>, time, with <bit>, full: giving the whole of the working time to one task, said mostly of church workers; {hunbit Pasian nasem} is a full-time minister and {hunbit in} is full time; the opposite is <hunlang>, part-time) (r:zd:20971/zd:21377/zd:19606) (q:draft)
hunciam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:time limit/term/deadline/set period) (d:<hun>, time, with <ciam>, set a limit: a period fixed in advance, as a prison term, a term of office or a deadline) (r:zd:19117/zd:25264/ts:1485) (q:draft)
hunciang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:when/at the time) (d:<hun>, time, and <ciang>, when, written as one word, often followed by <in>: at the time of, when; {tua hunciang in} is at that time) (j:hun/ciang) (r:zd:17595/zd:19427/zd:10973) (q:draft)
hunciangin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:at the time of/when/in times of) (d:<hun>, time, with <ciangin>, when, written as one word: when the time named before it comes) (j:hun/ciangin) (r:zd:21918/zd:23843) (q:draft)
hunding = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:time for/time to/coming time) (d:<hun> and <ding> written as one word: the time for something that is to happen, after a verb the time to do it; {mailam hunding} is the time to come) (j:hun/ding) (r:zd:12267/zd:21869/zd:20874) (q:draft)
hundong = (i:1) (t:prep) (f:time) (w:until/up to the time of) (d:<hun>, time, with <dong>, until, written as one word: until the time named before it) (j:hun/dong) (r:zd:21552/zd:17994/zd:16367) (q:draft)
hungaih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:have regard for/heed/be considerate of) (d:pay attention to a person or to what suits them and act with consideration or patience) (r:zd:20032/zd:12279) (q:draft, low confidence)
hungeelna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time/social) (w:programme/schedule/timetable) (d:<hun> and <geelna> written as one word: the planned order and times of a meeting, service or event) (j:hun/geelna) (r:zd:21127/zd:15527/zd:16052) (q:draft)
hunkhat = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:once/at one time/for a while) (d:<hun> and <khat> written as one word, a time: {hunkhat lai in} is once, at one time in the past, {hunkhat ciangin} is one day, in time, and {hunkhat sung} is for a while) (j:hun/khat) (r:zd:20071/zd:19006/zd:11251) (q:draft)
hunkhatlai = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:once/at one time/formerly) (d:<hun>, time, <khat>, one, and <lai>, the time when, written as one word: at one time in the past; {abeisa hunkhatlai in} is some time ago) (j:hun/khat/lai) (r:zd:13089/zd:13059) (q:draft)
hunla = (i:1) (t:v) (f:time/everyday) (w:take time/spend time) (d:<hun>, time, with <la>, take: take one's time, spend time with someone, or of a thing, take a length of time) (r:zd:24248/zd:12544/zd:25132) (q:draft)
hunlai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:time/period/days/era) (d:<hun> and <lai> written as one word: the time when something was so, the days of a person or a rule; {tua hunlai in} is at that time, and after a name or a clause it means in the time of, at the time when) (j:hun/lai) (r:zd:18200/zd:26097/ts:4569) (q:draft)
hunlaipawl = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:about/around the time of) (d:after a stretch of time or a date: at about that time; {abeisa kum 6 hunlaipawl} is about six years ago; from <hun>, time, <lai>, while, and <pawl>, about) (r:zd:20738/zd:11619/zd:16317) (q:draft)
hunlaipek = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:ago/back in the time of) (d:<hun> and <laipek> written as one word, after a length of time or a period: that long ago, as far back as that time; often with <akipan>, since) (j:hun/laipek) (r:zd:15417/zd:19875/zd:16849) (q:draft)
hunlaitak = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:moment/very time) (d:<hun>, time, with <laitak>, at the very time: the moment or period at which something happens; {hih hunlaitak in} is at this very time) (j:hun/laitak) (r:zd:25292/zd:21869/zd:21876) (q:draft)
hunlap = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:in time/on time/timely) (d:<hun>, time, with <lap>, catch up with: in good time, before it is too late, mostly as {a hunlap in}; {hunlap lo} is not in time) (r:zd:15105/zd:17149/zd:17586) (q:draft)
hunlian = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:exact time/very moment) (d:<hun>, time, with <lian>, here exactly, written as one word: the very time or moment at which something happens; {tulaitak hunlian} is this very moment, right now) (j:hun/lian) (r:zd:25924/zd:19109/zd:11532) (q:draft)
hunman = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:time) (w:punctual/on time) (d:<hun> and <man> written as one word: keeping the right time, on time; {hunman takin} is punctually) (j:hun/man) (r:zd:21370/zd:19676) (q:draft)
hunman = (i:2) (t:v) (f:time/religion) (w:the time ends/be over) (d:<hun> with <man>, finish, written as one word: the time of a meeting or service comes to its end, as in {hunman ciangin}, when the time was over) (j:hun/man) (r:zd:20016/zd:11110) (q:draft, low confidence)
hunnuam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/time) (w:good time/pleasant time/happy time) (d:<hun>, time, and <nuam>, pleasant, written as one word: an enjoyable time spent with others; {hunnuam zang} is have a good time) (j:hun/nuam) (r:zd:12487/zd:23367/zd:21421) (q:draft)
hunpawl = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:about the time/around) (d:<hun> and <pawl> written as one word, placed after a clock time: about that time; {9pm hunpawl in} is at around 9 pm) (j:hun/pawl) (r:zd:15521/zd:15651/zd:18947) (q:draft)
hunpen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:time) (w:the time) (d:<hun> and <pen> written as one word: the time, as the topic of the sentence; after a verb it is the time when something happened, and what follows tells when that was) (j:hun/pen) (r:zd:18947/zd:16194) (q:draft)
hunpia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:time/everyday) (w:give time/take time/devote time) (d:<hun>, time, with <pia>, give, written as one word: set aside time for a person or a task) (j:hun/pia) (r:zd:25924/zd:23977) (q:draft)
hunsawt = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:long time/long run) (d:<hun>, time, and <sawt>, long, written as one word: a long time, for long; {hunsawt ah} is in the long run) (s:hunsau) (j:hun/sawt) (r:zd:21417/zd:19327/zd:22742) (q:draft)
hunsim = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:all the time/at every moment/constantly) (d:<hun>, time, with the ending {-sim}, every, as in <nisim>, daily: at every time; often said together with <nisim> and <naisim>, every hour) (r:zd:21340/zd:17070) (q:draft)
hunsungah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:during/in the time of) (d:<hunsung> and <ah> written as one word: during the time of what is named before it) (j:hunsung/ah) (r:zd:22652) (q:draft)
hunsungin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:during/within the time/in the period) (d:<hunsung>, span of time, with the marker <in>, written as one word: during the time of something, within a period) (j:hunsung/in) (r:zd:21918/zd:14865/ts:301) (q:draft)
hunsungpen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:time) (w:the period/the duration) (d:<hunsung>, period or length of time, with the topic marker <pen>, written as one word: as for the time during which something happens) (j:hunsung/pen) (r:zd:16026/zd:17802) (q:draft)
hunsungteng = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:throughout the time/during the whole period) (d:<hun> and <sungteng> written as one word: through the whole of a period, all the time that something lasts) (j:hun/sungteng) (r:zd:20488/zd:15592/zd:21588) (q:draft)
huntawh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:time/social) (w:with the times/according to the time) (d:<hun> time and <tawh> with written as one word: {huntawh kituak} is in keeping with the times, up to date, and {huntawh kizui in} is in step with the times) (j:hun/tawh) (r:zd:21586/zd:24765/zd:20964) (q:draft)
hunteh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:at the time/when) (d:<hun>, time, with <teh>, written as one word: {tu hunteh} is at this time, nowadays, {tua hunteh} at that time, and {bang hunteh} at what time, when) (j:hun/teh) (r:zd:22479/zd:14930/zd:22860) (q:draft)
hunthak = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time/social) (w:modern times/new era/modern) (d:<hun> and <thak> written as one word: the new age, the present time; before a noun, modern) (j:hun/thak) (r:zd:22504/zd:22046/zd:23198) (q:draft)
huntomno = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:short time/short while/moment) (d:<hun> and <tomno> written as one word: a short time; {huntomno sungin} is within a short time, quickly) (j:hun/tomno) (r:zd:20854/zd:24276/zd:14852) (q:draft)
hunzang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:time/religion) (w:spend time/use the time) (d:<hun> and <zang> written as one word: spend time; at a meeting or service, take a part of the programme, and also the person who takes it) (j:hun/zang) (r:zd:20572/zd:17055) (q:draft)
hunzat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:use of time/time spent/spending time) (d:<hun>, time, with <zat>, use: the way time is used; {hunzat khop} is spend time together) (j:hun/zat) (r:zd:23453/zd:20958/zd:24963) (q:draft)
hunzatkhop = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/religion) (w:spend time together) (d:<hun>, time, <zat>, use, and <khop>, together, written as one word: spend time together; in funeral notices {anunungpen hunzatkhop ding} is the last time to be together with the one who died) (j:hun/zat/khop) (r:zd:22388/zd:25449) (q:draft)
hunzatkhopding = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/religion) (w:time to spend together) (d:<hun>, <zat>, <khop> and <ding> written as one word: the time to be spent together; in death notices {a nunungpen hunzatkhopding} is the last time to be together with the dead, the funeral service) (j:hun/zat/khop/ding) (r:zd:10901/zd:11832) (q:draft)
hunzatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/religion/time) (w:programme/service/use of time) (d:<hun>, time, with <zatna>, using: the spending of time on something, and so a programme, a session or a service held by a group) (r:zd:20792/zd:24036/zd:20172) (q:draft)
hunzui = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:time/everyday) (w:timely/seasonal/up to date/fashionable) (d:<hun>, time, with <zui>, follow: in keeping with the time or season; {a hunzui in} is in due time, as the times require) (j:hun/zui) (r:zd:24276/zd:23156/zd:25333) (q:draft)
Hurricane = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature/media) (w:hurricane) (d:a violent tropical storm of the Atlantic; written before the name of the storm and often followed by <huihpi>, as {Hurricane Irma huihpi}) (o:English) (r:zd:15054/zd:14983/zd:15679) (q:draft)
huup = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (j:hup) (r:zd:22784/zd:11323) (q:draft)
huup = (i:2) (t:v) (f:social) (w:attract/draw/win over) (d:draw people to oneself as a magnet draws iron; {sik huup} is a magnet) (r:zd:24574/zd:9259) (q:draft)
huzaap = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:influence/sway) (d:the power of a person, group or idea to affect what others think and do) (r:zd:25461/zd:16521) (q:draft)
huzaap = (i:2) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:influence) (d:have an effect on what people think and how they live) (r:ts:9859/zd:24593) (q:draft, low confidence)
huzap = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:influence/impact) (d:the power of a person or thing to shape others; {mi huzap} is an influential person) (r:zd:12341) (q:draft)
huzap = (i:2) (t:v) (f:social) (w:influence/affect) (d:have an effect on how someone thinks or acts) (r:zd:21013/zd:8667) (q:draft)
hygiene = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health) (w:hygiene/cleanliness) (d:cleanliness that guards health, as required of restaurants, hotels and water supply) (o:English) (r:zd:17003/zd:17668) (q:draft, low confidence)
Hymn = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:hymn) (d:a Christian song of praise for worship; the English word used in writing on church songs) (o:English) (r:zd:9219/zd:9211) (q:draft)
Hymnal = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:hymnal/hymn book) (d:the book of hymns of a church) (o:English) (r:zd:9211/zd:9244) (q:draft)
Hymns = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:hymn) (d:the English plural used in Zolai text for church songs of the older Western tradition) (o:English) (r:zd:17634) (q:draft, low confidence)
Hypermarket = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/work) (w:hypermarket) (d:a very large shop selling food and household goods) (o:English) (r:zd:16733/zd:20490) (q:draft, low confidence)
ibiak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:religion) (w:we worship) (d:<i>, we, and <biak>, worship, written as one word, standing before the one worshipped: whom we worship) (j:i/biak) (r:zd:24250/zd:19800) (q:draft)
ici = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:we say/we call) (d:<i>, we, and <ci>, say, written as one word: we say, we call it) (j:i/ci) (r:zd:20045/zd:19400/zd:23298) (q:draft)
icih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:what we call/so-called) (d:<i>, we, and <cih>, say, written as one word; placed after a word or phrase to take it up as a topic: what we call, the thing called) (j:i/cih) (r:zd:24047/zd:16245/zd:24214) (q:draft)
icihte = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:what we call/the so-called/those we say are) (d:<i> and <cihte> written as one word, after a name or a quoted saying: the things or people that we call so, what we say) (j:i/cihte) (r:zd:19641/zd:17161/zd:23037) (q:draft)
ID = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:ID/identity document/identity card) (d:a document that shows who a person is, also said {ID card}) (o:English) (r:zd:21421/zd:18144/zd:20486) (q:draft)
idea = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/education) (w:idea) (s:ngaihsutna) (o:English) (r:zd:22282/zd:22444/zd:22023) (q:draft)
identity = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:identity) (d:who a person or a people is; often set beside the Zolai {Zomi hihna}, being Zomi) (o:English) (r:zd:20337/zd:19302) (q:draft, low confidence)
ideology = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:ideology) (d:a system of political or religious ideas that a party or movement holds) (o:English) (r:zd:23325/ts:11162/zd:11906) (q:draft)
Idol = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media) (w:idol/singing contest) (d:English word used mostly in <Zomi Idol>, the name of a Zomi singing competition named after American Idol, and for its contestants; writers discuss it against the Bible sense of idol, <milim>) (o:English) (r:zd:23005/zd:23135/zd:15865) (q:draft, low confidence)
IDP = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/social) (w:internally displaced person/IDP) (d:English abbreviation: a person who has fled from home because of war and stays inside the own country, mostly in {IDP Camp}, a camp for such people) (o:English) (r:zd:11972/zd:14790) (q:draft)
igam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:our country/our land) (d:<i> and <gam> written as one word: our country, our homeland) (j:i/gam) (r:zd:22815/zd:24207/zd:12767) (q:draft)
igen = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:we say/we speak of) (d:<i>, we, and <gen>, say, written as one word: we say, what we have said) (j:i/gen) (r:zd:24320/zd:24157/zd:22802) (q:draft)
ih = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (j:i) (r:zd:22557/zd:24411/zd:22818) (q:draft)
ihci = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:we say/we call) (d:<ih>, another spelling of <i>, we, written as one word with <ci>, say: we say, we call it) (j:i/ci) (r:zd:14755/zd:17727) (q:draft)
ihcih = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:what we call/so-called) (d:<ih>, we, and <cih>, say, written as one word, placed after a term that is being explained: what we call, that which we mean by) (j:ih/cih) (r:zd:11020/zd:15810) (q:draft)
ihgam = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:social/politics) (w:our country/our land) (d:<ih>, another spelling of <i>, our, and <gam>, country, written as one word: our country, our homeland) (j:i/gam) (r:zd:11988/zd:23252) (q:draft)
ihgen = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:we say/we tell) (d:<ih>, we, and <gen> written as one word: we say, what we say) (j:ih/gen) (r:zd:24381/zd:12093/zd:19676) (q:draft)
ihhih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (j:ihih) (r:zd:22977/zd:15970) (q:draft)
ihiam = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:<i>, we, and the question particle <hiam> written as one word at the end of a question about ourselves: are we, shall we) (j:i/hiam) (r:zd:24157/zd:24068/zd:20073) (q:draft)
ihihi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:we are) (d:<ihi>, we are, and the sentence ending <hi> written as one word, closing a statement about all of us) (j:ihi/hi) (r:zd:21866/zd:23780/zd:23148) (q:draft)
ihihman = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:because we are/since we are) (d:<ihih>, we are, with <man>, reason, written as one word and followed by <in>: because we are or because we do; the lexicon writes {ihih manin}) (j:ihih/man) (r:zd:20808/zd:15274) (q:draft)
ihihmanin = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:because we are/since we) (d:<ihih> and <manin> written as one word: because we are, since we do or shall do what the clause before it says) (j:ihih/manin) (r:zd:15514/zd:25399) (q:draft)
ihki = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:<ih>, a spelling of <i>, we, and the prefix <ki> written as one word before a verb: we, with the action done to ourselves or to one another) (j:ih/ki) (r:zd:12345/zd:15814) (q:draft)
ihlei = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:social/politics) (w:our land/our soil) (d:<ih>, another spelling of <i>, our, and <lei>, land, written as one word: our land, mostly in the pair {ihgam ihlei}, our country and our land, the homeland) (j:i/lei) (r:zd:18258/zd:23252) (q:draft)
ihmu = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/body) (w:sleep) (a:khanglo/khanlawh)
ihmuh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:we see) (d:<ih> and <muh> written as one word: we see, what we see; {ihmuh ciangin} is when we see) (j:ih/muh) (r:zd:24231/zd:23843) (q:draft)
ihnei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:we have) (d:<ih>, we, and <nei>, have, written as one word: we have, speaker and hearers together) (j:ih/nei) (r:zd:19676/zd:16797) (q:draft)
ihneih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:we have/that we have) (d:<ih> and <neih> written as one word: we have, or what we have) (j:ih/neih) (r:zd:25919/zd:16360/zd:15300) (q:draft)
ihngah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:we get/we receive) (d:<ih>, we, and <ngah>, get, written as one word) (j:ih/ngah) (r:zd:19676/zd:16194/zd:18924) (q:draft)
ihom = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:we are/we live/we stay) (d:<ih>, we, and <om>, be, written as one word: we are in a place or a state, we live there; {ihom ciangin} is when we are) (j:ih/om) (r:zd:12093/zd:15433) (q:draft)
ihpa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/social) (w:our father/our fathers) (d:<ih>, our, with <pa>, father, written as one word; mostly in {ihpu ihpa te}, our forefathers) (j:ih/pa) (r:zd:8668/zd:18258) (q:draft)
ihpai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:we go) (d:<ih>, another spelling of <i>, we, written as one word with <pai>, go: we go, when we go) (j:i/pai) (r:zd:23784/zd:14709/zd:19421) (q:draft)
ihpilna = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:education/social) (w:our knowledge/our wisdom) (d:<ih>, we or our, and <pilna>, knowledge, written as one word) (j:i/pilna) (r:zd:22652) (q:draft)
ihpu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/social) (w:our forefathers/our ancestors) (d:<ih>, our, written as one word with <pu>, grandfather; found in the pair <ihpu ihpa>, our forefathers) (j:ih/pu) (r:zd:8668/zd:21590) (q:draft)
ihpu ihpa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/social) (w:our forefathers/our ancestors) (d:<ihpu>, our grandfathers, paired with <ihpa>, our fathers: our forefathers, the generations before us, mostly followed by <te>) (r:zd:8668/zd:20170) (q:draft)
ihsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:we consider/we think/we find) (d:<ih>, we, and <sak>, here feel or consider, written as one word: what we feel or take to be so, as in {nuam ihsak}, what we find pleasant) (j:ih/sak) (r:zd:25932/zd:25926/zd:25919) (q:draft)
ihsep = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:we do/we work) (d:<ih>, a spelling of <i>, we, and <sep> written as one word: that we do, our doing; {ihsep ding} is what we must do) (j:i/sep) (r:zd:25924/zd:15407/zd:25932) (q:draft)
ihteel = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/everyday) (w:we choose/we elect) (d:<ih>, we, and <teel>, choose, written as one word: we choose or elect) (j:ih/teel) (r:zd:24277/zd:8668) (q:draft)
ihtheih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/education) (w:we know/we learn) (d:<ih>, we, and <theih> written as one word: that we know, what we know) (j:ih/theih) (r:zd:25224/zd:23025/zd:19427) (q:draft)
ihtheihsa = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:as we know/what we already know) (d:<ih>, a spelling of <i>, we, with <theihsa>, already known, written as one word: what we already know; <ihtheihsa mahbangin> is as we already know) (j:i/theihsa) (r:zd:14531/zd:12581) (q:draft)
ihtheihsa mahbangin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/media) (w:as we know/as is well known) (d:<ihtheihsa>, what we already know, and <mahbangin>, just as: placed after the topic of a sentence to present what follows as common knowledge) (r:zd:11074/zd:14531) (q:draft)
ihzat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:we use) (d:<ih>, we, and <zat>, use, written as one word: that we use, our using) (j:ih/zat) (r:zd:25924/zd:22584) (q:draft)
ii = (i:1) (t:ppm) (f:everyday) (w:of) (d:marker placed after a noun or name to show that what follows belongs to it, like English of or the ending 's) (r:zd:16434/ts:11162/zd:19805) (q:draft)
iin = (i:1) (t:ppm) (f:everyday) (j:in) (r:zd:14820/zd:14821) (q:draft, low confidence)
