Isa = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:we consider/we feel/we find) (d:<i>, we, and <sa>, feel or consider, written as one word after a describing word: we find it so, as in {muan huai isa}, we find it trustworthy; the capital form {Isa.} in the articles is the abbreviation of the book of Isaiah) (j:i/sa) (r:zd:24043/zd:20999) (q:draft)
Isa = (i:2) (t:n) (f:body/family) (w:our flesh) (d:<i>, our, and <sa>, flesh, written as one word: our flesh, also our own kin, in the pairs {i ci leh isa} and {imi isa}) (j:i/sa) (r:zd:17488) (q:draft, low confidence)
