itsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/family) (w:love for/cherish/make love) (d:<it>, love, with <sak> written as one word: love or cherish what belongs to another, or cause to love; with <ki> before it, as {ki-itsak}, make a show of loving) (j:it/sak) (r:zd:26049/zd:11592) (q:draft, low confidence)
itzia = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/social) (w:way of loving/love) (d:<it>, love, with <zia>, manner, written as one word: the way in which, or how much, someone loves) (j:it/zia) (r:zd:17333/zd:20851/zd:24542) (q:draft)
izaakmanin = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:social/media) (w:because we heard) (d:<i>, we, <zak>, hear, here written with a long vowel, and <manin>, because, written as one word: because we have heard, having learned of; a set phrase of condolence notices) (j:i/zak/manin) (r:zd:24292/zd:21699) (q:draft)
izak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:we hear/we heard) (d:<i>, we, and <zak>, hear, written as one word) (j:i/zak) (r:zd:25180/zd:24200) (q:draft)
izakman = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:social/media) (d:<i>, <zak> and <man> written as one word and followed by <in>: because we have heard; used in notices of condolence, {cih thu izakman in}, having heard the news that) (j:i/zak/man) (r:zd:25872) (q:draft)
izat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:we use) (d:<i> and <zat> written as one word: we use, what we use) (j:i/zat) (r:zd:11076/zd:25473) (q:draft)
jacket = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:jacket) (d:a jacket; {Life Jacket} is a life jacket) (o:English) (r:zd:9451/zd:15790/zd:12936) (q:draft)
