kak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:side by side/in comparison) (d:placed after a verb of looking, measuring or thinking: one against the other, comparing the two; {et kak} and {teh kak} mean compare, as in <enkak> and <tehkak>) (r:zd:8667/zd:23453/zd:22371) (q:draft)
kakah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education) (w:I attended/I went to) (d:<ka>, I, and <kah> written as one word; mostly in {sang kakah}, I attended school) (j:ka/kah) (r:zd:16343/zd:17478) (q:draft)
kaki = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:<ka>, I, and the verb prefix <ki> written as one word before a verb: I or we, with <uh>, do the thing to myself or to one another, as {kaki ho uhhi}, we talked together) (j:ka/ki) (r:zd:17936/zd:16337/zd:19984) (q:draft)
