Kalewa = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel) (w:Kalewa) (d:town and township on the Chindwin river in Sagaing Region, Myanmar, east of Kalaymyo; its Zolai name is given as <Gunkhawm>) (r:ts:7775/zd:21626) (q:draft)
kalkhat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:one week/a week) (d:<kal>, week, and <khat>, one, written as one word: one week; {kalkhat in} is in a week, per week, and {nipi kalkhat} is also one week, as <nipikal>) (j:kal/khat) (r:zd:14921/zd:20806/zd:17428) (q:draft)
kalkhat = (i:2) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:one step/a step) (d:<kal>, step, and <khat>, one, written as one word: one step of the foot; {kalkhat suan} is take one step) (j:kal/khat) (r:zd:20971/zd:21948) (q:draft)
kalkhatsung = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:for a week/within a week) (d:<kal>, week, <khat>, one, and <sung>, in, written as one word: for one week, during one week) (j:kal/khat/sung) (r:zd:19803/zd:11256/zd:12723) (q:draft)
kalnih = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:two weeks/fortnight) (d:<kal>, week, and <nih>, two, written as one word: two weeks; {kalnih sungin} is within two weeks and {kalnih khitciangin} is two weeks later) (j:kal/nih) (r:zd:16045/zd:15816/zd:11700) (q:draft)
kalsim = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:weekly/every week) (d:<kal>, week, with <sim>, each: {kalsim in} is every week, and before a noun it means weekly, as in {kalsim thungetna}, the weekly prayer meeting) (r:zd:10892/zd:12822/zd:12647) (q:draft)
kalsuan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/body) (w:walk/step/take a step) (d:move forward on foot, take steps) (r:45.8.1) (q:draft)
