lainatpihna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/family) (w:sympathy/condolence/compassion) (d:<lainat>, feel compassion, with <pih>, together with, and the noun suffix <na>: feeling the pain of someone together with them; {lainatpihna lahna} is a showing of condolence to the bereaved) (b:lainat) (r:zd:11757) (q:draft)
Laipian = (i:1) (t:name) (f:religion) (w:Laipian) (d:the religion founded by Pau Cin Hau and the script he made, {Laipian Lai}; also said of its followers and their church) (r:ts:3375/zd:23171) (q:draft)
laipil = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:education) (w:educated/learned/good at studies) (d:<lai>, letters, with <pil>, wise: learned from books, doing well at school; also a person who is so, as in {laipil khat}) (r:zd:21991/zd:22556/zd:24502) (q:draft)
laipilna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:education/book learning/schooling) (d:<lai>, letters, and <pilna>, knowledge, written as one word: learning gained from books and school) (j:lai/pilna) (r:zd:24963/zd:25115/zd:23112) (q:draft)
laisiah = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:as long as/as far as) (d:placed after a clause: for as long as, or to the extent that, it is so; {ahih theih laisiah} is as far as possible) (r:zd:24069/zd:23394/zd:16202) (q:draft)
laisiam = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:education) (w:educated/learned/good at study) (d:<lai>, writing or study, with <siam>, skilled: learned, well educated or good at school work; also a noun, an educated person) (r:zd:9134/zd:20125/zd:21617) (q:draft)
Laisiangtho = (i:1) (t:name) (f:religion) (w:Bible/Scripture/Holy Scripture) (d:<lai>, writing, and <siangtho>, holy, written as one word: the Bible) (j:lai/siangtho) (r:zd:20798/zd:15810/zd:23191) (q:draft)
laisim = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education/everyday) (w:read/study) (d:<lai>, writing, with <sim>, read: read a text; {laisim ngei lo} is never having studied) (s:sim) (q:draft)
laisimna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:reading/study/education) (d:<laisim>, read or study, with the noun suffix <na>: the reading of books, and study or schooling as a whole) (b:laisim) (r:zd:22680/zd:11891/zd:21617) (q:draft)
laisin = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:study/schooling/learning) (d:<lai>, writing, and <sin>, learn, written as one word: studying, going to school; {laisin kum} is a school year) (j:lai/sin) (r:zd:10717/zd:24429/zd:23198) (q:draft)
laisinna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:education/schooling/study/learning) (d:<lai>, letters, with <sinna>, learning: study at school and what is gained by it; {laisinna sang} is a school) (r:zd:21529/zd:16415/zd:21168) (q:draft)
laitakpen = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:time) (w:at the very moment/while) (d:<laitak> and <pen> written as one word: the very moment when something was happening, taken as the topic of the sentence) (j:laitak/pen) (r:zd:11472/zd:16731) (q:draft)
laitakzong = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday/time) (w:even while/also at the moment when) (d:<laitak>, at the very time, and <zong>, also, written as one word: the very moment when something happens, as well) (j:laitak/zong) (r:zd:14616/zd:17419) (q:draft)
laitan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:education/level of education/schooling) (d:the level of schooling a person has reached, formal education; {laitan sang} is a high level of education) (r:zd:21991/zd:24471/zd:17971) (q:draft)
laitawh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:education/social) (w:in writing/by letter) (d:<lai> and <tawh> written as one word: in writing, by a written document; after the name of a language, in that language or script) (j:lai/tawh) (r:zd:14910/zd:15274/zd:25022) (q:draft)
Laituite = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (f:social) (w:Laitui people) (d:the people of the village <Laitui>) (b:Laitui) (r:zd:23489/zd:20406) (q:draft)
laivuan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:examination/exam) (d:<lai>, writing, with {vuan}: a school examination, and to sit one; {Tan 10 laivuan} is the grade ten examination) (r:zd:22683/zd:25666/zd:11748) (q:draft)
laivuanding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education) (w:sit an examination/take an exam) (d:<laivuan>, sit an examination, and <ding>, will, written as one word: to sit an examination, going to sit an examination; also the examination that is to be held) (j:laivuan/ding) (r:zd:11392/zd:18012/zd:11748) (q:draft)
laivuanna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:examination/exam) (d:a written examination at school or university; {Tan 10 laivuanna} is the tenth standard, matriculation, examination) (r:zd:15459/zd:25630) (q:draft)
Laizo = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (f:social) (w:Laizo) (d:name of the Chin people of the Falam area and of their language, also called Falam; {Laizo pau} is the Laizo language) (r:zd:22334/zd:26700) (q:draft)
laizom = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/social) (w:full sibling/blood brother or sister/kin) (d:a brother or sister born of the same mother, often <sanggam laizom>, {unau laizom} or {pianpih laizom}; in a wider sense fellow members of one people, as {Zomi laizom}) (s:sanggam) (r:zd:12998/zd:23717/zd:25866) (q:draft)
laizomte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/social) (w:kinsfolk/brothers and sisters/relatives/brethren) (d:plural of <laizom>, one joined by the same navel cord: brothers and sisters, and more widely relatives or fellow members of the people, often said with <sanggam>) (r:zd:25287/ts:1343) (q:draft)
lak = (i:3) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:take) (d:take something into the hand or into one's keeping. The form of <la>, take, used before endings and other words) (a:pia) (q:example wanted)
laka khat = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:one of/one among) (d:<laka>, among, and <khat>, one: placed after a plural noun phrase, usually ending in <te> or {te'}, one of those named; often followed by {ahi hi}, is) (r:zd:9445/zd:13340/zd:23137) (q:draft)
lakah kihel = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:be among/be one of/be counted among) (d:<lakah>, among, and <kihel.2>, be included: after a plural noun, be one of that group or be counted in it; with <sak>, {lakah kihel sak}, count someone among) (r:zd:21978/zd:9253/zd:24227) (q:draft)
lakahzong = (i:1) (t:prep) (f:everyday) (w:also among/even among) (d:<lakah>, among, and <zong>, also, written as one word: among those people or things too) (j:lakah/zong) (r:zd:12656/zd:19586) (q:draft)
lakam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education/media) (w:poetic word/poetic language/poetic diction) (d:<la>, song, with <kam>, word: the special words and phrases used in Zomi songs and poetry, different from everyday speech) (r:zd:15396/zd:23651) (q:draft)
lakding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:to take/to be taken) (d:<lak>, take, and <ding> written as one word: that is to be taken or for taking; {Refugee lakding} is the taking in of refugees) (j:lak/ding) (r:zd:15465/zd:22159/zd:11011) (q:draft)
lakh = (i:1) (t:num) (f:work) (w:hundred thousand/lakh) (d:one hundred thousand, used in counting money and people) (o:Hindi, lakh) (r:zd:17675/zd:16754) (q:draft)
lakh = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:show/display) (d:another spelling of <lak>, show, let something be seen; compare <lah> and <kilak>) (r:zd:25025) (q:draft, low confidence)
lakhin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:have taken/have received) (d:<la>, take, and <khin>, already, written as one word: have already taken or received; {pension lakhin} is retired, having taken the pension) (j:la/khin) (r:zd:12876/zd:16900/zd:16640) (q:draft)
lakhs = (i:1) (t:num) (f:work) (w:lakh/hundred thousand) (d:a hundred thousand, used in counting Myanmar kyats; the English plural form stands after any number) (s:tengh/tulza) (o:English, lakh) (r:zd:19166/zd:19210) (q:draft)
lakhui = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media) (w:album/song album) (d:a set of recorded songs released together; often followed by the English word, {lakhui album}) (r:zd:20920/zd:16442/zd:21070) (q:draft)
laklawh = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:unfinished/incomplete/halfway/half-done) (d:left in the middle before it is complete, of work, schooling or talk; of a person, half-taught or half-grown, as in {mipil laklawh}) (r:zd:26565/zd:22773/zd:23591) (q:draft)
laksawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:plan to take/try to take/be about to take) (d:<lak>, take, and <sawm>, intend, written as one word: plan, try or be about to take, take in or capture; in headlines of a country that plans to take in refugees) (j:lak/sawm) (r:zd:15465/zd:15116/zd:11924) (q:draft)
lala = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:repeatedly/again and again/on and on) (d:placed after a verb: do the action over and over or without restraint; {tai lala} is keep scolding) (r:zd:24072/zd:18023) (q:draft, low confidence)
lala = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:keep taking/take again and again) (d:the verb for take said twice: take one after another, take up repeatedly) (r:zd:22742) (q:draft, low confidence)
lalna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/social) (w:migration/immigration/moving) (d:<lal>, move to live elsewhere, with the noun ending {-na}: moving from one place or country to live in another) (b:lal) (r:zd:11697/zd:23479) (q:draft)
lalo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:not take/not charge) (d:the verb take, whose other form is <lak>, and <lo>, not, written as one word: not take, not accept; {sum lalo} is without taking money) (j:la/lo) (r:zd:15453/zd:12487/zd:19939) (q:draft)
Lalta = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua) (f:travel/social) (w:Lalta) (d:a Zomi village, named as the home village of persons and in the name of its village association; said to be in the Tedim area of Chin State) (r:zd:15275) (q:draft, low confidence)
lam phawk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:realize that/be aware that/bear in mind that) (d:<lam>, way, used here as the fact that, and <phawk>, remember or be aware: realize or keep in mind that something is so; follows a clause that ends in <ahih> or another verb, and is often closed by a hortative, as {lam phawk ni}, let us bear in mind that, or by <tawntung>, always) (r:zd:9445/zd:21340/zd:25891) (q:draft)
lam zuanin = (i:1) (t:prep) (f:travel/everyday) (w:toward/towards/in the direction of/bound for) (d:<lam>, direction, and <zuanin>, heading for: placed after a place name or a noun of place and before a verb of movement, toward that place) (r:zd:26708/zd:20083/zd:9254) (q:draft)
lamal = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/religion) (w:lyrics/words of a song) (d:<la>, song, with <mal>, a single word: the words of a song, as distinct from {la-aw}, its tune) (r:zd:9258/zd:16337/zd:14789) (q:draft)
lamalte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/religion) (w:lyrics/words of a song) (d:<la>, song, and <malte>, words, written as one word: the words of a song or hymn, as distinct from its tune) (j:la/malte) (r:zd:9220/zd:9228) (q:draft)
lamdang kasa = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:I am amazed/I find it strange/I wonder) (d:<lamdang>, strange or wonderful, and <kasa>, I feel: the expression {lamdang sa}, find something strange or marvellous, in the first person; the thing wondered at stands before it) (r:zd:10973/zd:21034) (q:draft)
lamdang kisa = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be astonished/cause amazement/be thought strange) (d:<lamdang>, surprise, and <kisa>, the form with {ki-} of <sa>, feel: people find it strange, there is astonishment; said of an event without naming who is surprised, often closing a headline, while {lamdang sa} names the person who is surprised) (r:zd:25227/zd:21042) (q:draft)
lamdanna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:difference/distinctiveness/strangeness) (d:<lamdang> with the noun suffix {-na}: what makes a person or thing different or unusual; {ki lamdanna} is the difference between two) (b:lamdang) (r:zd:25919/zd:11447/zd:20790) (q:draft)
lamdawt = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/everyday) (w:shortcut/short cut) (d:a shorter way that cuts across, and so a quick or easy way to get something without the proper effort; {lamdawt tawn} is take a shortcut) (r:zd:26645/zd:23590/zd:26310) (q:draft)
lametbei = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/social) (w:hopeless/despairing/without hope) (d:<lamet>, hope, with <bei>, come to an end: having no hope left; also as a noun, hopelessness, despair) (j:lamet/bei) (r:zd:19975/zd:21384) (q:draft)
lametloh = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:unexpected/unexpectedly) (d:<lamet> and <loh> written as one word: not expected; {lametloh laitak in} is at a moment when no one expects it, {lametloh in} unexpectedly) (j:lamet/loh) (r:zd:14709/zd:22717) (q:draft)
lametlohpi = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:unexpectedly/suddenly/by surprise) (d:<lamet>, expect, and <lohpi>, without, written as one word: without its being expected, usually followed by <in>) (j:lamet/lohpi) (r:zd:14776/zd:19197) (q:draft)
lamh = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/work) (w:property/possessions/belongings) (d:found in the pair {neih leh lamh}, what one has and owns; elsewhere in the articles it is part of personal names) (r:zd:23594) (q:draft, low confidence)
lamhna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/home) (j:lamna) (r:zd:23667/zd:17060) (q:draft)
lamhonsakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion/travel) (w:opening of a way/opportunity) (d:<lam> way and <honsakna> opening written as one word: the opening of a way for someone, said mostly of God making it possible to go abroad, as in {Pasian lamhonsakna tawh}) (j:lam/honsakna) (r:zd:22664/zd:25060) (q:draft)
lamkaal = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (j:lamkal) (r:zd:19435/zd:20545) (q:draft)
lamkan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:cross the road/cross the street) (d:<lam>, road, with <kan>, step over or cross, as in <kantan>, written as one word: go across a road; {khetawh lamkan} is cross on foot) (j:lam/kan) (r:zd:11710/zd:14676/zd:15846) (q:draft)
lamkhang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/nature) (w:lower roadside/downhill side of the road) (d:the side of a road that falls away below it, the opposite of the upper side; {lamsak lamkhang} is both sides of the road) (r:zd:14824/zd:17952) (q:draft, low confidence)
lamkhat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:one side/one way) (d:<lam> and <khat> written as one word: one side or one point of view; {lamkhat panin} is in one way, on the one hand) (j:lam/khat) (r:zd:20818/zd:22557) (q:draft)
lampai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:walk/travel) (d:<lam>, road, and <pai>, go, also used as a noun, journey) (s:khualzin) (q:draft)
lampan = (i:1) (t:prep) (f:everyday) (w:from the side of/on the part of/from) (d:<lam>, side or direction, and <pan>, from, written as one word: from the side of, on the part of, as regards) (j:lam/pan) (r:zd:15992/zd:21050/zd:16442) (q:draft)
lampanin = (i:1) (t:prep) (f:everyday/politics) (w:from the side of/on the part of) (d:<lam>, side or direction, and <panin>, from, written as one word and placed after a noun: from that side or direction, on the part of that person or body) (j:lam/panin) (r:zd:20676/zd:18112/zd:12938) (q:draft)
lampi = (i:3) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:road) (b:lam)
lampi maan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/religion) (w:right path/right way) (d:<lampi>, road, and <maan>, true or right: the right path, said of right conduct in life and not of a road; the object of verbs of walking, leading and teaching, as in {lampi maan tot}, walk the right path, and {lampi maan hilh}, show the right way) (r:zd:23191/zd:26645/zd:23301) (q:draft)
lampigei = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:roadside/side of the road) (d:<lampi>, road, and <gei>, side, written as one word: the side of the road, beside the road) (j:lampi/gei) (r:zd:17924/zd:20008/zd:19581) (q:draft)
lampithak = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/everyday) (w:new road/new way/new route) (d:<lampi> and <thak> written as one word: a new road or railway line, or a new way of doing or living) (j:lampi/thak) (r:zd:21898/zd:19975/zd:22540) (q:draft)
lampitung = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:travel) (w:on the road/on the street) (d:<lampi>, road, and <tung>, on, written as one word: on the road, also after the name of a road; {lampitung tuahsiatna} is a road accident) (j:lampi/tung) (r:zd:20641/zd:17735/zd:25047) (q:draft)
lamsan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work) (w:be under construction) (d:in {aki lamsan}, which is still being built: build, with the ending {-san}, while it is going on; compare <kilam>, be built) (r:zd:12448/zd:20488) (q:draft)
lamsap = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/work) (w:fare/travel cost/travel expenses) (d:<lam>, way, with <sap>, hire: the money paid for a journey, as <innsap> is the rent for a house) (r:zd:20639/zd:20587/zd:21717) (q:draft)
lamsiau = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:take a walk/stroll/walk about) (d:go about on foot for exercise or pleasure, without an errand; of a small child, be able to walk) (r:zd:24276/zd:25115/zd:20841) (q:draft)
lamtawh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:in the area of/by way of) (d:<lam>, side or direction, and <tawh>, with, written as one word: {biakna lamtawh kisai} is concerning religion, and {politic lamtawh} is by way of politics) (j:lam/tawh) (r:zd:24469/zd:20899/zd:22850) (q:draft)
lamteh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (d:<lam> and <teh> written as one word after a word of time: at about that time, only then; {a nung lamteh} is only afterwards and {tu lamteh} nowadays) (j:lam/teh) (r:ts:2731/zd:12352) (q:draft, low confidence)
lamteh = (i:2) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:cross) (d:second part of {sing lamteh}, the cross, written as one word in <singlamteh>) (r:zd:25947) (q:draft)
lamten = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:those of the side/people of) (d:<lam>, side or direction, with the plural <te> and the subject marker <in> written as one word: the people of that side, group or region, as the ones who act) (j:lam/te/in) (r:ts:8304/zd:22350) (q:draft)
lamthak = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:new road/new way) (d:<lam>, way, and <thak>, new, written as one word: a newly made road, or a new way of doing things) (j:lam/thak) (r:zd:20176/zd:25569) (q:draft)
lamthak = (i:2) (t:v) (f:work/home) (w:build new/newly built) (d:<lam> as a verb, build, with <thak>, new: {aki lamthak} is newly built) (r:zd:20456) (q:draft, low confidence)
Lamzaang = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua) (f:travel) (j:Lamzang) (r:ts:7872) (q:draft)
lamzik = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:road/street) (d:a road for vehicles, in a town or between towns) (s:lampi) (r:zd:11646/zd:20023) (q:draft)
lamzikpi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:highway/main road) (d:a large road for motor traffic) (r:zd:12811/zd:16942/zd:17164) (q:draft)
lamzikpitung = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:travel) (w:on the highway/on the main road) (d:<lamzikpi>, main road or highway, and <tung>, on, written as one word: on the road named, along the highway) (j:lamzikpi/tung) (r:zd:15913/zd:21020/zd:19082) (q:draft)
lamzong = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (d:<lam> and <zong> written as one word: also the way, side or manner; after a clause, also the fact that, as in {ahih lamzong}, also that it is so) (j:lam/zong) (r:zd:17862/zd:12487/zd:11251) (q:draft)
lamzuan = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:travel) (w:toward/bound for/heading for) (d:<lam> and <zuan> written as one word, placed after a place name: heading in the direction of that place) (j:lam/zuan) (r:zd:16892/zd:26976/zd:17661) (q:draft)
Lancaster = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel/education) (w:Lancaster) (d:English place name, of towns in the United States, as in Lancaster Bible College; also met as a family name) (o:English) (r:zd:25305) (q:draft, low confidence)
Landmine = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:landmine/mine) (d:an explosive hidden in the ground; {landmine siah} is lay mines and {landmine sikkha} is step on a mine) (o:English) (r:ts:5635/zd:20562/ts:3784) (q:draft)
Lane = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:lane) (d:one of the strips of a road or of a running track) (o:English) (r:zd:17488/zd:19925) (q:draft, low confidence)
langdo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/social) (w:oppose/resist/go against) (d:<lang>, side, with <do>, fight: take a stand against a person, a rule or a government; {kumpi langdo te} are those who oppose the government) (s:langpang/langpan) (r:zd:18952/zd:25923/zd:13354) (q:draft)
langdona = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:opposition/rebellion/resistance/insurgency) (d:the act of taking the other side and fighting against someone, from <lang> and <dona>; {kumpi langdona} is rebellion against the government) (r:zd:23670/zd:19316) (q:draft)
Langkawi = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel) (w:Langkawi) (d:island and holiday resort off the north-west coast of Malaysia) (r:zd:17802/zd:17941) (q:draft)
langlam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/politics) (w:other side/opposite side/opposing side) (d:<lang>, side, with <lam>, direction: the side across from one, the opposite direction, or the side opposed to one; {a langlam pan} is from the other side, on the other hand) (r:zd:11234/zd:9433/zd:20358) (q:draft)
Lanka = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:travel/politics) (w:Sri Lanka) (d:second word of the name Sri Lanka, the island country south of India, formerly Ceylon) (r:zd:12370/zd:24207) (q:draft)
Laos = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:travel/politics) (w:Laos) (d:country in Southeast Asia that borders the east of Shan State of Myanmar) (r:zd:18020/zd:23957) (q:draft)
laphuaksiam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion/media) (w:songwriter/composer/hymn writer) (d:<laphuak>, compose songs, and <siam>, skilled, written as one word: a skilled maker of songs or hymns) (j:laphuak/siam) (r:zd:9223/zd:9235) (q:draft)
lapin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:in time/on time/in good time) (d:early enough, before it is too late; mostly as {a hun lapin}, in time) (r:zd:22479/zd:22228) (q:draft)
lapsang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/religion) (w:lift up/exalt/raise up/promote) (d:lift someone or something high, in rank, honour or esteem; the opposite of <niamkhiat>, bring low) (a:niamkhiat) (r:zd:23386/zd:23394/zd:14844) (q:draft)
Laptop = (i:1) (t:n) (f:it) (w:laptop/laptop computer) (d:a computer that can be carried and used on the lap) (o:English) (r:zd:21543/zd:22499/zd:15300) (q:draft)
lapzo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:be in time/catch up/make it) (d:<lap>, catch up with, and <zo>, here in its sense of be able, written as one word: manage to reach something in time or keep up with it) (j:lap/zo) (r:zd:25937/zd:24630) (q:draft)
lasa = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:sing) (d:sing a song, from <la>, song, and <sa>, sing) (s:lasak) (q:draft)
Lashio = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel) (w:Lashio) (d:a city in northern Shan State, Myanmar) (r:zd:26620/zd:17067) (q:draft)
lasiamte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media) (w:singers) (d:plural of <lasiam>: singers, those who sing well) (b:lasiam) (r:zd:10743/zd:16040) (q:draft)
Lataih = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion/media) (w:song practice/singing practice) (d:practice sessions of singers before a concert, a contest or a festival, from <la>, song; the practices come before the final rehearsal) (r:zd:23365/zd:17234) (q:draft, low confidence)
lau = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:afraid/frightened/fearful) (d:feeling fear; {lau mahmah} is very afraid) (s:meidawi) (a:hang/lungmuang)
lauh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:fear/be afraid) (d:form of <lau> used before <ding>, <nading>, <man> and <dan>; {lauh ding om lo} is there is nothing to fear) (b:lau) (r:zd:20484/zd:23986/zd:24035) (q:draft)
lauhhuai = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (j:lauhuai) (r:zd:25927/zd:26643/zd:24748) (q:draft)
lauhna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:fear/dread) (d:the feeling of being afraid, also fear that something may happen; {gal lauhna} is fear of war) (s:launa) (r:zd:14916/zd:17685/zd:24804) (q:draft)
lauhuailua = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:too dangerous/very frightening) (d:<lauhuai> and <lua> written as one word: too fearful, very dangerous) (j:lauhuai/lua) (r:zd:24276/zd:22223/zd:19814) (q:draft)
Laukkai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:politics) (w:Laukkai) (d:town in the north of Shan State, Myanmar, chief town of the Kokang area) (r:zd:11625/ts:5105) (q:draft)
laulo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:unafraid/fearless/without fear) (d:<lau>, afraid, and <lo>, not, written as one word; {laulo in} is without fear) (j:lau/lo) (r:zd:21389/zd:20092/zd:17549) (q:draft)
lauthawnggawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:panic/be terrified) (d:<lauthawng>, be struck with fear, and <gawp>, severely, written as one word: be badly frightened, panic; often paired with <patau>) (j:lauthawng/gawp) (r:zd:16595/zd:14875/zd:13063) (q:draft)
lauthawngsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:frighten/threaten/intimidate/scare) (d:<lauthawng>, sudden fear, with the causative <sak>: make someone afraid, threaten, as with a knife or with a false bomb warning) (s:lausak) (b:lauthawng) (r:zd:19100/zd:16811/zd:20132) (q:draft)
lawhcinglo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/work) (w:unsuccessful/failing) (d:<lawhcing> succeed and <lo> not written as one word: not succeed, fail; {a lawhcinglo te} are those who fail) (j:lawhcing/lo) (r:zd:21502/zd:23157) (q:draft)
lawhcingte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/work) (w:successful people/the successful) (d:<lawhcing>, succeed, with the plural <te>: those who succeed, mostly as {mi lawhcingte}) (b:lawhcing) (r:zd:16340/zd:16625/zd:21568) (q:draft)
lawhcinna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/everyday) (w:success/achievement) (d:<lawhcin>, succeed, with the noun suffix <na>: success, what a person has achieved) (b:lawhcin) (r:zd:20805/zd:16340) (q:draft)
lawhphei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:spread to/spread across/catch) (d:of fire, disease, an earthquake or bad conduct: pass sideways onto what is near, as <kilawh> is spread; {kilawhphei} is used in the same way) (r:zd:18947/zd:11738/zd:14575) (q:draft)
lawhsam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:fail/be unsuccessful) (d:not achieve what was aimed at; the form <lawhsap> is used before endings such as <na>) (a:lawhcing) (r:zd:25227/zd:19975/zd:16340) (q:draft)
lawhsap = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:fail/be unsuccessful) (d:form of <lawhsam>, fail, used before words such as <ni>, <hun> and <loh>; the opposite of <lawhcin>, succeed) (a:lawhcin) (r:zd:21392/zd:25751) (q:draft)
lawhsapna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/work) (w:failure/disappointment) (d:not succeeding in what was aimed at, the opposite of <lawhcinna>, success) (a:lawhcinna) (r:zd:24313/zd:21502/zd:11279) (q:draft)
Lawibual = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel/social) (w:Lawibual) (d:a quarter, <veng>, of the town of Tedim in Chin State) (r:zd:12765/zd:20131) (q:draft)
lawm = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:friend/companion) (d:a friend or companion; {lawm ngaih} is a lover or beloved) (s:lawmpa) (a:gal) (r:20.18.24) (q:draft)
lawm aw = (i:1) (t:intj) (f:everyday/social) (w:my friend/friend) (d:<lawm>, friend, and <aw>, here the calling word placed after the one addressed: used in speech to address a friend or the reader, at the start or end of a sentence) (r:zd:20652/zd:22858) (q:draft)
lawm kingai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/family) (w:lovers/sweethearts/courting couple) (d:<lawm>, friend, and <kingai>, love each other: a young man and woman who are in love and courting but not married, as against <nupa>, husband and wife; with <te> for the plural or a number after it) (r:zd:20730/zd:13072) (q:draft)
lawmaker = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:lawmaker/member of parliament/legislator) (d:the English word used in news reports for a member of a parliament, often placed before the name) (o:English) (r:zd:17677/zd:11459) (q:draft, low confidence)
lawmhoih = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:good friend) (d:<lawm>, friend, with <hoih>, good, written as one word: a good friend) (j:lawm/hoih) (r:zd:21085/zd:19841/zd:23902) (q:draft)
lawmit = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:dear friend/beloved friend/close friend) (d:<lawm> friend and <it> love as one word: a friend one holds dear) (r:zd:25097/zd:21432/zd:21355) (q:draft)
lawmlegual = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:friends/companions/peers) (d:<lawm>, friend, <le>, and, and <gual>, here one's peers, written as one word: friends and companions as a group) (j:lawm/le/gual) (r:zd:24276/zd:21667/zd:22683) (q:draft)
lawmlehgual = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:friends/friends and companions/peers) (d:<lawm>, friend, <leh>, and, and <gual>, here peer or companion, written as one word: one's friends and companions taken together) (j:lawm/leh/gual) (r:zd:17309/zd:14720) (q:draft)
lawmngaih = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/family) (w:lover/sweetheart/boyfriend/girlfriend) (d:<lawm>, friend, with <ngaih>, beloved: the person one is in love with and courting) (r:zd:9231/zd:11714/zd:21432) (q:draft)
lawmngaihnu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/family) (w:girlfriend/sweetheart) (d:<lawmngaih>, sweetheart, with <nu> for a woman: the girl or woman someone is in love with) (b:lawmngaih) (r:zd:16133/zd:19425) (q:draft)
lawmngaihpa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/family) (w:boyfriend/lover/sweetheart) (d:<lawmngaih>, sweetheart, with <pa> marking a man: the man a woman loves; the woman is <lawmngaihnu>) (b:lawmngaih) (r:zd:20854/zd:24056) (q:draft)
lawmten = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:friends) (d:<lawmte>, friends, with <n>, the short form of <in> that marks the doer of the action, written as one word) (j:lawmte/n) (r:zd:23556/zd:23148) (q:draft)
lawn = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:throw/cast/hurl) (d:throw something or someone away from oneself, into or onto a place) (s:lot) (q:draft)
lawngkhat = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:social) (w:in unison/as one) (d:in one channel or one stream; {lawngkhat in luangkhawm} is flow together as one, and {awkhat lawngkhat} is with one voice, in unison) (r:zd:22557/zd:20971/zd:21369) (q:draft)
lawphuai = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/social) (w:exciting/enjoyable/inspiring) (d:<lawp>, eager, with <huai>: making people eager and glad, exciting to take part in) (b:lawp) (r:zd:12688/zd:24814) (q:draft)
lawptak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:eagerly/enthusiastically/gladly) (d:<lawp>, eager, with <tak> written as one word, usually followed by <in>: eagerly, with enthusiasm) (s:lawptakin) (j:lawp/tak) (r:zd:24574/zd:18121/zd:13011) (q:draft)
lawyer = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/work) (w:lawyer/attorney) (o:English) (r:zd:11452/zd:23329) (q:draft)
le gual = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:social/everyday) (w:and companions/and peers) (d:<le>, and, with <gual>, here one of the same rank or age, a peer: the second half of the fixed pair {lawm le gual}, friends and companions, friends of every kind; it stands after <lawm>, friend) (r:zd:20860/zd:23797) (q:draft)
le hangh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:if we) (d:<le>, here a short form of <leh>, if, and <hangh>, we including the hearer: placed after a verb at the end of a clause, if we do it; the clause that follows says what then holds or is seen) (r:zd:16243/zd:17374/zd:17976) (q:draft)
lead = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media) (w:lead/lead guitar) (d:the lead part in a music band, usually the lead guitar; {lead tum} is play lead) (o:English) (r:zd:20920) (q:draft, low confidence)
lead = (i:2) (t:n) (f:health/work) (w:lead) (d:the heavy metal lead, named as a poison) (o:English) (r:zd:11860) (q:draft, low confidence)
Lecturer = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:lecturer/university teacher) (o:English) (r:zd:15624/ts:3375) (q:draft)
leengla = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:guest/visitor) (d:often paired as {zin le leengla}, guests and strangers; {zin le leengla do} is to show hospitality) (s:zin/zinpa) (a:innteek) (q:draft)
leh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:and) (d:joins words and phrases; also written <le>) (s:le)
leh = (i:3) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:if/when) (d:placed after the verb of a clause to make it a condition; {bang hang hiam cih leh}, literally if one asks why, means because) (s:aleh/le) (r:1.4.15) (q:term added from the example, Genesis 4.15)
leh apawlte = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:politics/social) (w:and associates/and company/and allies/and followers) (d:<leh>, and, with {a pawlte}, his group, from <pawl>: placed after the name of a person or country, that one together with the people or countries on the same side) (r:zd:23792/zd:14734) (q:draft)
lehbulh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:reverse/invert/put the wrong way round) (d:put two things in the opposite order or place; {ki lehbulh} is be reversed, be the opposite of each other, contradict) (r:zd:25467/zd:15996/zd:20406) (q:draft)
lehkik = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:turn back/return) (d:turn round and go back, usually after the prefix <ki>, as in <kilehkik>; said of people and of an aircraft returning to where it took off) (r:zd:23054/zd:22618) (q:draft)
lehkik = (i:2) (t:v) (f:education) (w:translate back/translate) (d:turn a text from another language back into Zolai) (r:zd:25478) (q:draft, low confidence)
lehlah = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:if on the other hand/and if) (d:<leh>, if, with the emphatic <lah>, written as one word after a verb: if on the other hand, and then again if; often after <kei>, as {om kei lehlah}, and if there is none) (j:leh/lah) (r:zd:16148/zd:19816) (q:draft, low confidence)
lehzong = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:even if/even though) (d:<leh>, if, and <zong>, also, written as one word and placed after a verb: even if that is so) (j:leh/zong) (r:zd:24276/zd:25919) (q:draft)
lei = (i:3) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:buy) (r:zai:buy) (q:draft)
leibat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:debt) (d:money that is owed; {leibat nei} is be in debt and {leibat loh} is pay a debt) (s:leiba) (r:zd:19462/zd:16317/zd:23904) (q:draft)
leiding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:to buy/will buy) (d:<lei>, buy, and <ding> written as one word: to buy, going to buy, something to be bought) (j:lei/ding) (r:zd:25616/zd:24530) (q:draft)
Leilum = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua) (f:travel/social) (w:Leilum) (d:a quarter of Tedim town, called both <veng>, quarter, and <khua>, village, in the articles) (r:zd:22586) (q:draft, low confidence)
leisai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature) (w:loose earth/soil/heap of earth) (d:loose earth or soil, as on a grave, at a roadside or in a landslide) (r:zd:20155/zd:15781) (q:draft, low confidence)
leisawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work) (w:plan to buy/seek to buy) (d:<lei>, buy, and <sawm>, intend, written as one word: intend or try to buy; common in headlines) (j:lei/sawm) (r:zd:11329/zd:21567) (q:draft)
leisungah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:nature) (w:in the ground/underground/into the soil) (d:<leisung> with the place marker <ah> written as one word: in or into the ground) (j:leisung/ah) (r:zd:17335/zd:19875) (q:draft)
leitangh = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature) (j:leitang) (r:zd:20747/zd:18086) (q:draft)
leitawh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/nature) (w:against the ground/with earth) (d:<lei>, ground, and <tawh>, with, written as one word: with or against the ground, with earth) (j:lei/tawh) (r:zd:21248/zd:26124/zd:12450) (q:draft)
leitawh = (i:2) (t:n) (f:travel/nature) (w:south) (d:south, in {leitawh lam}, the south or the southern part; the dictionary writes {leitaw lam}) (r:zd:20730) (q:draft, low confidence)
Leitawhtan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel) (w:Leitawhtan) (d:a place by Tedim town in Chin State; the name means a cutting dug through the earth, and one article uses it for the Panama Canal) (r:zd:22577/zd:24280) (q:draft)
leitawi = (i:2) (t:v) (f:work/social) (w:borrow) (d:take something on loan, to be paid back later; said of what one does for another person it also means give on loan, lend) (q:draft)
leitawisak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/social) (w:lend) (d:<leitawi>, borrow, with the causative <sak>: let someone borrow, lend) (a:leitawi) (b:leitawi) (q:draft)
leitawlam = (i:1) (t:n) (c:direction) (f:travel/nature) (w:south/southern part) (d:<leitaw>, south, with <lam>, side or direction: the south, the southern part of a country, or southward) (s:leitaw/khanglam) (a:leilulam) (j:leitaw/lam) (r:zd:13125/zd:19786/zd:17474) (q:draft)
leithei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work) (w:can buy/be able to buy) (d:<lei> buy and <thei> able, written as one word; {ki leithei} is it can be bought, is on sale) (j:lei/thei) (r:zd:23528/zd:14531/zd:14577) (q:draft)
leitheih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:be able to buy/can be bought) (d:<lei>, buy, and <theih>, be able, written as one word; {leitheih nadingin} is so that it can be bought, and {leitheih hilo} is it cannot be bought) (j:lei/theih) (r:zd:14577/zd:16205/zd:19558) (q:draft)
leitolh = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature) (w:landslide/landslip) (d:<lei>, earth, with <tolh>, slip out: a slide of earth down a slope; often written <mencim leitolh>) (r:zd:20155/zd:20582) (q:draft)
leitung galpi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:world war) (d:<leitung>, world, and <galpi>, great war: a world war; a number or ordinal follows, as in {leitung galpi nihna}, the Second World War) (r:zd:22046/zd:17990) (q:draft)
leitung gambup = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/media) (w:the whole world/worldwide) (d:<leitung>, world, and <gambup>, the whole land: the whole world; mostly with <ah> as {leitung gambup ah}, worldwide, in all the world, before a statement of rank or number) (r:zd:24500/zd:24369) (q:draft)
leitung khantohna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:progress of the world/modern development/worldly advancement) (d:<leitung>, world, and <khantohna>, progress: the advance of the modern world in knowledge, technology and living, the progress of the times; often followed by <tawh> or <hang>, in keeping with it or because of it) (r:zd:24022/ts:3375/zd:9447) (q:draft)
leitung khuahun = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/nature) (w:world situation/world affairs/global climate) (d:<leitung>, the world, and <khuahun>, weather or the state of things: the condition of the world, either the course of world affairs, as in {leitung khuahun luanzia}, or the climate of the earth, as in {leitung khuahun kikhelna}, climate change) (r:zd:23992/zd:23729) (q:draft)
leitung pilna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:secular knowledge/science/worldly learning) (d:<leitung>, the world, and <pilna>, knowledge or wisdom: the learning of the world, that is science and school education, often set against the knowledge of God or against money) (r:zd:9430/zd:16254) (q:draft)
leitung tangthu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education/social) (w:world history/history of the world) (d:<leitung>, the world, and <tangthu>, story or history: the history of the world; often followed by <ah> or <sungah>, in world history) (r:zd:20667/zd:26026) (q:draft)
leitungaa = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/social) (w:of the world/in the world) (d:<leitung>, world, with <aa>, of, written as one word: belonging to or found in the world, as in {leitungaa mihau belpa}, the richest man in the world) (j:leitung/aa) (r:zd:22922/zd:19683) (q:draft)
leitungbuppi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:the whole world/all the world) (d:<leitung> and <buppi> written as one word: the whole world, all its countries and people) (s:leitungbup) (j:leitung/buppi) (r:zd:23821/zd:15637/zd:23975) (q:draft)
leitungin = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/social) (w:the world/the whole world) (d:<leitung> and <in> written as one word: the world or the people of the world as the doer of the action) (j:leitung/in) (r:zd:23754/zd:19168) (q:draft)
lel = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:lose/be defeated) (d:lose to an enemy or an opponent, the opposite of <zo>, win; {gal lel} is lose a war; the form <lelh> is used before some endings) (s:guallel/kizo) (a:zo/gualzo) (q:draft)
lelah = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:when/if) (d:<le>, if or when, and the emphatic <lah> written as one word after a verb or clause: when that is so, then; used in proverbs that set one case against another) (j:le/lah) (r:zd:19441/zd:14861) (q:draft, low confidence)
lelding = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:will just/will simply) (d:<lel>, merely, and <ding>, will, written as one word after a verb: will just do so, will simply happen) (j:lel/ding) (r:zd:17395/zd:10687) (q:draft)
lemlo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:not convenient/not suitable/not workable) (d:<lem>, here be convenient or fitting, and <lo>, not, written as one word; after a verb with <ding>, it is not convenient or not possible to do it) (j:lem/lo) (r:zd:24594/ts:7133) (q:draft)
lemlohna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:disagreement/difficulty/inconvenience) (d:<lem>, go well or be agreeable, with <lohna>: something that does not go well, a disagreement between people or a difficulty that hinders a plan; {ki lemlohna} is discord between people) (r:zd:11504/zd:23594/zd:15023) (q:draft)
lemlote = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:those unable/those for whom it does not work out) (d:<lem>, here be convenient or work out, with <lote> written as one word: those for whom something is not possible or does not go well) (j:lem/lote) (r:zd:23709) (q:draft, low confidence)
lemna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:peace/reconciliation) (d:being on good terms with one another; mostly written after <ki> as {ki lemna}, which is <kilemna>; {lemna bawl} is make peace) (s:kilemna) (r:zd:23984/zd:20682/zd:21125) (q:draft)
lemtang = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:convenient/smooth/favourable/go well) (d:working out easily and without hindrance, of a time, a plan or an affair; also as a verb, go well, become easy) (r:zd:12567/zd:10743/zd:20899) (q:draft)
lemzaw = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:more convenient/easier/handier) (d:<lem>, here convenient or suitable, and <zaw>, more, written as one word; the Bible text has <lem> only in the sense repair) (j:lem/zaw) (r:zd:24765/zd:25824/zd:12441) (q:draft)
leng hoih = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:it is good to/it would be good if/should) (d:<leng>, if, and <hoih>, good: placed after a verb to give advice, it is good to do so, one should do so; {kei leng hoih} after the verb advises against it, and {leng hoih pen hi} is it is best to) (r:zd:21417/zd:22413/zd:25909) (q:draft)
leng kilawm = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:it would be fitting to/ought to/might well) (d:<leng>, if I or if we, and <kilawm>, fitting: placed after a verb, it would be right or likely that I or we do so, I had better, I may well; often followed by <sa> and <ing>, I think it fitting) (r:zd:21925/zd:23037) (q:draft, low confidence)
lengkhiading = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:will take off/will fly out) (d:<lengkhia> with <ding>, will, written as one word; here in the sense fly off: of an aircraft or a traveller, will depart by air; also be about to leap out) (j:lengkhia/ding) (r:zd:13157/zd:11627) (q:draft)
lengla = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (j:leengla) (r:zd:25178/zd:25192/zd:22773) (q:draft)
lenglang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:dangling/hanging loose/swinging) (d:describes a thing that hangs free in the air, mostly after <kikhai>: {kikhai lenglang} is hang dangling) (r:zd:19763/zd:14662) (q:draft)
lengleng = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/nature) (w:fly about/keep flying) (d:the verb <leng>, fly, also written <leeng>, said twice: fly on and on or fly about) (r:zd:25346) (q:draft)
lengleng = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:trailing along/dangling/on and on) (d:placed after a verb such as <zui>, follow, <kai>, pull, <kikhai>, hang, or <pai>, go: the action goes on in a trailing or dangling way) (r:zd:20942/zd:14591) (q:draft, low confidence)
lengthei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:be able to fly/can fly) (d:<leng>, fly, and <thei>, able, written as one word: be able to fly, also of people travelling by plane) (j:leng/thei) (r:zd:16210/zd:11197) (q:draft)
lengthei = (i:2) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:aircraft/flying craft) (d:a thing that can fly, such as a plane or a balloon) (j:leng/thei) (r:zd:17293) (q:draft, low confidence)
lenkawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/body) (w:while holding/holding) (d:<len>, hold, and <kawm>, while, written as one word: holding something in the hand while doing something else) (j:len/kawm) (r:zd:15727/zd:14935) (q:draft)
lenlan = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:just/merely/idly) (d:placed after a verb: do only that and nothing more, without care or effort, as in {om lenlan}, just stay there; often said in reproach) (r:zd:19790/zd:15946) (q:draft, low confidence)
lenna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:flight/flying) (d:<leeng>, fly, with the noun suffix <na>: flying, a flight; {vanleng lenna} is the flight of an aircraft) (r:zd:22658) (q:draft, low confidence)
lenna = (i:2) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:place of stay/haunt/abode) (d:the place where someone stays or moves about, often in songs: {ka lenna} is the place where I am staying) (r:zd:23828/zd:20131) (q:draft, low confidence)
LenNupa = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:politics/travel) (w:Lennupa) (d:a scenic place in the land of Kaptel village in the Tedim area of Chin State, mostly written {Lennupa}; the Falam side calls it Buannel and the boundary there is disputed) (r:zd:20550/zd:20513/zd:22547) (q:draft)
Lentang = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua) (f:travel) (w:Lentang) (d:a village and ridge in the Tedim area of Chin State, on a road route toward the India border) (r:zd:20406) (q:draft, low confidence)
leptuah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:settle/reconcile/negotiate/resolve) (d:put right a quarrel or a matter that is at odds, bring two sides or two things into agreement) (r:zd:16900/zd:25461/ts:7133) (q:draft)
lesbian = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:lesbian) (d:a woman who is attracted to women; mostly written with a capital letter and often added to explain {numei leh numei}) (o:English) (r:zd:19472) (q:draft, low confidence)
lesson = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education/everyday) (w:lesson) (d:something learned from an event or from experience; {lesson la} is learn a lesson) (o:English) (r:zd:22492/zd:20260) (q:draft)
letsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/body) (w:take hold of/grab/grasp) (d:<let>, a form of <len>, hold, with <sak>: take hold of something of another person, such as the hand, or seize a thing from someone) (j:let/sak) (r:zd:20944/zd:12021) (q:draft)
letsong = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:gift/present) (d:something given to honor or please a person; {letsong pia} is give a gift) (s:piakkhong) (r:20.18.16) (q:draft)
leu = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:again/in turn) (d:written twice after a verb, {leu leu}, which is <leuleu> written as two words: again, in turn) (r:zd:11323/zd:11367/zd:23037) (q:draft)
leulau = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (d:descriptive word placed after a verb: lying or left there limp and still, said of a body lying on the ground, a part cut off or a vehicle overturned) (r:zd:14689/zd:22267) (q:draft, low confidence)
leuleu = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:again) (d:placed after a verb: once more, another time) (s:kik/kikkik)
leuleuding = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/time) (w:will again/will in turn) (d:<leuleu> and <ding> written as one word after a verb: the action will happen once more, or in its turn) (j:leuleu/ding) (r:zd:12271/zd:20387/zd:11997) (q:draft)
level = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/education) (w:level/rank/grade) (d:a level in an order of ranks or grades, as of government, of an organisation or of study; mostly after the word that names it, as in {State level}) (o:English) (r:zd:22586/zd:16442/zd:25130) (q:draft)
Lezang = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua) (f:travel) (w:Lezang) (d:a Zomi village, listed with villages of the Tedim and Tonzang area of Chin State; written after the name of a person to show the home village) (r:zd:21182) (q:draft)
lezong = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:even if/even though/although) (d:<le>, if, and <zong>, also, written as one word after the verb of a clause: even if, even though) (j:le/zong) (r:zd:13340/zd:21351/zd:24276) (q:draft)
Lia = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:Miss) (d:title written before the name of a girl or an unmarried young woman, as {Tg} is written before the name of a young man) (r:zd:24349/zd:25288) (q:draft)
liamliam = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:barely/only just/narrowly) (d:placed after a verb: the thing does happen, but only just, with nothing to spare; {suakta liamliam} is escape narrowly) (r:zd:16245/zd:25105/zd:20264) (q:draft)
liamna ngah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health/politics) (w:be wounded/be injured/get hurt) (d:<liamna>, a wound, and <ngah>, get: receive an injury, be wounded in fighting or in an accident; stands after the person or the number of persons hurt, and reports set it beside <si>, die) (s:liam) (r:zd:17703/zd:11229/ts:10413) (q:draft)
liamngawh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health) (w:be seriously injured/be badly hurt) (d:be wounded severely; said of the injured in accidents and attacks) (b:liam) (r:zd:14509/zd:14899/zd:12405) (q:draft)
liamsanta = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:pass away) (d:<liam>, here go out of sight, with <san>, here leaving others behind, and <ta>, now; in {mual liamsanta}, has gone beyond the hill and left us, a respectful way of saying that someone has died) (r:zd:10688) (q:draft)
lian = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:large) (d:big in size) (s:gol/lianpi) (a:neu)
liana = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:exactly/just/precisely) (d:<lian>, exactly, with a following <a>, placed after the word it stresses: {ahi bang liana} is exactly as it is; the same spelling is also part of personal names) (r:zd:24303/zd:24029) (q:draft, low confidence)
lianding = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/time) (w:just about to/on the point of) (d:placed after a verb, formed with <ding>, will: on the very point of doing or suffering something; {alenkhia lianding} is just about to take off) (r:zd:13030/zd:16164/zd:12061) (q:draft, low confidence)
lianga = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:to the point of/so much that) (d:<liang>, even, with the linking <a>, written as one word after a verb or clause: to the point of, so far that; {ihmu lo lianga} is to the point of not sleeping) (j:liang/a) (r:zd:10963/ts:4831/zd:26585) (q:draft)
liangding = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:to the point of/so much as to) (d:<liang.2>, even, and <ding> written as one word, mostly as {liangding in} after a verb: so far as to do it; {sihlawh liangding} is so as to die of it) (j:liang/ding) (r:zd:15437/zd:15260) (q:draft)
lianghi = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:<liang> even, to the point of, and the sentence ending <hi> written as one word at the end of a sentence: it went so far as that, said with surprise or emphasis) (j:liang/hi) (r:zd:19127/zd:15387) (q:draft)
liangko kikim = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:social/politics) (w:equality/on equal footing/equal standing) (d:<liangko>, shoulder, and <kikim>, equal: with shoulders level, an idiom for equality of rank and rights between peoples or between women and men; with <in>, <zahin> or <takaa> after it, on an equal footing) (r:zd:20930/zd:19612/zd:20772) (q:draft)
lianlo = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:not exactly/not quite/not really) (d:<lian> and <lo>, not, written as one word after a verb: not exactly, not quite, not really so; <lian> is here the word that stresses exactness, not the word for large) (j:lian/lo) (r:zd:15636/zd:23904/zd:8668) (q:draft)
lianmahmah = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:very large/huge/very serious) (d:<lian>, large, and <mahmah>, very, written as one word and placed after the noun: very big, or of a matter or injury very serious) (j:lian/mahmah) (r:zd:12194/zd:12854/zd:12290) (q:draft)
Lianpitawh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:social) (w:with great/with much) (d:<lianpi>, great, and <tawh>, with, written as one word after a noun: {dahpihna lianpitawh}, with deep sympathy, closes a message of condolence, and {zahtakna lianpitawh} is with great respect) (j:lianpi/tawh) (r:zd:20782) (q:draft)
liausakthei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/work) (w:can be fined/may be made to pay) (d:<liausak>, make pay a fine, and <thei>, can, written as one word; mostly after <ki> and an amount: a fine of that sum can be imposed) (j:liausak/thei) (r:zd:16919/zd:15848) (q:draft)
Liberal = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:politics/religion) (w:liberal) (d:liberal in politics or in theology, the opposite of conservative; {liberal upna} is liberal belief) (o:English) (r:zd:23479/zd:21272/zd:22873) (q:draft)
Licence = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/travel) (w:licence/permit) (d:an official paper that allows a person to do something, as drive a vehicle or run a business, the English word; {Driving Licence} is a driving licence) (o:English) (r:zd:20534/zd:11913/zd:16592) (q:draft)
license = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/politics) (w:licence/permit) (d:an official paper that allows a person to do, keep or use something, also called <phalna>, permission) (o:English) (r:zd:16682/zd:14820) (q:draft)
Lieutenant = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:lieutenant) (d:an army rank; also the first word of the rank Lieutenant Colonel) (o:English) (r:zd:25097/ts:4309) (q:draft)
Lift = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/travel) (w:lift/elevator) (d:the machine that carries people up and down inside a tall building) (o:English) (r:zd:17143/zd:14954) (q:draft)
like = (i:1) (t:n) (f:it/media) (w:like) (d:a like given to a post or a page on Facebook and other social media; {like pia} is to give a like and {like ngah} to get one) (o:English) (r:zd:23148/zd:25139) (q:draft)
liklek = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:brand/quite/very) (d:intensifying word placed after a describing word, most often <thak>, new: {thak liklek} is brand new; also {tom liklek}, very short) (r:zd:16724/zd:22040) (q:draft)
limet = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media) (w:watch with interest/enjoy watching) (d:look at something with pleasure or close attention, <lim>, here well, with <et>, look; {ki limet mahmah} is it was much watched, said of a popular video) (r:zd:15579/zd:16410) (q:draft)
limgen = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/media) (w:emphasise/stress/speak much of) (d:speak of something earnestly and at length, give it weight; {ki limgen} is be much talked about) (r:zd:24396/zd:20771/zd:21803) (q:draft)
limit = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:limit) (d:the point or amount that may not be passed) (s:ciangtan) (o:English) (r:zd:20928/zd:21783) (q:draft)
limlak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/social) (w:act/portray/show/demonstrate) (d:<lim>, image, with <lak>, show: show something as a picture of it, act a part on stage or in film, or show plainly by what one does) (r:zd:9222/zd:16640) (q:draft)
limlak = (i:2) (t:n) (f:media) (w:photo/picture) (d:a picture taken or shown of someone or something, a photograph) (s:lim) (r:zd:21365/ts:4134) (q:draft)
limlim = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:whatsoever/at all/any) (d:placed after a noun or clause: any that is such, whatever is called so, without exception; after a verb it presses the statement, by all means, in every case) (r:zd:14704/zd:12998/zd:22860) (q:draft)
limlo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:food/health) (w:tasteless/not tasty/unappetising) (d:<lim> in its sense tasty, with <lo>, not: of food, not tasting good; {ankam limlo} is having no appetite, a sign of illness) (r:zd:12436/zd:24365/zd:22065) (q:draft)
limsiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:be badly damaged/be wrecked) (d:be badly damaged, said of vehicles and buildings after a crash, fire or earthquake: <siat>, be ruined, with a first part that strengthens the verb, as in other words for severe harm) (r:zd:12113/zd:15089/zd:12837) (q:draft)
limsuai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education/media) (w:draw/paint/sketch) (d:<lim>, picture, with <suai>, draw: make a picture or a plan by drawing or painting; {limsuai siam} is skilled at drawing, an artist) (r:zd:19166/zd:22988) (q:draft)
limsuai = (i:2) (t:n) (f:media/work) (w:painter/artist) (d:a person who draws or paints pictures) (r:zd:9264/zd:17466) (q:draft, low confidence)
limsuaih = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education/media) (w:painting/drawing) (d:the making of pictures as an art or skill, from <lim>, picture, and <suaih>, draw; {limsuaih siam} is a skilled painter, an artist) (r:zd:23037/zd:20317/zd:9264) (q:draft)
limzat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:use widely/use much/favour) (d:use a thing much and gladly; with <ki>, {ki limzat mahmah}, be very widely used, be popular) (r:zd:22686/ts:7364/zd:20920) (q:draft)
line = (i:1) (t:n) (f:it/travel) (w:line/connection) (d:a telephone, power or pipe line, and the connection it gives: {phone line} is the telephone network; {Line Car} is a bus that runs a regular route) (o:English) (r:zd:22394/zd:15338/zd:24271) (q:draft)
lingpak = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (f:nature) (w:rose) (d:<ling>, thorn, with <pak>, flower: the rose) (j:ling/pak) (r:zd:16254/zd:23729) (q:draft)
Lingthuk = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua) (f:travel) (w:Lingthuk) (d:a Zomi village in Chin State, Myanmar; written after a personal name it tells the home village of the person) (r:zd:22877) (q:draft)
link = (i:1) (t:n) (f:it) (w:link) (d:an address on the internet that opens a page or file when it is pressed) (o:English) (r:zd:12948/zd:19430) (q:draft)
linnliann = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (j:linlian) (r:zd:17060/zd:20176/zd:21590) (q:draft)
list = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/work) (w:list) (d:a written list of names or items) (s:sazian) (o:English) (r:zd:11224/zd:20968) (q:draft)
litre = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/food) (w:litre/liter) (d:the metric unit for measuring liquids) (o:English) (r:zd:20588/zd:20831/zd:22650) (q:draft)
liuleu = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:completely/clean off/outright) (d:placed after a verb of cutting off, separating, overturning or dying: the thing is wholly severed or lies there finished) (r:zd:22540/zd:13159) (q:draft, low confidence)
Live = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/it) (w:live broadcast/live stream) (d:a broadcast or video stream shown while the event happens, mostly on Facebook; {Live in khah} is broadcast live) (o:English) (r:zd:17788/zd:24226) (q:draft)
lo = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:not) (d:negative word placed after a verb or describing word: {nei lo} is not have, {om lo} is not be there)
lo = (i:2) (t:n) (f:work/nature) (w:farm/field) (d:a piece of land that is worked to grow crops)
loan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:loan) (d:money borrowed that is to be paid back, in the articles mostly a student loan or a loan to a government) (s:leitawi) (o:English) (r:zd:20545/zd:23787) (q:draft, low confidence)
Lobby = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/home) (w:lobby/entrance hall) (d:the entrance hall of a hotel, hospital, apartment block or other large building) (o:English) (r:zd:14568/zd:17661) (q:draft)
lockdown = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/politics) (w:lockdown) (d:the closing of a town or country and the order to stay at home, as during the Covid-19 epidemic; {lockdown bawl} is to impose it) (o:English) (r:zd:23825/zd:24019) (q:draft)
lockup = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/social) (w:lockup/police cell/detention cell) (d:the cells of a police station, in Malaysia, where a person is held after arrest; named after the station, as in {Jinjang lockup}) (o:English) (r:zd:23709/zd:11706/zd:21282) (q:draft)
loding = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:will not/shall not) (d:<lo>, not, and <ding>, will, written as one word after a verb: will not, is not going to; at the end of a rule it means must not) (j:lo/ding) (r:zd:19556/zd:22888/zd:15958) (q:draft)
Logo = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/work) (w:logo/emblem) (d:the emblem or symbol of a party, company or organisation) (o:English) (r:zd:24607/zd:10743/zd:17630) (q:draft)
loh hangin = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:although not/even though not/even if not) (d:<loh>, the negative after a verb, and <hangin>, although: placed after a verb, although that is not so; the main statement follows, often with <veve>, still) (r:zd:22849/zd:21254/zd:23758) (q:draft)
loh nadingin = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:so that not/in order not to/lest) (d:<loh>, the negative form used before an ending, and <nadingin>, so that: placed after a verb, it states the thing that the following action is meant to prevent, so that it does not happen) (r:zd:23729/zd:25355/zd:24037) (q:draft)
loh phamawh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:must/have to/cannot but) (d:<loh>, not doing, and <phamawh>, serious: placed after a verb in its second form, not to do it would be serious, so it must be done; {tai loh phamawh} is have to flee) (r:zd:23057/zd:24240/zd:16441) (q:draft)
lohding = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:not to/so as not to) (d:<loh> and <ding> written as one word after a verb: that the thing not be done or not happen; {lohding thupi hi} is it is important not to, {lohding in} is so as not to) (j:loh/ding) (r:zd:12115/zd:18943/zd:13314) (q:draft)
lohhang = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:although not/even though not) (d:<loh> and <hang> written as one word after a verb, with or without <in>: even though it is not so or was not done) (j:loh/hang) (r:zd:12267/zd:12057/zd:25932) (q:draft)
lohi = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:not) (d:<lo>, not, and the sentence ending <hi> written as one word: closes a negative statement, is not, does not) (j:lo/hi) (r:zd:23551/zd:20905/zd:23492) (q:draft)
lohman = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:because not) (d:<loh> and <man> written as one word after a verb, with or without <in>: because it is not so or was not done) (j:loh/man) (r:zd:25178/zd:12068/zd:21134) (q:draft)
lohna dingin = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:so that not/lest) (d:<lohna>, the not doing, and <dingin>, in order to: placed after a verb, so that it does not happen, in order not to; the negative of <nadingin>) (r:zd:21458/zd:9141) (q:draft)
lohna hangin = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:because of not/for not) (d:<lohna>, the noun form of the negative, and <hangin>, because of: placed after a verb, because of not doing or not being so; the clause that follows gives the result) (r:zd:21845/zd:20418) (q:draft)
lohnading = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/work) (w:in order to pay off/to repay) (d:<loh>, pay off, with <nading>, written as one word: in order to pay a debt, as in {leibat lohnading}) (j:loh/nading) (r:zd:15651) (q:draft)
lohnading = (i:2) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:so as not to/not to) (d:the negative <loh> with <nading>, written as one word after a verb: for not doing, so that it is not done; usually written {loh nading}) (j:loh/nading) (r:zd:17955) (q:draft, low confidence)
Loikaw = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel/politics) (w:Loikaw) (d:capital of Kayah State in eastern Myanmar) (r:zd:14609/ts:4379) (q:draft)
lokhopa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:farmer) (d:<lokho>, farm, with <pa> for a man: a man who works the land)
lokuan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/nature) (w:go to the field/work in the fields/farm) (d:<lo>, field, with <kuan>, set out: go out to work in the fields; also said of the person who does so, a field worker) (j:lo/kuan) (r:zd:23797/zd:25075/zd:15228) (q:draft)
Lombok = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel) (w:Lombok) (d:island of Indonesia, east of Bali) (r:zd:20582/zd:17733) (q:draft)
lomlom = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/social) (w:in groups/in flocks/in bunches) (d:<lom>, bundle, doubled, mostly as {a lomlom in}: group by group, many together) (b:lom) (r:zd:22305/zd:22758) (q:draft)
London = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel/politics) (w:London) (d:capital city of England and of the United Kingdom) (r:zd:13009/zd:23975/zd:21649) (q:draft)
longkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:pry off/wrench out/pull out/uproot) (d:force something loose from the place where it is fixed and take it out, as nails, a window grille, a wheel or a plant with its root; the second part is <khia>, out) (r:zd:19816/zd:22046/zd:17779) (q:draft)
Lorry = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/work) (w:lorry/truck) (d:a large motor vehicle that carries goods, often said together with <mawtawpi>) (o:English) (r:zd:17816/zd:12761) (q:draft)
losan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:firecracker/fireworks) (d:a firecracker, and fireworks of any kind set off at festivals) (r:zd:15978/zd:17558) (q:draft)
losiah = (i:1) (t:prep) (f:everyday) (w:except/apart from/other than) (d:placed after the thing excepted: all but that one) (s:simloh) (r:zd:20547/zd:25346/zd:24544) (q:draft)
Lotdaw = (i:1) (t:name) (f:politics) (w:Hluttaw/parliament) (d:the parliament of Myanmar, its house of representatives; also written {Lutdaw}) (o:Burmese, hluttaw) (r:zd:16087/zd:24164) (q:draft)
lothangkang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food) (w:garlic) (d:{lothang} with <kang>, white: garlic; {lothang san} or <lothangsan>, the red one, is onion) (r:zd:24276/zd:24501) (q:draft)
lothangsan = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (f:food) (w:onion/red onion) (d:the onion, the red bulb used in cooking; named beside <lothangkang>, garlic) (r:zd:20959/zd:23729/zd:25115) (q:draft)
lotngah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education) (w:memorize/learn by heart) (d:fix something in the memory so that it can be said without looking) (r:zd:20968) (q:draft)
Lottery = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/everyday) (w:lottery) (d:a draw in which a prize of money, or a visa as in the American DV Lottery, goes to tickets or names picked by chance) (o:English) (r:zd:22076/zd:17504) (q:draft)
Louisville = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel) (w:Louisville) (d:city in Kentucky, United States, where a Zomi community lives) (r:zd:15805/zd:9217) (q:draft)
lovegift = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:love gift/gift of money/honorarium) (d:a gift of money given out of thanks to a preacher, singer or other servant of the church) (o:English, love gift) (r:zd:25572/zd:19451) (q:draft)
luailuai = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:on and on/merely) (d:placed after a verb: keep on doing it and nothing more, just go along doing it without thought or aim) (r:zd:24411/zd:15894) (q:draft, low confidence)
luaksuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health) (w:feel sick/be nauseous/vomit) (d:feel like vomiting, or vomit; named among the signs of illness, of pregnancy and of travel sickness) (r:zd:20433/zd:19593) (q:draft)
lualo = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:not very/not so much) (d:<lua>, very or too much, and <lo>, not, written as one word after a verb or describing word: not very, not much) (j:lua/lo) (r:zd:18927/zd:21180/zd:24276) (q:draft)
luamahmah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:extremely/far too/very much) (d:<lua> and <mahmah> written as one word: placed after a describing word or verb, to a very great or excessive degree) (j:lua/mahmah) (r:zd:14648/zd:15890/zd:11837) (q:draft)
luanglet = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:overflow/go to excess/be extreme) (d:<luang>, flow, with <let.1>, overflow: run over; in the articles used of people or views that go beyond the proper measure, as {a luanglet te}, the extremists) (r:zd:25312/zd:22369/zd:22592) (q:draft, low confidence)
luangphamna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/work) (w:death benefit) (d:money that a community association or its insurance fund pays to the family when a member dies) (r:zd:25265/zd:25789) (q:draft, low confidence)
luankhi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (w:tears/tear) (d:tears, a word of songs and poetic writing; {luankhi nul} is wipe away tears) (s:khitui) (r:zd:22095/zd:15874/zd:12033) (q:draft)
luanzia = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/nature) (w:course/flow/trend) (d:<luan>, flow, with <zia>, manner: the way something flows or runs its course; <khuahun luanzia> is the trend of the times) (s:paizia) (r:zd:24765/zd:25863) (q:draft)
luatman = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:because of too much) (d:<luat> too much and <man>, because, written as one word after a verb or describing word: because one does or is so too much) (j:luat/man) (r:zd:12341/zd:15600) (q:draft)
lubawk = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:head/top leader/chief) (d:the one at the very head, the topmost leader or the top position; {makai lubawk} is the top leader) (r:zd:25026/zd:20823) (q:draft)
lubawk = (i:2) (t:adj) (f:family) (d:in {tagah lubawk}: said of an orphan who lost a parent in infancy or before birth) (r:zd:14930/zd:20808) (q:draft, low confidence)
ludam = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:health) (w:healthy/well) (d:second word of the pair {cidam ludam}, in good health in every way; used in greetings, prayers and blessings) (s:cidam) (r:zd:21141/zd:21421) (q:draft)
Luggage = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:luggage/suitcase/bag) (o:English) (r:zd:21294/zd:12040) (q:draft)
luheek = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:conduct/behaviour/manners) (d:found only as the second word of the pair {gamtat luheek}, with <gamtat>, behave: the way a person acts and carries himself, behaviour and manners) (r:zd:22639/zd:17152) (q:draft)
luhek = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:conduct/behaviour/manners) (d:the way a person carries himself; found after <gamtat> in the pair <gamtat luhek>, conduct and behaviour, character) (r:zd:19900/zd:17896) (q:draft)
lui = (i:2) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:old) (d:old, said of things, customs and times, the opposite of <thak>, new; {hun lui} is the days of old) (a:thak) (r:3.25.22) of objects which are just old
luikhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/social) (w:bring out/bring up/present) (d:bring a matter, a piece of news or a plan out before others, with <khia>, out) (r:zd:11409/zd:21455/zd:16580) (q:draft, low confidence)
luina = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food/social) (w:feast/shared meal) (d:mostly in {ankuang luina}, a meal that people sit down to together, a dinner given for guests) (r:zd:12862/zd:14579) (q:draft, low confidence)
luipang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature) (w:riverbank/riverside/bank of a stream) (d:<lui>, stream, with <pang>, side: the land along the edge of a river or stream) (r:zd:12717/zd:20516) (q:draft)
luisung = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature) (w:river/inside of a river) (d:<lui>, stream or river, with <sung>, inside, written as one word; {luisung ah} is in the river) (j:lui/sung) (r:zd:15389/zd:22609) (q:draft)
lukhu = (i:2) (t:n) (f:home) (w:hat/cap) (r:zai:hat) (q:draft)
lukun = (i:1) (t:v) (f:body/social) (w:bow the head/bow down) (d:<lu>, head, and <kun>, bow, written as one word: bend the head down, in respect, shame or submission) (j:lu/kun) (r:zd:23616/zd:21655/zd:20446) (q:draft)
lum = (i:3) (t:adj) (f:everyday/nature) (w:warm) (d:warm; used with <khua>, the weather or how the body feels: {khua lum} is be warm, keep warm) (a:vot) (r:59.2.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
lumlua = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:nature) (w:too hot/very hot) (d:<lum>, warm or hot, and <lua>, too much, written as one word; mostly of the weather, {khua lumlua}) (j:lum/lua) (r:zd:23018/zd:11236) (q:draft)
Lunch = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food/time) (w:lunch/midday meal) (d:the midday meal, mostly as an item in the programme of a meeting) (o:English) (r:zd:16038) (q:draft, low confidence)
lungdam = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/social) (w:happy/glad/joyful) (d:glad or happy at heart, from <lung>, heart, and <dam>, well) (s:nuam)
lungdam = (i:4) (t:intj) (f:everyday/social) (w:thank you/thanks) (d:said to thank someone; the same word as {lungdam}, glad) (r:zai:thank) (q:draft)
lungdam ing = (i:1) (t:intj) (f:everyday/social) (w:thank you/I am thankful) (d:<lungdam>, be glad, and <ing>, the first person ending: I am glad, the usual way to say thank you; what is thanked for stands before it) (r:zd:17760) (q:draft)
lungdambawl = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion/time) (w:Christmas) (d:<lungdam>, joy, with <bawl>, make: the feast of the birth of Jesus, Christmas; {Lungdambawl ni} is Christmas Day) (r:zd:25472/zd:16506/zd:26385) (q:draft)
lungdamko = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/religion) (w:give thanks/thank) (d:<lungdam>, joy, with <koh>, express, written as one word: give thanks, express gratitude to someone, who is marked with <tungah>) (j:lungdam/koh) (r:zd:23019/zd:16253/zd:22496) (q:draft)
lungdamkoh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:thank/give thanks) (d:express thanks to someone, from <lungdam>, glad, and <koh>, express) (q:draft)
lungdamlua = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/social) (w:overjoyed/very glad/very thankful) (d:<lungdam> glad and <lua> very much, written as one word: very happy; {lungdamlua ung} is we thank you very much) (j:lungdam/lua) (r:zd:20652/zd:15298/zd:20289) (q:draft)
lungdamna lian = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:social) (w:be very grateful/great joy) (d:<lungdamna>, joy or thanks, and <lian>, great: a formula of thanks, the joy is great; the person thanked stands before it with <tungah>, and <mahmah> usually follows, as in {ka lungdamna lian mahmah hi}, I am very grateful) (r:zd:19435/zd:11159) (q:draft)
lungdamnathu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:gospel/good news) (d:<lungdamna> and <thu> written as one word: the good news of Christ, the gospel) (j:lungdamna/thu) (r:zd:25751/zd:22544/zd:25451) (q:draft)
lungdeih = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:heart's desire/wish/will) (d:<lung>, heart, with <deih>, want: what the heart wishes for; frequent in songs and poetic language) (j:lung/deih) (r:zd:21948/zd:25020) (q:draft)
lungduaitak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/social) (w:patiently) (d:<lungduai>, patient, and <tak> written as one word, mostly followed by <in>: patiently, calmly) (s:lungduaitakin) (j:lungduai/tak) (r:zd:20037/zd:20093/zd:18142) (q:draft)
lunggulhhuai = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/social) (w:desirable/to be wished for) (d:<lunggulh>, long for, with <huai>, worthy of: something one would very much like to see or have; {lunggulhhuai ka sa hi} is I find it desirable) (b:lunggulh) (r:zd:25678/zd:10726) (q:draft)
lunghimawhhuai = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/health) (w:worrying/worrisome/alarming) (d:<lunghimawh>, worry, with <huai>, causing: giving cause for worry; of an injured person, in a critical condition) (b:lunghimawh) (r:zd:15103/zd:14939) (q:draft)
lungkimloh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:be dissatisfied/be displeased) (d:<lungkim> be satisfied and <loh> not written as one word: not be content; also the state itself, dissatisfaction, and {lungkimloh lahna} is a protest, a showing of dissatisfaction) (j:lungkim/loh) (r:zd:9434/zd:24579/zd:25924) (q:draft)
lungkimtak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:contentedly/gladly/willingly) (d:<lungkim>, be satisfied, with <tak>, usually followed by <in>: with satisfaction, gladly, to one's content) (j:lungkim/tak) (r:zd:15491/zd:16133/zd:24276) (q:draft)
lunglau = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be anxious/be worried/be alarmed) (d:<lung> and <lau> written as one word: be afraid at heart, worried or alarmed; {lunglau sak} is to alarm someone) (j:lung/lau) (r:zd:25397/zd:25165) (q:draft)
lunglen = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:long for/feel nostalgic/be homesick/miss) (d:feel longing or sadness at heart for a person, place or time that is far away or gone; often paired as {lunglen khuangaih}, and {lunglen huai} is what stirs such longing) (r:zd:23069/zd:26626/zd:22585) (q:draft)
lungleng = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/family) (w:lonely/homesick/wistful) (d:feeling lonely or sad from missing a person, a place or a time; also as a verb, miss or long for) (r:zd:15459/zd:22808/ts:3369) (q:draft)
lunglenna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:longing/loneliness/homesickness/melancholy) (d:a sad longing for a person or place that is far away or lost, often named together with <dahna>, grief) (r:zd:22755/zd:24276/zd:25863) (q:draft)
lunglut = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:be interested/take an interest) (d:<lung>, mind, with <lut>, enter: have the mind drawn to something; <lunglut huai> is interesting) (r:zd:15845/zd:11394/zd:12110) (q:draft)
lunglut huai = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/media) (w:interesting/fascinating) (d:<lunglut>, be interested, with the suffix <huai>, causing that feeling: interesting, worth one's attention; stands before a noun with <a> or ends a statement, often with <mahmah>) (r:zd:17437/zd:22695) (q:draft)
lunglutna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/education) (w:interest/attention/enthusiasm) (d:<lung>, mind, with <lutna>, entering: what the mind goes into, interest in or attention to something) (r:zd:21168/zd:15264) (q:draft)
lunglutte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:those who are interested/interested people) (d:<lunglut>, be interested, with the plural <te>: the people who are interested, usually as {a lunglutte in} in an invitation or notice) (r:zd:19065/zd:23083) (q:draft)
lungneu = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:be discouraged/lose heart/be downhearted/feel hurt) (d:<lung> heart with <neu> small: feel small and low in spirit, be easily hurt or discouraged; {lungneu sak} is make someone feel so) (r:zd:26626/zd:19898/zd:21305) (q:draft)
lungneuna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/health) (w:dejection/low spirits/hurt feelings/melancholy) (d:the state of feeling small and hurt in the heart, downcast or aggrieved; named beside <hehna>, anger, and <lunggimna>, weariness of mind) (r:zd:20801/zd:20778/zd:16376) (q:draft)
lungnote = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/nature) (w:germs/microbes/worms) (d:<lungno> with the plural <te>: small living things such as worms and insects, and in writing about health the germs that cause disease, {natna lungnote}) (b:lungno) (r:zd:19330/zd:22803/zd:21239) (q:draft)
lungpho = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:protest/demonstrate) (d:show opposition in public, as a crowd in the streets; the noun is <lungphona>, a protest) (r:zd:15602/zd:15080/zd:23013) (q:draft)
lungphona = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:protest/demonstration) (d:a public show of anger or disagreement by a crowd; <lungphona nei> is to hold a protest) (b:lungpho) (r:zd:23437/zd:20673/zd:24579) (q:draft)
lungphona kinei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:a protest is held/demonstrate) (d:<lungphona>, protest, and <kinei>, here the passive of <nei>, have or hold: a protest is held, people demonstrate; the place or the cause with <hangin> stands before it, and it often ends a headline) (r:zd:17549/zd:22981) (q:draft)
lungphona nei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:protest/demonstrate/hold a protest) (d:<lungphona>, protest, and <nei>, have: hold a protest or demonstration; the place stands before it with <ah>, the protesters with <in>, and <uh> <hi> may follow) (r:zd:25015/zd:25584) (q:draft)
lungsim cidam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health) (w:mental health/sound mind/healthy mind) (d:<lungsim>, mind, and <cidam>, healthy: a healthy mind, mental health, often set beside {pumpi cidam}, a healthy body; also said of a person who is sound in mind) (r:zd:24244/zd:17976) (q:draft)
lungsim cidamna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health) (w:mental health/mental well-being) (d:<lungsim>, mind, and <cidamna>, health: mental health, named beside {pumpi cidamna}, bodily health, and {kha cidamna}, spiritual health) (r:zd:25170/zd:17613/zd:23989) (q:draft)
lungsim ngaihsutna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:thinking/mind/thoughts/mindset) (d:<lungsim>, mind or heart, and <ngaihsutna>, thought, two words of near meaning said together as one: the thinking of a person, the mind and its thoughts; with a possessive before it, as {a lungsim ngaihsutna}, his way of thinking) (r:zd:24056/zd:9428/zd:24276) (q:draft)
lungsim puak = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:attitude/mindset/disposition) (d:<lungsim>, mind, and <puak>, here the carrying or bearing of it: the way a person carries the mind, an attitude or mindset; stands after a possessor and often before <zia>, manner, as in {lungsim puak zia}) (r:zd:14525/zd:17488) (q:draft)
lungsim pumpi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/body) (w:mind and body) (d:<lungsim>, mind, and <pumpi>, body, joined without <leh>: mind and body together, the whole person, in talk of health, tiredness and rest) (r:zd:25178/zd:25175/zd:22779) (q:draft)
lungsim siangtho = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/religion) (w:pure heart/clean heart/sincerity) (d:<lungsim>, heart or mind, and <siangtho>, holy or clean: a pure and sincere heart; with <nei> to have one, with <sak> to make the heart pure) (r:zd:24119/zd:24276/zd:22868) (q:draft)
lungsim takpi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/religion) (w:sincere heart/sincerity/whole heart) (d:<lungsim>, heart or mind, and <takpi>, true: a true heart; nearly always followed by <tawh>, with, and then meaning sincerely, wholeheartedly) (r:zd:22683/zd:20956) (q:draft)
lungsimhoih = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:good heart/kind heart/good intention) (d:<lungsim>, heart, and <hoih>, good, written as one word: a good or kind heart, also kind-hearted) (j:lungsim/hoih) (r:zd:16313/zd:16433) (q:draft)
lungsimpuakzia = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:attitude/mindset/disposition) (d:<lungsim> and <puakzia> written as one word: the way one carries the mind, attitude) (j:lungsim/puakzia) (r:zd:25919/zd:21037/zd:22364) (q:draft)
lungsona = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:anger/rage/fury) (d:<lungso>, furious, with the noun suffix <na>: hot anger, the heart burning) (s:hehna) (b:lungso) (r:zd:24804/zd:15422) (q:draft)
lungtangnatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health) (w:heart disease) (d:<lungtang>, heart, and <natna>, disease, written as one word: illness of the heart) (j:lungtang/natna) (r:zd:24276/zd:20004) (q:draft)
lungtuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:be of one mind/be united/agree) (d:<lung>, heart, with <tuak>: be of one heart and mind; {lungtuak in} is with one mind, together; mostly met in the name of the news group Phualva Lungtuak Media) (s:kilungtuak) (r:zd:17485) (q:draft, low confidence)
Lunmual = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel) (w:Lunmual) (d:a village and a mountain of that name in the Tedim area of Chin State) (r:zd:21182) (q:draft, low confidence)
lupding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/home) (w:go to bed/be about to lie down) (d:<lup>, lie down, and <ding>, the marker of what is to come, written as one word: going to bed, about to lie down; {lupding ciangin} is at bedtime) (j:lup/ding) (r:zd:21876/zd:20874/zd:23388) (q:draft)
lupma = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time/home) (w:before going to bed/at bedtime) (d:<lup>, lie down, with <ma>, before, written as one word: before going to sleep; often {nitak lupma in}) (j:lup/ma) (r:zd:24276/zd:24252) (q:draft)
lupna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:bed/couch) (d:a place to lie on and sleep, a bed) (s:lupphah) (q:draft)
Lusei = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (f:social) (w:Lusei/Lushai) (d:a Zo people of Mizoram in India and their language, also called Mizo; {Lusei gam} is their land) (r:zd:21066/zd:25478/zd:21105) (q:draft)
Luseite = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (f:social) (w:Lushai/Lusei/Mizo) (d:the Lusei or Lushai people of Mizoram, <Lusei> with the plural <te>) (b:Lusei) (r:ts:301/zd:21066) (q:draft)
Lushai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (f:social/politics) (w:Lushai/Lusei/Mizo) (d:older name of the Mizo people and of their country, the Lushai Hills, now Mizoram in India) (r:ts:3168/ts:3506/zd:24227) (q:draft)
lut = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:enter/go in) (d:go or come into a place; the place entered is usually marked with <sungah>, into, and the opposite is <pusuak>, go out) (s:sungtum) (a:pusuak/paikhiat) (r:40.12.9) (q:draft)
lutding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:will enter/to enter/to join) (d:<lut> and <ding> written as one word: will go in, in order to go in; also of joining a group or a programme) (j:lut/ding) (r:ts:11162/zd:17927/zd:15602) (q:draft)
Lutheran = (i:1) (t:name) (f:religion) (w:Lutheran) (d:the Lutheran church, a Protestant denomination; {Lutheran Pawlpi} is the Lutheran Church) (o:English) (r:zd:24933/zd:14927) (q:draft)
lutkha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:get into/happen to enter/enter by accident) (d:<lut>, enter, and <kha>, happen to, written as one word: get into something without being meant to, as air, germs or soap into the body or into food, or a car into a shop) (j:lut/kha) (r:zd:11695/zd:14854/zd:22977) (q:draft)
lutkhuan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/politics) (w:permission to enter/entry permit/admission/right of entry) (d:<lut>, enter, and <khuan>, permission, written as one word: leave to enter a country, a place or a body, such as a visa or membership) (j:lut/khuan) (r:zd:25601/zd:11635/zd:17504) (q:draft)
lutlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:not enter/not join) (d:<lut> and <lo> written as one word: not go in, not take part in or not become a member of) (j:lut/lo) (r:zd:19571/zd:24064/zd:20905) (q:draft)
lutma = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/travel) (w:before entering/before going in) (d:<lut>, enter, and <ma>, before, written as one word, mostly followed by <in>: before going into a place, or before a matter is taken up) (j:lut/ma) (r:zd:21042/zd:20172/zd:12403) (q:draft)
lutman = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/social) (w:entrance fee/entry fee/admission) (d:<lut>, enter, with <man>, price: the money paid to enter a place or to take part in a contest) (j:lut/man) (r:zd:23114/zd:22967) (q:draft)
lutphei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:go in/enter/go across into) (d:<lut>, enter, with <phei> as a direction word, across or over to a place on the same level: go over and into a house, a room or a station) (b:lut) (r:zd:16148/zd:17143/zd:18943) (q:draft)
lutsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/social) (w:already entered/already joined/enrolled) (d:<lut>, enter, with <sa> marking a finished act: that has already entered or joined; {a lutsa innkuan} is a household already enrolled) (b:lut) (r:zd:25789/zd:24158) (q:draft)
lutsawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:try to enter/attempt to get in) (d:<lut>, enter, with <sawm>, intend, written as one word: try or set out to get into a place; {aguk lutsawm} is try to sneak in) (j:lut/sawm) (r:zd:11717/zd:15602) (q:draft)
lutsuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:go right in/enter straight into) (d:<lut>, enter, with <suak>, right through: go straight into a place without stopping) (j:lut/suak) (r:zd:16998/zd:23036/zd:12146) (q:draft)
lutthak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:newly join/newly enter) (d:<lut>, enter, with <thak>, new: have newly come in or joined; {pawl lutthak} is a new member of a group) (r:zd:21042/zd:23731) (q:draft)
luttheihna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/social) (w:entry/admission/access) (d:<luttheih>, be able to enter, with the noun ending {-na}: being able or allowed to enter a place or join a body; {luttheihna ding} is so that one may enter) (b:luttheih) (r:zd:25347/zd:25601/zd:23022) (q:draft)
lutto = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:go up into/enter/advance into) (d:<lut>, enter, with <to>, upward: go in and up, come up into a place) (j:lut/to) (r:zd:10912/zd:15456/zd:25165) (q:draft)
luut = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (j:lut) (r:zd:22606/ts:479) (q:draft)
luvai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health/body) (w:be dizzy/feel giddy/feel light-headed) (d:have the feeling that the head, <lu>, is spinning, often before fainting or vomiting) (r:zd:21015/zd:21667) (q:draft)
LZI = (i:1) (t:name) (f:social) (w:LZI) (d:short for {Leitungbup Zomi Innkuan}, the worldwide association that joins the Zomi Innkuan community organisations of many countries) (r:zd:24658) (q:draft)
ma apang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:take the lead/work at the forefront/take an active part) (d:<mapang>, take part in a common cause, written in two words with the relative <a> before <pang>: one who stands at the front and works for a cause; follows the cause, often with <dingin> or <nadingin>, and stands before the noun it describes) (r:zd:23742/zd:16254/zd:15772) (q:draft, low confidence)
ma kipang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:take the lead/press forward/work at the front) (d:<ma>, here the front, and <kipang>, take up a position: put oneself at the front, lead the way or work actively for a common cause; often followed by <khawm>, together, or <den>, always) (r:zd:22595/zd:21232/zd:22696) (q:draft)
maakai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (j:makai) (r:zd:24277/zd:24058) (q:draft)
maanlo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/religion) (w:untrue/false/wrong/not right) (d:<maan>, true, and <lo>, not, written as one word: not true, not right) (s:manlo) (j:maan/lo) (r:zd:18081/zd:10864) (q:draft)
Maansuang = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel) (w:Maansuang) (d:a place on the road from Tedim towards Laaitui, known for its bridge) (r:zd:21458) (q:draft, low confidence)
maanzaih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:it/media) (w:photograph/take a photo) (d:take a picture of something, as of a bank receipt in order to send it by e-mail) (r:zd:11797) (q:draft, low confidence)
maasuan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/media) (w:way ahead/outlook) (d:what a people is heading toward, the direction it faces; found only in the title of a series of articles, and perhaps the same word as <masuan>, go in front) (r:zd:10860) (q:draft, low confidence)
mabaan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/work) (w:way ahead/future course/next steps) (d:what lies ahead of a person or a work: the future course, the work still to be carried on; {mabaan zom} is carry on, continue onward) (r:zd:22897/zd:17046/zd:22652) (q:draft, low confidence)
mabante = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/social) (w:tasks ahead/future plans/matters ahead) (d:plural of <maban>: the things still to be done, the work and affairs that lie ahead) (b:maban) (r:zd:10983/zd:19051/zd:12431) (q:draft)
Macau = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city/land) (f:travel) (w:Macau/Macao) (d:city and territory of China on the south coast, near Hong Kong) (r:zd:11283/zd:11709) (q:draft)
Machine = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/home) (w:machine) (d:a machine, mostly after the English word for its kind, as in Washing Machine and X-ray Machine) (o:English) (r:zd:19863/zd:17741) (q:draft)
maciat = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:each and every) (d:<mah> and <ciat> written as one word after <kua>: {a kua maciat} is every single one, everybody without exception) (j:mah/ciat) (r:zd:19093/zd:11064/zd:24244) (q:draft)
madeuh = (i:1) (t:prep) (f:time) (w:just before/shortly before) (d:<ma> and <deuh> written as one word, placed after a verb or a time and often followed by <in>: a little before) (j:ma/deuh) (r:zd:17047/zd:12176/zd:24932) (q:draft)
madong = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:time) (w:until/up to) (d:<ma> before and <dong> until written as one word after a verb or noun: right up to the time when) (j:ma/dong) (r:zd:19915/zd:20860/zd:16952) (q:draft)
Madrid = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel) (w:Madrid) (d:capital city of Spain; also in the name of the football club Real Madrid) (r:zd:17622/zd:12829) (q:draft)
Magazine = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media) (w:magazine) (d:a magazine, mostly the yearly or jubilee magazine of a church, school or association, and often part of its name) (o:English) (r:zd:12039/zd:16678) (q:draft)
Magnitude = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature/media) (w:magnitude) (d:the measure of the strength of an earthquake, written after the number, as {6.0 Magnitude thahatna tawh zinling}, an earthquake with a strength of magnitude 6.0) (o:English) (r:zd:24532/zd:11610) (q:draft)
Magway = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:travel/politics) (w:Magway) (d:a region of central Myanmar, and its chief town) (r:ts:6702/zd:12048) (q:draft)
Magwe = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land/city) (f:travel/politics) (w:Magway/Magwe) (d:a region of central Myanmar and its chief town, also written Magway) (r:zd:25616/zd:18012) (q:draft)
mah bangun = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday/religion) (w:just as/in the same way as) (d:the emphatic <mah> with <bangun>, as, the form used when several people are addressed or act: closes a clause, just as that is done, and the main clause follows; the plural counterpart of <mahbangin>) (s:mahbangin) (r:zd:26953/zd:15572/zd:23297) (q:draft)
mah taleh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:even though/although/even if) (d:<mah>, the stressing marker, and <taleh>, even if: placed after the verb of a clause, often after <phial>, even though that is so; the main clause follows) (s:phial) (r:zd:22040/zd:25322) (q:draft)
mah tase = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:even though/although indeed) (d:<mah>, indeed, and <tase>, although: placed after a verb and followed by <leh> or {le uh}, even though that is truly so; the main clause that follows says what holds all the same; compare <taseleh>) (r:zd:21166/zd:22565/zd:21340) (q:draft)
maha = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:work/politics) (w:great/main) (d:Burmese word for great, used in {maha dat line}, the main power line of the national electricity grid) (o:Burmese) (r:zd:24544/zd:10860) (q:draft, low confidence)
maha = (i:2) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (d:<mah>, the emphatic marker, and <a> written as one word after a noun or {tua bang}: just so, at that very place) (j:mah/a) (r:zd:25668) (q:draft, low confidence)
Maharajalela = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel/education) (w:Maharajalela) (d:area and street, Jalan Maharajalela, in Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia; in the articles mostly the name of the Zomi Education Center school there) (r:zd:21906) (q:draft, low confidence)
mahbang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:just as/just like/in the same way) (d:<mah> and <bang> written as one word, followed by <in>: exactly as; {tua mahbang in} is in that same way, likewise) (j:mah/bang) (r:zd:16114/zd:12765/zd:25414) (q:draft)
mahbangin = (i:1) (t:ppm) (f:everyday) (w:just as/just like/in the same way as) (d:<mah> and <bangin> written as one word, placed after a noun or clause: exactly as, in the very same way as; {tua mahbangin} is in that same way, likewise) (j:mah/bangin) (r:zd:20670/zd:19875/zd:21869) (q:draft)
mahding = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:surely will/really will) (d:the emphatic <mah> and <ding> written as one word after a verb: it will certainly be so; in a question, will it really) (j:mah/ding) (r:zd:23485/zd:16844/zd:21989) (q:draft)
mahhi = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:indeed/truly) (d:emphatic <mah> and sentence-final <hi> written as one word at the end of a statement: it is indeed so) (j:mah/hi) (r:zd:24464/zd:21340) (q:draft)
mahhiam = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:the emphatic <mah> with the question particle <hiam>, written as one word at the end of a question: is it really so, is it indeed) (j:mah/hiam) (r:zd:21392/zd:15116) (q:draft)
mahinzong = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/time) (w:also just/even on that very) (d:<mahin> and <zong>, also, written as one word after a word of time or place: on that very day too, in that very place too) (j:mahin/zong) (r:zd:14535/zd:17622) (q:draft)
Mahkahmah = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:court/law court) (d:a court of law in Malaysia, where an arrested person is brought before a judge) (s:thukhenzum) (o:Malay, mahkamah) (r:zd:12112/zd:15379) (q:draft)
mahleh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:although/though/even though) (d:<mah> and <leh> written as one word after a verb: although it is so, even though) (s:napi) (j:mah/leh) (r:zd:24375/zd:22584) (q:draft)
mahlo = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:not at all/by no means) (d:<mah> and <lo> written as one word, a strong negative after the verb, mostly as {peuh mahlo}: not at all, certainly not) (j:mah/lo) (r:ts:1202/zd:25186/zd:25515) (q:draft)
mahmah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:the very thing/very/indeed) (d:emphasises the word before it: after a describing word or verb it means very or indeed, after a noun the very one) (s:nakpi/nakpitakin)
mahmahding = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:will be very/will very much) (d:<mahmah> and <ding> written as one word after a verb or describing word: it will be so to a high degree, or is expected to be) (j:mahmah/ding) (r:zd:15099/zd:17955/zd:16934) (q:draft)
mahmahhi = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:very/indeed) (d:<mahmah>, very, and the sentence-final <hi>, written as one word at the end of a statement: it is very much so) (j:mahmah/hi) (r:zd:17933/zd:21003) (q:draft)
mahmahkhat = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/media) (w:a very) (d:<mahmah> and <khat> written as one word, after a describing word: one that is very so, as {minthang mahmahkhat}, a very famous one) (j:mahmah/khat) (r:zd:17547/zd:12244/zd:15245) (q:draft)
mahmahlai = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:still very) (d:<mahmah> with <lai>, here still, written as one word, after a describing word: still very much so) (b:mahmah) (r:zd:19355/zd:17735) (q:draft)
mahmahlo = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:not at all/not really/hardly) (d:<mahmah> and <lo> written as one word, placed after a verb: not really, not at all; {muzo mahmahlo} is not able to find at all) (j:mahmah/lo) (r:zd:26495/zd:12042) (q:draft)
mahmahmawk = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:very indeed/truly very) (d:<mahmah> and <mawk> written as one word after a describing word: very much so, said with surprise or dismay) (j:mahmah/mawk) (r:zd:14731/zd:15781/zd:12752) (q:draft)
mahmahta = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:very much now/indeed now) (d:<mahmah> and <ta> written as one word: very, with the sense that the state has now been reached, as in {haksa mahmahta}, it has become very hard) (j:mahmah/ta) (r:zd:24276/zd:19599) (q:draft)
mahmahtek = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:very much, each one/all very) (d:<mahmah> and <tek> written as one word, after a verb or describing word: very much so, said of everyone concerned) (j:mahmah/tek) (r:zd:21279/zd:19807/zd:15507) (q:draft)
mahmahzong = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:even) (d:<mahmah> and <zong> written as one word after a noun or phrase: even that very one, even itself) (j:mahmah/zong) (r:zd:15609/zd:15056) (q:draft)
mahpan = (i:1) (t:prep) (f:everyday) (w:from that very/right from) (d:<mah>, the very one, and <pan>, from, written as one word: from that same place, source or thing and no other) (j:mah/pan) (r:zd:24234/zd:14654/zd:23906) (q:draft)
mahpeuh = (i:1) (t:det) (f:everyday) (w:whoever/anyone at all/every) (d:<mah> and <peuh> written as one word, placed after a question word: <akua mahpeuh> is whoever it may be, everyone) (j:mah/peuh) (r:zd:17335/zd:12289/zd:25318) (q:draft)
mahtawh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:with that very/just like) (d:<mah> and <tawh> written as one word, placed after a noun or pronoun: with that very thing, by that itself; with <kibang>, just the same as) (j:mah/tawh) (r:zd:15572/zd:20932/zd:22282) (q:draft)
Maid = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/home) (w:maid/housemaid/domestic worker) (d:a woman who is employed to do the work of a household and lives in it) (o:English) (r:zd:15103/zd:11285) (q:draft)
maiet = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:curry favour with/seek to please/win over) (d:<mai>, face, with <et>, look at: seek the favour of someone, try to please or placate, also with gifts or money) (r:zd:16331/zd:21138) (q:draft)
maikai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (j:makai) (r:zd:17958/zd:9227) (q:draft)
maikal = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:next week/coming week) (d:<mai>, ahead, with <kal>, week, written as one word: the week that comes next; {maikal ah} is next week, also under an article that is to be continued; it may be meant more loosely as the time ahead) (j:mai/kal) (r:zd:15622/zd:11224/zd:12112) (q:draft, low confidence)
maikalsung = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:next week/in the coming week) (d:<mai>, ahead, <kal>, week, and <sung>, during, written as one word: in the week to come) (j:mai/kal/sung) (r:zd:13211/zd:13157) (q:draft)
maikha = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:next month/the coming month) (d:<mai>, ahead, with <kha>, month, written as one word: the month that comes next; before the name of a month, this coming) (j:mai/kha) (r:zd:11782/zd:20276/zd:14912) (q:draft)
maikhat = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:education) (w:one page) (d:<mai>, face, here the page of a book, and <khat>, one, written as one word; {lai maikhat} is one page of writing) (j:mai/khat) (r:zd:21593/zd:21876) (q:draft)
maikum = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:next year/the coming year) (d:<mai>, ahead, with <kum>, year: the year that lies ahead) (s:kumkik) (r:zd:16799/zd:15800) (q:draft)
mail = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/it) (w:mail/post) (d:letters and parcels sent by post; also in {e-mail}) (o:English) (r:zd:23545/zd:23973) (q:draft)
mailam kalsuan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:go forward/move ahead/way forward) (d:<mailam>, the future or the front, and <kalsuan>, step: go forward into the future, of a people or an organisation; with {zia ding} or <nading> it names the course to be taken, the way forward) (r:zd:10983/zd:22810/zd:24158) (q:draft)
mailamding = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time/everyday) (w:future) (d:<mailam> and <ding> written as one word: what is to come for someone, the future of a person, a family or a country) (j:mailam/ding) (r:zd:19396/zd:17309) (q:draft)
main = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (j:manin) (r:zd:15951/zd:24978) (q:draft)
main = (i:2) (t:conj) (f:everyday/time) (w:before) (d:<ma>, before, and <in> written as one word after a verb: before doing it) (j:ma/in) (r:zd:21664/zd:23935) (q:draft, low confidence)
