Militia = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:militia) (d:armed group of civilians, in Myanmar news mostly one that fights on the side of the army) (o:English) (r:zd:26620/ts:5326/ts:1566) (q:draft)
million = (i:1) (t:num) (f:work) (w:million) (d:the number one million, written before or after the figure it counts) (s:awn) (o:English) (r:zd:22203/zd:24116/zd:25109) (q:draft)
millions = (i:1) (t:num) (f:everyday/work) (w:million) (d:the English plural used as the number word million, written after the number or before it) (o:English) (r:zd:8667/zd:13285) (q:draft)
mim = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food/nature) (w:millet/grain) (d:a grain crop, millet or Job's tears, compare <vaimim>, maize; in songs paired with {sawmtang} for the grain one lives on, and {mim bang piang} is a phrase of songs for being born into this world) (r:zd:15996/zd:20406) (q:draft, low confidence)
mimai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:public/presence of others) (d:<mi>, people, with <mai>, face or front, written as one word: before other people, in public, mostly as {mimai ah}) (j:mi/mai) (r:zd:14587/zd:25673) (q:draft)
mimal muhna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/media) (w:personal opinion/personal view/own point of view) (d:<mimal>, individual, and <muhna>, way of seeing: the opinion of one person and not of a group; writers mark an article with {mimal muhna pan}, from a personal point of view, and say {kei mimal muhna}, my personal opinion) (r:zd:19329/zd:23929/zd:17903) (q:draft)
mimal vai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:personal matter/private affair/privacy) (d:<mimal>, an individual, and <vai>, here a matter or affair: a matter that concerns one person only, a private or personal affair, privacy; set against the affairs of a group or the public) (r:zd:19302/zd:24699) (q:draft)
mimalin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:social) (w:individually/personally/as an individual) (d:<mimal>, individual, with <in>, written as one word: as an individual or as individuals; {kei mimalin} is I personally) (j:mimal/in) (r:zd:16612/zd:24030) (q:draft)
mimalkim = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:social/everyday) (w:every individual/each person/everyone) (d:<mimal> individual and <kim> every written as one word: each single person) (s:mikim) (j:mimal/kim) (r:zd:16790/zd:22171/zd:15268) (q:draft)
mimang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:missing person) (d:<mi>, person, with <mang>, here be lost: someone who has disappeared and is being looked for) (r:zd:20331/zd:12099) (q:draft)
mimawkmawk = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:ordinary person/commoner/nobody in particular) (d:<mi>, person, with <mawkmawk>, ordinary, written as one word: a person of no special rank or standing) (j:mi/mawkmawk) (r:zd:15315/zd:12512) (q:draft)
mimuan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:trusted person/confidant/trusted aide) (d:<mi>, person, with <muan>, trust: a person someone relies on, a trusted helper or adviser of a leader) (r:zd:19934/zd:21657) (q:draft)
min = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:name)
min kitaih = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/social) (w:name clash case/fraud case) (d:<min>, name, and <kitaih>, collide: a clash of names, said of refugee resettlement files held back because the name or identity of the applicant conflicts with another record, a fraud case; {min kitaih te} are the persons whose files are so held) (r:zd:22608) (q:draft, low confidence)
minam = (i:3) (t:n) (f:social) (w:tribe/people/nation) (d:a people of one descent and language) (r:zai:tribe) (q:draft)
minam hihna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:national identity/ethnic identity/nationhood) (d:<minam>, a people, and <hihna>, the fact of being: the fact of being a people or of belonging to one, its identity; a possessive such as <i> or <a> stands before it) (r:zd:25461/zd:21309) (q:draft)
minam it = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:love one's people/be patriotic) (d:<minam>, people or nation, and <it>, love: love one's own people, be devoted to the nation; the object stands before the verb without a marker, and the pair also stands before a noun, as in {minam it zia}, the way of loving one's people) (r:zd:24699/zd:21090/zd:25461) (q:draft)
