minam khangto = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:developed nation/advanced people) (d:<minam>, a people, and <khangto>, grow: a people that has advanced in learning and prosperity, a developed nation, said beside {gam khangto}, a developed country; the same two words also form a clause, a people advances) (r:zd:22713/zd:24028/ts:4564) (q:draft)
minam kician = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/social) (w:established nation/recognised people/people in its own right) (d:<minam>, a people or nation, and <kician>, firm, well-founded: a people that stands as a full nation in its own right, with its own name, language and recognition; often with <khat> after it and a people's name before it, {Zomi minam kician khat}) (r:zd:21815/zd:23762) (q:draft)
minam party = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:ethnic party/ethnic political party) (d:<minam>, a people or ethnic group, and <party>, political party: a political party that stands for one ethnic group, as against a party of the whole country; a term of the politics of Myanmar) (r:zd:22989/zd:23011/zd:22365) (q:draft)
minam puan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/social) (w:national dress/traditional cloth/ethnic costume) (d:<minam>, people or nation, and <puan>, cloth: the woven cloth or dress that marks a people, worn at festivals; {Zo minam puan} is the Zo national dress, set against {fashion puan}) (r:zd:22303/zd:11076) (q:draft)
minamkee = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:sub-tribe/ethnic subgroup/branch of a people) (d:<minam> people with {kee}, branch: one of the smaller groups into which a people is divided, each often with its own speech) (r:zd:22802/zd:16509) (q:draft, low confidence)
