nahi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:you are) (d:<na> and <hi> written as one word: you are; with <uh>, you all are) (j:na/hi) (r:zd:19733/zd:19397/zd:17955) (q:draft)
nahi = (i:2) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (d:the noun ending {-na} written apart from its verb and joined to <hi>: it is the doing of what the verb says, as {kitan nahi hi}, it is a break) (j:na/hi) (r:zd:22470) (q:draft, low confidence)
