numei kizuakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:brothel/prostitution) (d:<numei>, woman, and <kizuakna>, selling: the selling of women, that is prostitution, and the place where it is done, a brothel; with <ah> and a verb of sending, into prostitution or to a brothel) (r:zd:19145/zd:12470) (q:draft)
numei naupang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/family) (w:women and children) (d:<numei>, woman, and <naupang>, child, set side by side without <leh>: women and children, named together as those who are weak and to be protected; in other sentences the same two words are a female child, a girl) (r:zd:16157/ts:1885) (q:draft, low confidence)
numei pasal = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/everyday) (w:women and men/both sexes/male and female) (d:<numei>, woman, and <pasal>, man, set side by side without <leh>, and: women and men together, people of either sex; {numei pasal cih omlo} is without regard to sex) (r:zd:20930/zd:24948) (q:draft)
numeikhat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/media) (w:a woman/one woman) (d:<numei> and <khat> written as one word: a woman, a certain woman) (j:numei/khat) (r:zd:21015/zd:17536) (q:draft)
numeino = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/family) (w:girl/little girl/young girl) (d:<numei>, female, with <no>, young or small: a girl) (b:numei) (r:42.8.54) (q:draft)
nungak = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:young woman/girl/maiden) (d:a young unmarried woman, a virgin) (a:tangval) (r:19.148.12) (q:draft)
nungak siangtho = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:virgin) (d:<nungak>, young woman, and <siangtho>, holy: a virgin, a woman who has not been with a man, said above all of Mary the mother of Jesus; among Roman Catholics also a nun, a religious sister) (r:zd:23792/zd:21978) (q:draft)
nungak tangval = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/family) (w:young people/young women and men/unmarried youth) (d:<nungak>, a young woman, and <tangval>, a young man, set side by side without a conjunction: the unmarried young people of a community taken together, or a girl and a boy as a couple) (r:zd:17023/zd:20794) (q:draft)
nungciangin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/time) (w:afterward/later/then) (d:<nung>, after, with <ciangin>, when; {tua nungciangin} is after that, {a nungciangin} is afterward or in turn) (s:nungcianga) (q:draft)
nungdeuh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:recently/lately/a little later) (d:<nung>, after or behind, with <deuh>, somewhat: a little while back, as in {nungdeuh mahmah in}, very recently; also a little further on in a text or in time) (j:nung/deuh) (r:zd:11924/zd:23784/zd:15784) (q:draft)
nungdiak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:recently/lately/not long ago) (d:<nung>, after, with <diak>: a short time ago, mostly as {nungdiak in}; before a noun it means recent, as in {nungdiak thupiangte}, the recent events) (r:zd:11150/zd:18067/zd:12033) (q:draft)
nungkal = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:last week) (d:<nung>, back, with <kal>, week: in the week before this one; before the name of a day it means that day of last week, as {nungkal Thursday ni in}, last Thursday) (r:zd:17175/zd:15535/zd:19385) (q:draft)
nungkalsung = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time/media) (w:last week/in the past week) (d:<nung> behind, <kal> week and <sung> during written as one word, mostly as {nungkalsung in}: during the week that has passed) (j:nung/kal/sung) (r:zd:12309/zd:19860/zd:15374) (q:draft)
nungkha = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:last month) (d:<nung>, behind, and <kha>, month, written as one word: the month before this one, last month) (j:nung/kha) (r:zd:11864/zd:18058/zd:12807) (q:draft)
nungkhasung = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:last month) (d:<nung>, behind or past, <kha>, month, and <sung>, during, written as one word: during last month; usually followed by <in>) (j:nung/kha/sung) (r:zd:18110/zd:14648/zd:15679) (q:draft)
nungkum = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:last year) (d:<nung>, behind or after, with <kum>, year: the year before this one) (s:nikum) (r:zd:12259/zd:22046/zd:16239) (q:draft)
nungkumsung = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:last year/during last year) (d:<nung>, back, <kum>, year, and <sung>, during, written as one word: in the course of last year) (j:nung/kum/sung) (r:zd:21563/zd:18028) (q:draft)
nungsangah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:afterwards/later/in the end) (d:<nungsang> with <ah>, written as one word: {a nungsangah} is afterwards, later on, and after a person, after that person is gone) (j:nungsang/ah) (r:zd:20646/zd:23882) (q:draft)
nungsungteng = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time/media) (w:recently/lately/in recent days) (d:<nung>, behind, past, with <sungteng>, throughout: during the time just past, in recent days or weeks) (r:zd:17628/zd:14566/zd:11652) (q:draft)
nungta = (i:3) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:alive/live/be alive) (d:live, be alive; {a nungta lai} is still living) (a:si/sih) (r:27.6.21)
nungta pasian = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:the living God) (d:<nungta>, alive, and <Pasian>, God: the living God, a fixed term of Christian speech, nearly always with <a> before it as {a nungta Pasian}, the God who lives, set against idols and the gods of the forefathers) (r:zd:23394/zd:20786) (q:draft)
nungtakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (j:nuntakna) (r:zd:23367/zd:24336) (q:draft)
nungthuap = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/work) (w:back up/support/reinforce) (d:<nung>, behind, with <thuap>, add a layer: stand behind someone as support or reserve, or be what gives backing to a work) (r:zd:20999/zd:20649) (q:draft)
nungtolh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:go backward/fall back/regress/backslide) (d:move back instead of forward: draw back from an undertaking, decline instead of progressing, fall away in faith) (s:nungkik) (r:zd:25056/zd:25273/zd:19662) (q:draft)
nungzuihna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:discipleship/following) (d:<nungzuih>, follow after, with the noun ending {-na}: the following of someone, especially of Christ) (b:nungzuih) (r:zd:23936/zd:17329/zd:23928) (q:draft)
nungzuipite = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:apostles/disciples) (d:<nungzui>, disciple, with {-pi}, chief, and the plural <te>: the apostles, the first disciples of Jesus) (b:nungzui) (r:zd:25751/zd:21530) (q:draft)
nuno = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:aunt/mother's sister) (d:<nu>, mother, with <no>, young: the younger sister of one's mother) (b:nu) (q:draft)
nunta = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (j:nungta) (r:zd:11994/zd:17271/zd:15528) (q:draft)
nuntaak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (j:nuntak) (r:zd:25414/zd:23770) (q:draft)
nuntaakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/religion) (j:nuntakna) (r:zd:23148/zd:25414/zd:16428) (q:draft)
nuntak khuasak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/everyday) (w:live one's life/lead a life/make a living) (d:<nuntak>, live, and {khuasak}, the second form of <khuasa>, lead one's daily life: the two verbs together mean live and get along from day to day; {nuntak khuasak zia} is a way of life, and the noun is <nuntak khuasakna>; not the village name Khuasak) (r:zd:22944/zd:25749) (q:draft)
nuntak khuasakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/work) (w:living/livelihood/living conditions/standard of living) (d:<nuntak>, live, and <khuasakna>, way of life, a pair of two words of like meaning: the daily life and living of people, how well they live; followed by a describing word such as <niam>, low, or <haksa>, hard) (r:zd:21717/zd:22262) (q:draft)
nuntak khuasakzia = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/everyday) (w:way of life/living conditions/standard of living) (d:<nuntak>, live, and <khuasakzia>, way of life: a pair of near synonyms used as one noun for how people live and what their living conditions are; the people concerned stand before it) (s:khuasakzia) (r:zd:15720/zd:15234/zd:19462) (q:draft)
nuntak nading = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/everyday) (w:livelihood/means of living/for living) (d:<nuntak>, live, and <nading>, for the purpose of: what one needs in order to live, a living or livelihood, as the object of verbs of seeking and gathering; also plainly in order to live) (r:zd:20800/zd:17313) (q:draft)
nuntak sungin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:in one's lifetime/during one's life/as long as one lives) (d:<nuntak>, live, and <sungin>, within: during the whole time that someone is alive; a subject marker such as <a> or <na> stands before it) (r:zd:21978/zd:25222) (q:draft)
nuntak tawntungna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:eternal life/everlasting life) (d:<nuntak>, live, and <tawntungna>, everlastingness: living for ever, the eternal life of Christian teaching; used as a noun, as object of verbs such as <ngah>, receive, and <pia>, give) (r:zd:23806/zd:23394/zd:20848) (q:draft)
nuntakna bei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media/health) (w:lose one's life/die) (d:<nuntakna>, life, and <bei>, come to an end: the life ends, a respectful way to say that a person died; mostly as {nuntakna bei lawh}, lose one's life as a result of something) (r:ts:7296/zd:17990) (q:draft)
nuntakpih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:religion/everyday) (w:live by/live out/practise) (d:<nuntak>, live, with <pih>, together with: live with something as part of one's life, live according to a teaching or a value) (b:nuntak) (r:zd:15894/zd:21097/zd:21607) (q:draft)
nunun = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:put last/do later/leave till later) (d:do or place something after other things, the opposite of <masak>, do first; verb form of <nunung>, last) (b:nunung) (r:zd:25467/zd:19222/zd:23725) (q:draft)
nunzia = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:way of life/lifestyle/conduct) (d:short form of <nuntakzia>: the way a person or a people live) (s:nuntakzia/nuntakdan) (r:zd:20972/zd:11571/zd:12121) (q:draft)
nupa kaal = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:between husband and wife/married life/marital relationship) (d:<nupa>, husband and wife, and <kaal.2>, the space between: what is between a husband and wife, their life together as a couple; it stands before a noun such as <kizopna>, relationship, or before <sung> and <sungah>, within) (r:zd:21673/zd:19287/zd:24087) (q:draft)
nupakop = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:couple/married couple) (d:<nupa>, husband and wife, and <kop>, pair, written as one word: a man and a woman as a pair, usually a married couple) (j:nupa/kop) (r:zd:12091/zd:12567/zd:22312) (q:draft)
nupen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:the woman/she) (d:<nu>, the woman, with the topic marker <pen>, written as one word: the woman just spoken of, as the topic of the sentence) (j:nu/pen) (r:zd:12555/zd:12701) (q:draft)
nupi naupaai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/family) (w:pregnant woman/expectant mother) (d:<nupi>, woman, and <naupaai>, be pregnant: a pregnant woman; the verb follows the noun without a relative marker and the pair is used as one noun, with <te> for the plural or <khat> for one) (r:zd:11337/zd:16853) (q:draft)
nupikhat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/family) (w:a woman/a married woman) (d:<nupi>, woman, and <khat>, one, written as one word: a certain woman) (j:nupi/khat) (r:zd:19871/zd:15048/zd:19676) (q:draft)
nupinu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/family) (w:woman/married woman/lady) (d:<nupi>, woman, with <nu>, the female one: a grown or married woman, in news reports the woman who is spoken of; the male word is <papipa>) (r:zd:16600/zd:13024/zd:15943) (q:draft)
Nurse = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/work) (w:nurse) (d:a nurse; {Nurse nu} is a female nurse and {Nurse pa} a male nurse) (o:English) (r:zd:12466/zd:15724) (q:draft)
nusiatna hangin = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:social) (w:on the passing of/because of the death of) (d:<nusiatna>, leaving behind, and <hangin>, here because of: with <hong> before it, {hong nusiatna hangin}, because he or she has left us, the usual wording of a condolence notice for a death; the person stands before it) (r:zd:21550/zd:22685) (q:draft)
nute pate = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:parents/mothers and fathers) (d:<nute>, mothers, and <pate>, fathers, set side by side without <leh>: parents as a group, used as subject or possessor when speaking of parents in general) (r:zd:22140/zd:23803) (q:draft)
nutsiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/social) (w:leaving/departure/passing) (d:<nutsiat>, leave behind, with the noun suffix {-na}: the leaving of someone or something; {hong nutsiatna hangin} is because he has left us, said of a death) (s:nusiatna) (b:nutsiat) (r:zd:18955/zd:12013) (q:draft)
nzong = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:also/too) (d:the doer marker <n> and <zong>, also, written as one word after an apostrophe, as in {te'nzong} for {te in zong}: they also, even they) (j:n/zong) (r:zd:12727/zd:13100/zd:20225) (q:draft)
Oaxaca = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:travel) (w:Oaxaca) (d:state in the south of Mexico) (r:zd:15089) (q:draft)
Odisha = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:travel/politics) (w:Odisha) (d:state on the east coast of India) (r:zd:19536/zd:15958) (q:draft)
off = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:day off/time off) (d:time free from work; job notices tell with it how many days off there are, and {off ni} is a day off) (o:English) (r:zd:11011/zd:17327/zd:10794) (q:draft)
Offday = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:day off/rest day) (d:the day of the week on which a worker does not work; a heading in job advertisements in Malaysia) (o:English) (r:zd:16799/zd:17978) (q:draft, low confidence)
Office = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/politics) (w:office) (d:an office: the place where the work of a company, an organisation or a government body is done, and that body itself) (s:zum) (o:English) (r:zd:17327/zd:12437/ts:7051) (q:draft)
Officer = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/work) (w:officer/official) (d:a person holding rank or office in the police, the army or a government department; {Police Officer} is a police officer) (o:English) (r:zd:19745/zd:14814/zd:15952) (q:draft)
Officers = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/work) (w:officer/official) (d:officers of the police or of a government office; the English plural form is used as the word, often after Police and followed by the plural <te>) (o:English) (r:zd:20252/zd:15012) (q:draft)
official = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:official/officer) (d:a person who holds a post in a government or other public body) (o:English) (r:zd:20252/zd:15803) (q:draft)
official = (i:2) (t:adj) (f:politics) (w:official/officially) (d:said or done with the authority of a government or other body; {official in} is officially) (o:English) (r:zd:24414/zd:15237/ts:2513) (q:draft)
officially = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:politics/social) (w:officially/formally) (d:the English adverb used in Zolai sentences, mostly as {officially in}: in an official way, with public authority) (o:English) (r:zd:17675/zd:13268/zd:24058) (q:draft)
Officials = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/work) (w:officials/official) (d:the English plural, used for the people who hold office in a government or a body, mostly after its English name and followed by <te>) (o:English) (r:zd:15101/zd:11725) (q:draft)
Ohio = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:travel) (w:Ohio) (d:state of the United States of America) (o:English) (r:zd:9227/zd:15101) (q:draft)
Oklahoma = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:travel) (w:Oklahoma) (d:a state of the United States; many Zomi live in its city of Tulsa) (r:zd:22004/zd:24453) (q:draft)
Olympic = (i:1) (t:name) (f:social/media) (w:Olympics/Olympic Games) (d:the Olympic Games, the international sports competition) (o:English) (r:zd:23780/zd:19578) (q:draft)
om = (i:5) (t:v) (f:everyday/home) (w:abide) (d:stay or live in a person or a place, remain there)
om hithiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/religion) (w:be still/stay quiet/keep calm/rest) (d:<om>, stay, and <hithiat>, at ease: stay still and quiet, doing nothing and not stirring; often a piece of advice, with <in> or <ding> after it, and with <daitak>, quietly, before it) (r:zd:22563/zd:20329/zd:25932) (q:draft)
oma = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:there is and/exist) (d:<om>, be or there is, and the linking <a> written as one word: there is, and; it ends a clause and joins it to the next) (j:om/a) (r:zd:14751/zd:9251/zd:17911) (q:draft)
ombang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:politics/everyday) (w:according to/as it stands) (d:<om> and <bang> written as one word: as there is, in keeping with what exists; {thukhun ombang in} is according to the law in force) (j:om/bang) (r:zd:25111/zd:14797) (q:draft)
ombangin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/politics) (w:according to/in accordance with) (d:<om> and <bangin> written as one word: as there is, in keeping with what exists; {thukhun ombangin} is according to the law in force) (j:om/bangin) (r:zd:22813/zd:19805) (q:draft)
omciang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:when there is/when one is) (d:<om>, be, and <ciang>, when, written as one word: when there is, when one is in a place; {ih omciang} is when we are) (j:om/ciang) (r:zd:21745/zd:12596/zd:19676) (q:draft)
omdan khawldan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:conduct/manners/way of life) (d:<omdan>, way of being, and <khawldan>, way of staying: a pair that names as one thing how a person lives and behaves among others) (r:zd:19990/zd:22138) (q:draft)
omding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:will be/will take place) (d:<om> and <ding> written as one word: there will be, will be held; also is to stay) (j:om/ding) (r:zd:12862/zd:12168/zd:24024) (q:draft)
omhetlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:there is none at all/not be at all) (d:<om>, be, and <hetlo>, not at all, written as one word: there is none at all, be not there at all) (j:om/hetlo) (r:zd:13186/zd:13203/zd:14751) (q:draft)
omhi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:there is/there are/exist) (d:<om>, be there, and the sentence-final <hi> written as one word: closes a statement that something or someone is there) (j:om/hi) (r:zd:20720/zd:22203/zd:17919) (q:draft)
omhiam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:is there/are there) (d:<om>, be, with the question particle <hiam>, written as one word: is there, what is there, how is it) (j:om/hiam) (r:zd:20860/zd:21085/zd:20574) (q:draft)
omkawikawi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be here and there/occur in many places) (d:<om>, be, and <kawikawi>, here and there, written as one word: be found in many places, be all around) (j:om/kawikawi) (r:zd:14650/zd:16926/zd:20012) (q:draft)
omkei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:there is not/not be/not exist) (d:<om> and the negative <kei> written as one word: there is none, is not there; <omkei leh> is if there is none, without) (j:om/kei) (r:zd:25173/zd:20971/zd:19556) (q:draft)
omkei leh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:without/if there is no/were it not for) (d:<omkei>, there is not, and <leh>, here if: placed after a noun, if there is none of it, without it; the result follows) (r:zd:20971/zd:19556) (q:draft)
omkhading = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:there may be/there will probably be) (d:<omkha>, happen to be, with <ding>, will, written as one word: there may well be, there are likely to be) (j:omkha/ding) (r:zd:14581/zd:13266/zd:15245) (q:draft)
omkhalo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:there is none/not be there) (d:<omkha> and <lo> written as one word: there happened to be none, no one was there, often of people killed or hurt) (j:omkha/lo) (r:zd:14545/zd:13140) (q:draft)
omkhinta = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:already exist/be there already) (d:<om> and <khinta> written as one word: there is already, has already come to be in a place or state) (j:om/khinta) (r:zd:19648/zd:12845/zd:14531) (q:draft)
omkhollo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:hardly exist/be scarce) (d:<om> and <khollo> written as one word: there is hardly any, there are not many) (j:om/khollo) (r:zd:20142/zd:14704/zd:12281) (q:draft)
omlaiding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:will still be/there are probably still) (d:<omlai>, still be there, with <ding>, will, written as one word: there will still be, there are thought to be more) (j:omlai/ding) (r:zd:15828/zd:19543) (q:draft)
omlaitak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:be staying/while being) (d:<om> and <laitak> written as one word: while being or staying, be in a place or busy with something at that moment) (j:om/laitak) (r:zd:17256/zd:11759) (q:draft)
omle = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:if there is/if there are) (d:<om> with <le>, here the short form of <leh>, if, written as one word: if there is, if there are; {i omle} is if we are, if any of us) (j:om/le) (r:zd:20795/zd:25248/zd:15726) (q:draft)
omleh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:if there is) (d:<om>, be, and <leh>, if, written as one word: if there is, if someone is in a place) (j:om/leh) (r:zd:22773/zd:20004/zd:11759) (q:draft)
omlel = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:just be there/simply exist) (d:<om> and <lel>, merely, written as one word: there simply is, just be or stay there) (j:om/lel) (r:zd:10821/zd:25573) (q:draft)
omleuleu = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:there is again/there is also) (d:<om> and <leuleu> written as one word: there is once more, or there is on the other hand; closes a report of another event of the same kind) (j:om/leuleu) (r:zd:17252/zd:15629/zd:15274) (q:draft)
omloding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:there will not be/will not be) (d:<om>, be, <lo>, not, and <ding>, will, written as one word: there will be none, will not be; as an instruction, must not stay) (j:om/lo/ding) (r:zd:21032/zd:11371/zd:11956) (q:draft)
omloh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not be/be absent/be without) (d:<om> and <loh> written as one word: form of <omlo> used before <ding>, <nading>, <laitak> and <man>; {a omloh nadingin} is so that there may not be, and {a omloh laitak} is while there is none) (j:om/loh) (r:zd:22654/zd:24276/zd:14734) (q:draft)
omlua = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:there are very many/abound) (d:<om> and <lua> written as one word: there is very much or very many of something; with a negative, there is not so very much) (j:om/lua) (r:zd:20297/zd:14941/zd:26017) (q:draft)
ommawh = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:family/social) (w:naughty/restless/unruly) (d:not staying still or behaving properly, said mostly of a child; {khut ommawh} is said of a man who cannot keep his hands to himself) (r:zd:19465/zd:9451/zd:21168) (q:draft)
ommello = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:there seems to be none/hardly exist) (d:<om>, be, <mel>, appearance, and <lo>, not, written as one word: there is no sign of it, there seems to be none) (j:om/mel/lo) (r:zd:12159/zd:12099/zd:17094) (q:draft)
ommuan = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:idly/at ease/casually) (d:<om>, stay, with <muan>: just staying as one is, without effort or special purpose; {ommuan in} is idly, casually, from where one happens to be) (r:zd:23332/zd:22639) (q:draft, low confidence)
omna ciat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/religion) (w:each one's place/wherever each is) (d:<omna>, the place where one is, and <ciat>, each: the place where each one is; mostly as {i omna ciat ah}, wherever each of us is, in blessings and exhortations to people who live scattered) (r:zd:24382/zd:12122/zd:25042) (q:draft)
omna inn = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:residence/dwelling/home) (d:<omna>, the place where one is, and <inn>, house: the house where a person lives or stays, a residence; a possessive such as <a> or <ka> stands before it) (r:zd:22451/zd:14650/zd:8667) (q:draft)
omna mun = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/travel) (w:location/whereabouts/place of residence) (d:<omna>, being or staying, and <mun>, place: the place where someone or something is or lives; stands after a possessor, as {i omna mun}, the place where we live, or after the thing located) (r:zd:12196/zd:23928/zd:11215) (q:draft)
omna pia = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:work) (w:accommodation provided/lodging given) (d:<omna>, place to stay, and <pia>, give: a formula of job notices, the employer gives a place to stay; it stands beside {an vak} or {an pia}, food is provided, and {an pialo}, no food) (r:zd:12695/zd:12024) (q:draft)
omnading = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/home) (w:place to stay/for staying/so that there may be) (d:<om> and <nading> written as one word: for living in, a place to stay; also so that something may exist) (j:om/nading) (r:zd:18104/zd:18012) (q:draft)
omnailo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:there is not yet/not exist yet) (d:<om> and <nailo> written as one word: there is none so far, has not yet come about) (j:om/nailo) (r:zd:11553/zd:21032) (q:draft)
omnawnlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:there is no longer/be no more/no longer exist) (d:<om> and <nawnlo> written as one word: there is no longer, is not there any more; {bangmah omnawnlo} is there is nothing left) (j:om/nawnlo) (r:zd:13222/zd:22584/zd:11485) (q:draft)
omngeilo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:have never been/have never happened) (d:<omngei>, have once been, with <lo>, not, written as one word: there has never been, it has never happened before) (j:omngei/lo) (r:zd:15751/zd:15609) (q:draft)
omomna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:wherever one is/each one's place) (d:<omom> with the noun suffix <na>, after a person marker: the place where each one is living; {i omomna ah} is wherever we are) (j:omom/na) (r:zd:15529/zd:25686/zd:23893) (q:draft)
omphial = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:there even is/happen to be) (d:<om>, be, and <phial>, even, written as one word: there even is such a one, it goes so far that there is) (j:om/phial) (r:zd:11177/zd:22391) (q:draft, low confidence)
omsam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:there are indeed/there certainly are) (d:<om>, be, with the particle <sam>, indeed, to be sure: there certainly is or are, often granting a point before a contrast) (b:om) (r:zd:24955/zd:25923/zd:19464) (q:draft, low confidence)
omsamlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:there is none/not be at all) (d:<om>, be, with <samlo>, not at all, written as one word: there is none after all, there was not any) (j:om/samlo) (r:zd:20966/zd:12982/zd:17104) (q:draft)
omtakpi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:really exist/there really is) (d:<om>, be, and <takpi>, truly, written as one word: there really is, really take place) (j:om/takpi) (r:zd:11099/zd:23485/zd:20046) (q:draft)
omtheilo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:cannot be/cannot be present/cannot exist) (d:<om>, be, with <theilo>, unable, written as one word: cannot be there, cannot take place, there cannot be) (j:om/theilo) (r:zd:22818/zd:17450/zd:24604) (q:draft)
omtuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:seem to be/there probably is) (d:<om>, be there, with <tuak>, here showing what the writer supposes, written as one word: there seems to be, there surely is) (j:om/tuak) (r:zd:11924/zd:15968) (q:draft)
omtuak = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:both be/each be) (d:<om>, be or live, with <tuak>, each or both, written as one word: both are, each of them is) (j:om/tuak) (r:zd:21369) (q:draft, low confidence)
omtuan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:there is/exist) (d:<om>, be there, and <tuan> written as one word, nearly always before a negative or in a question: there is not really any, there is no such thing after all) (j:om/tuan) (r:zd:11761/zd:13149/zd:15184) (q:draft)
omtuanlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:there is none/not be at all) (d:<om> be, <tuan> and the negative <lo> written as one word: there is none after all, nothing of the kind exists) (j:om/tuan/lo) (r:zd:12349/zd:14611/zd:15023) (q:draft)
omvetlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:there is none at all/not exist at all) (d:<om>, be, with the emphatic <vet> and <lo>, not, written as one word: there is nothing at all, not a single one) (j:om/vet/lo) (r:zd:11617/zd:11587) (q:draft)
omveve = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:still exist/there is nevertheless) (d:<om>, be there, with <veve>, all the same: there still is, there is such a thing in spite of what was said) (j:om/veve) (r:zd:17655/zd:11251/zd:14686) (q:draft)
ong nusiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/family) (w:passing/death/decease) (d:{ong}, a spelling of <hong>, toward us, and <nusiatna>, a leaving behind: the leaving of us, a respectful word for the death of a person; stands after the name of the dead and before words such as <hangin> or {tawh kisai}) (r:zd:22595/zd:13178) (q:draft)
ongkhak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/it) (w:send to/send here) (d:{ong}, another spelling of <hong>, toward the speaker or hearer, written as one word with <khak>, send: send a message, money or a document to me, to us or to you) (j:hong/khak) (r:zd:16813/zd:12371/zd:11797) (q:draft)
ongnusia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:leave us/pass away) (d:{ong}, a spelling of <hong>, toward the speaker, and <nusia>, leave, written as one word: has left us, used in condolence notices of a person who has died) (r:zd:21699/zd:22703) (q:draft)
ongpai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:come/come here) (d:{ong}, a spelling of <hong>, with <pai>, written as one word: come toward the speaker) (j:hong/pai) (r:zd:15933/zd:17723) (q:draft)
ongpia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/religion) (w:give us/give to me/grant) (d:{ong}, a spelling of <hong>, toward the speaker, and <pia>, give, written as one word: give to us or to me; {thupha ongpia} is bless us) (r:zd:17181/zd:25768/zd:20016) (q:draft)
ongtung = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:arrive/come to) (d:{ong}, another spelling of <hong>, and <tung> written as one word: arrive here, come to a place) (j:hong/tung) (r:zd:22664/zd:10688) (q:draft)
ongtungding = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:time) (w:coming/upcoming/next) (d:{ong}, a spelling of <hong>, with <tung>, arrive, and <ding>, written as one word: that will arrive, the coming; placed before a date) (j:hong/tung/ding) (r:zd:15190/zd:11832) (q:draft)
online = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:it) (w:online/on the internet) (d:on the internet; {online pan} is from the internet, by way of the internet, and {online ah} is on the internet) (o:English) (r:zd:21042/zd:24393/zd:26411) (q:draft)
Ooredoo = (i:1) (t:name) (f:it) (w:Ooredoo) (d:a mobile phone company, one of the telecoms operators of Myanmar) (r:zd:17607/zd:25332) (q:draft)
Oparasi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/social) (w:raid/immigration raid/operation) (d:an operation of the Malaysian police or immigration officers in which people without documents are checked and arrested; {Oparasi tawh kiman} is arrested in a raid) (o:Malay, operasi) (r:zd:13291/zd:23629) (q:draft)
oparasi lut = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/social) (w:raid/carry out a raid) (d:{oparasi}, an immigration raid, and <lut>, enter: of the authorities, come into a place to check papers and arrest people without them; the place stands before with <ah>) (r:zd:23629) (q:draft)
Operasi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:raid/operation/crackdown) (d:in Malaysia, an operation of the police or immigration officers to check and arrest foreigners without papers; {Operasi lut} is a raid comes in) (o:Malay, operasi) (r:zd:14836/zd:21552/zd:15739) (q:draft)
operasi lut = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:raid/carry out a raid) (d:{operasi}, raid, and <lut>, enter: the authorities carry out a raid on a place, above all an immigration raid in Malaysia; the place stands before it with <ah> and the number of people arrested follows) (r:zd:15745/zd:12464) (q:draft)
operasi lutin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:politics) (w:in a raid/in a crackdown) (d:<Operasi>, a raid of the Malaysian police or immigration officers, and <lutin>, entering: a raid having come in, that is in a raid; the place stands before it with <ah> or <sungah>, and the number of people arrested follows with <kiman>) (r:zd:15187/zd:16197) (q:draft)
Operation = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health) (w:operation/surgery) (d:a surgical operation; {operation bawl} is to operate on someone or to have an operation) (o:English) (r:zd:24029/zd:12285) (q:draft)
Operation = (i:2) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:operation) (d:an organised action of soldiers, police or rescuers) (o:English) (r:zd:11043/zd:13082) (q:draft, low confidence)
Operator = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:operator) (d:a person who works a machine such as a crane or a lift, or a company that runs a service such as buses or telephones) (o:English) (r:zd:15639/zd:17607) (q:draft)
Opium = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/politics) (w:opium) (d:the drug made from the poppy; usually written beside the Zolai word for it, <beng>) (o:English) (r:zd:11637) (q:draft)
opportunity = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/education) (w:opportunity/chance) (d:English word used in Zolai for a good chance to do something; it is often added in brackets to explain <hamphatna>) (s:hamphatna) (o:English) (r:zd:24978/zd:14755) (q:draft, low confidence)
opposition = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:opposition/opposition party) (d:the party or parties that stand against the government in power, in Zolai also {langpang pawl}; mostly as {opposition party}) (o:English) (r:zd:24699/zd:24677) (q:draft)
Oprasi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/social) (w:raid/immigration raid/operation) (d:an immigration or police raid in Malaysia in which people without papers are arrested, and the officers who carry it out; also written <Operasi>) (o:Malay, operasi) (r:zd:19320/zd:17442) (q:draft)
Option = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:option/choice) (d:one of the choices offered by an office or an authority, usually named with its number as Option 1 or Option 2) (o:English) (r:zd:22138/zd:21664) (q:draft, low confidence)
order = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/work) (w:order/command) (d:an order given by one who has authority; {order pia} is give an order) (o:English) (r:zd:24714/zd:24111) (q:draft)
ordination = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:ordination) (d:the act by which a church sets a person apart as pastor or minister; {ordination ngah} is be ordained and {ordination pia} is ordain) (o:English) (r:zd:17168/zd:9237/zd:25265) (q:draft)
Oregon = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:travel) (w:Oregon) (d:state in the northwest of the United States; its city Portland has a Zomi community) (r:zd:25157/zd:9249) (q:draft)
organ = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion/media) (w:organ) (d:keyboard instrument played in church; {organ tum} is play the organ) (o:English) (r:zd:9260/zd:9245) (q:draft)
organ = (i:2) (t:n) (f:body/health) (w:organ) (d:a part inside the body, such as a kidney, that can be transplanted) (o:English) (r:zd:10702) (q:draft, low confidence)
original = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:media/everyday) (w:original/genuine) (d:first and not copied or changed: the original text or word, a genuine product as against a copy; also as a noun, the original) (o:English) (r:zd:21369/zd:25111/zd:17634) (q:draft)
Orlando = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel) (w:Orlando) (d:city in the state of Florida in the United States) (r:zd:12843/zd:24453) (q:draft)
Orthodox = (i:1) (t:name) (f:religion) (w:Orthodox/Orthodox Church) (d:the Eastern Orthodox churches and their members, named beside the Catholics) (o:English) (r:zd:21027/zd:21723) (q:draft)
otot = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:keep shouting/shout again and again) (d:<ot>, shout, said twice: go on shouting or calling out) (b:ot) (r:zd:21850/zd:16024/zd:20808) (q:draft)
Ottoman = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:politics) (w:Ottoman) (d:the Turkish empire that ruled much of the Middle East, and Palestine from 1516 to 1917; also said of its rulers) (r:zd:25099/zd:16651) (q:draft)
ou = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:sentence-final particle of friendly urging or exclamation, added to a request, a wish or a question addressed to the hearer) (r:zd:11368/zd:25288) (q:draft, low confidence)
Outlet = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:outlet/branch/shop) (d:one of the shops or branches of a business, also a place of entertainment; it occurs mostly after an English name) (o:English) (r:zd:19648/zd:15370) (q:draft, low confidence)
Outlets = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:outlet/branch/shop) (d:a shop or restaurant of a business, used in the English plural form) (o:English) (r:zd:14665/zd:15370) (q:draft, low confidence)
Overstay = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/travel) (w:overstay/overstaying) (d:staying in a country after the visa or permit has run out, and a person who does so; {Overstay in om} and {Overstay tawh om} are stay on as an overstayer) (o:English) (r:zd:11762/zd:12534/zd:20012) (q:draft)
overtime = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:overtime) (d:work done beyond the regular hours, and the pay for it) (o:English) (r:zd:17060/zd:13291) (q:draft)
Oxford = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:education) (w:Oxford) (d:city in England, named mostly for its university) (o:English) (r:zd:23329/zd:21288) (q:draft)
oxygen = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/nature) (w:oxygen) (d:the gas in the air that living things need to breathe, also given to the sick from a cylinder, <oxygen bung>) (o:English) (r:zd:25184/zd:25134/zd:22584) (q:draft)
oxygen bung = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health) (w:oxygen cylinder/oxygen tank) (d:<oxygen> with <bung>, here a container or tank: a cylinder of oxygen for the sick to breathe from, counted with a numeral after it) (r:zd:25184/zd:18186) (q:draft)
pa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:father) (d:male parent; with a possessive, as in {ka pa}, my father, and {a pa}, his father) (a:nu)
paa = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be included/have with) (d:be included or be taken along, mostly with <lo>: {paa lo} is without, not included; the same spelling is also written for <pa>, father) (o:Burmese, pa) (r:zd:15501/zd:18081) (q:draft, low confidence)
paai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:throw/cast/throw away) (d:throw, cast or throw away) (s:lawn/paii/lot) (r:43.10.11) (q:draft)
paakhuan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature/home/travel) (w:flower garden/park/garden) (d:<paak>, flower, and <huan>, garden, written as one word: a flower garden, also a public park) (j:paak/huan) (r:zd:24649/zd:16777/zd:22680) (q:draft)
paakkual = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:wreath/garland) (d:<paak>, flower, with <kual>, ring: a wreath or garland of flowers, sent to a funeral as a sign of sympathy or given to honour someone) (r:zd:10908/zd:24183) (q:draft)
paakta = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (j:pakta) (r:zd:21279/zd:17858) (q:draft)
Paakzang = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua) (f:travel/social) (w:Paakzang) (d:Zomi village in the Tedim area; written in brackets after a personal name it shows the home village of the person) (r:ts:301) (q:draft, low confidence)
paal = (i:1) (t:v) (f:nature/social) (w:bloom/blossom/flourish) (d:come into flower, and of a person, a people or a land be in the bloom of life, flourish; a word of songs and elevated speech, and also a personal name) (r:zd:23896/zd:21690/zd:23531) (q:draft, low confidence)
paallun = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/nature) (w:flourish/prosper/bloom) (d:be in full bloom; said of a land or people that thrives and prospers, as in {Zogam hong paallun ding hi}) (r:zd:23554/zd:22464/zd:11571) (q:draft)
Pacific = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:nature/travel) (w:Pacific) (d:the Pacific Ocean, mostly as {Pacific tuipi}, and the region around it) (r:zd:16828/zd:19262) (q:draft)
Page = (i:1) (t:n) (f:it/media) (w:page) (d:a page of a person or group on Facebook or other social media, where news and notices are posted) (o:English) (r:ts:9299/zd:22688) (q:draft)
Pagoda = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:pagoda) (d:a Buddhist shrine or temple tower) (o:English) (r:zd:24469/zd:16101) (q:draft)
pah vingveng = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:straight away/at once/without delay) (d:<pah>, immediately, strengthened by <vingveng>, hurriedly: placed after a verb, mostly a verb of going, to say that it is done at once and in haste) (r:zd:20935/zd:25625/zd:24594) (q:draft)
Pahang = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:travel) (w:Pahang) (d:a state of Malaysia; also in Jalan Pahang, a street of Kuala Lumpur named in addresses) (r:zd:17777/zd:14628) (q:draft)
pahding = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:at once/right away) (d:<pah> and <ding> written as one word after a verb: will or should do it at once, or it will follow as a matter of course) (j:pah/ding) (r:zd:10960/zd:19676/zd:14523) (q:draft)
pahhi = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:at once/immediately/right away) (d:<pah> and the sentence-final <hi> written as one word after a verb: it was done at once, and so it followed) (j:pah/hi) (r:zd:11140/zd:16259/zd:21340) (q:draft)
pahlel = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:readily/simply) (d:<pah>, at once, with <lel>, merely, written as one word after a verb: the thing follows readily, simply as a matter of course) (j:pah/lel) (r:zd:20176/zd:24276) (q:draft, low confidence)
pahlian = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:right away/readily/straight away) (d:<pah>, at once, with the emphatic <lian>, placed after a verb: the action follows at once or readily) (r:zd:12370/zd:23733) (q:draft, low confidence)
pahlo = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:not at once/not necessarily) (d:<pah>, at once, with <lo>, not, written as one word after a verb: it does not happen right away, it does not follow as a matter of course) (j:pah/lo) (r:zd:20926/zd:25078/zd:8668) (q:draft)
pahna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (d:<pah>, at once, with the noun ending {-na}, written after a verb: the doing of the action at once or as a direct consequence, as in {kipat pahna}, the immediate start, and {suah pahna}, becoming straight away) (b:pah) (r:ts:9570/zd:22238) (q:draft)
pahpahna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (d:<pahpah>, readily or again and again, with the noun ending {-na}, placed after a verb: the doing of it often or too readily; {heh pahpahna} is being quick to anger) (b:pahpah) (r:zd:22778/zd:22923) (q:draft)
pahpih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:support/encourage/back) (d:stand behind someone with approval and encouragement, cheer on) (r:zd:14751/zd:25560/zd:21050) (q:draft)
pai = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:go) (d:move from one place to another, go or walk to a place)
pai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:come) (d:move toward the speaker or the place spoken of, usually with <hong> before it: {hong pai}, come here)
paidan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:way of going/course/procedure/manner) (d:<pai>, go, with <dan>, way: how something goes or proceeds, as the course of events, the working of an office or a way of thinking; of a person or animal also the gait) (r:zd:23830/zd:20418/zd:17655) (q:draft)
