pasian deihna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:will of God/God's will) (d:<Pasian>, God, and <deihna>, what one wants: the will of God, a fixed term of church speech; one follows it, {Pasian deihna zuih}, and it is set against {ci leh sa deihna}, the desire of the flesh) (r:zd:23394/zd:23629) (q:draft)
