patkhiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/travel) (w:origin/starting point) (d:<patkhiat>, start off, with the noun ending <na>: where something starts; after <ki> it is the place a person or thing came from, as in {ki patkhiatna gam}, country of origin) (b:patkhiat) (r:zd:20850/zd:11945) (q:draft)
pattah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:family/education) (w:train/bring up/discipline/nurture) (d:teach and guide a child or young person toward good conduct; {ki pattah} is train oneself or be trained) (r:zd:21155/ts:3375/zd:23191) (q:draft)
pattahna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/education) (w:upbringing/training/discipline) (d:the bringing up and training of children or young people in conduct and character, from <pattah>, train, with the noun ending {-na}) (r:zd:20955/zd:21886/zd:23591) (q:draft)
