paulo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:not speak/say nothing) (d:<pau>, speak, and <lo>, not, written as one word: not speak, without speaking; one who does not speak a language) (j:pau/lo) (r:zd:22683/zd:25573) (q:draft)
pawi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:festival/feast) (d:a feast or festival kept with eating and rejoicing; {pawi bawl} and {pawi kham} both mean hold a feast, and {pawi hun} is festival time) (s:pawikhamna) a day or period of celebration
pawi muakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:festival celebration/celebration) (d:<pawi>, festival, and <muakna>, welcoming: the celebration held to mark a festival, placed after the name of the festival, as in {Khuado pawi muakna}) (r:zd:23083/zd:21156) (q:draft)
pawisim = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:attend a festival/keep a festival) (d:<pawi> and <sim> written as one word: go to and take part in a festival; before a noun or <khempeuh>, those who attend it) (j:pawi/sim) (r:zd:21232/zd:15592) (q:draft)
pawlah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/time) (w:at about/at around) (d:<pawl> and <ah> written as one word after a time, a distance or a number: at about, somewhere around) (j:pawl/ah) (r:ts:5635/zd:17428/zd:18872) (q:draft)
pawlah = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:social) (w:among/in the group of) (d:<pawl>, group, with <ah>, written as one word: in the group of, among those who are so) (j:pawl/ah) (r:zd:23476/zd:21626) (q:draft)
pawlkhat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:a group/some) (d:<pawl>, group, with <khat>, one: one group; after a noun it means some of them) (s:honkhat)
