photding = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:will first/for the time being) (d:<phot>, first or for now, and <ding>, will, written as one word after a verb: will do it first, will do it for the time being) (j:phot/ding) (r:zd:16786/zd:20295) (q:draft)
photni = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:let us first) (d:<phot>, first or for now, written as one word with the ending <ni>, let us, placed after a verb: let us do this first, let us do it for the time being) (j:phot/ni) (r:zd:19108/zd:20845) (q:draft)
Photo = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/it) (w:photo/photograph/picture) (d:a picture taken with a camera; {photo zaih} is to take a photo) (o:English) (r:zd:21365/zd:17983/zd:26163) (q:draft)
Photographer = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/work) (w:photographer) (d:a person who takes photographs; the Zolai word beside it in the articles is {manzaih}) (o:English) (r:zd:11780/zd:13293) (q:draft)
photphot = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:just/first/for now) (d:<phot> said twice, after a verb and mostly in a request: just do it, go ahead and do it for now) (b:phot) (r:zd:22474/zd:21598/zd:22473) (q:draft)
phuahna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/everyday) (w:composing/composition/making up) (d:<phuah>, compose or make up, with the noun ending <na>: the composing of a song or poem; {zuau phuahna} is the making up of lies, fabrication) (b:phuah) (r:zd:9254/zd:12269) (q:draft)
phuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:name/call/give a name) (d:give a name to a child, a place or a thing, with <min>, name) (s:phuah)
phuaka = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/religion) (w:compose) (d:<phuak>, compose a song, and the linking <a> written as one word: composed, and then) (j:phuak/a) (r:zd:9224/zd:9255/zd:9257) (q:draft)
phuakpa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/religion) (w:composer/author/writer) (d:<phuak>, compose, with <pa>, man: the man who composed a song, its words or its tune; {la phuakpa} is the writer of a song) (b:phuak) (r:zd:9245/zd:9244) (q:draft)
phualsatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:camp/encampment/military camp/base) (d:<phualsat>, set up camp, with the noun suffix <na>: the place where troops are stationed, a military camp or post) (b:phualsat) (r:ts:3446/ts:4653/ts:9033) (q:draft)
Phualva = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (f:nature) (w:hornbill) (d:the hornbill, a large forest bird taken as an emblem of the Zomi; in most articles part of the name Phualva Lungtuak Media) (r:zd:20800) (q:draft)
Phualva Lungtuak = (i:1) (t:name) (f:media) (w:Phualva Lungtuak) (d:<Phualva>, hornbill, and <lungtuak>, be of one mind: name of a Zomi news group, mostly as {Phualva Lungtuak Media}, given as the source or the translator at the head or foot of an article) (r:zd:20078/zd:20464) (q:draft)
phuankhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/work) (w:found/establish/set up) (d:<phuan>, set up, with <khia>, out: start an organisation, a company or a church; {a phuankhia pa} is the founder) (r:zd:21720/zd:14531/zd:25447) (q:draft)
phuankhiapa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/work) (w:founder) (d:<phuankhia>, found or set up, with <pa> for a male person: the man who founded an organisation, a company or a movement) (r:zd:9257/zd:24957/zd:17577) (q:draft)
phuat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:found/establish/set up) (d:found an organisation such as a church, a party or an armed group) (b:phuan) (r:zd:12337/zd:25562) (q:draft)
phuhkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/social) (w:establish/found/set up) (d:<phuh>, found, with <khiat>, out: bring an organisation, a committee or a state into being; the form used before <ding> and <uh>) (r:ts:4823/ts:7820/zd:25020) (q:draft)
phuitong = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (f:nature) (w:cherry/cherry tree) (d:a tree of the Chin hills that blossoms in December, and its fruit; {phuitong pak} is cherry blossom and {phuitong gah} is the cherry fruit; Phuitong is also the name of a village) (r:zd:11400/zd:24276) (q:draft)
Phuket = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel) (w:Phuket) (d:island and province in the south of Thailand, visited by many tourists) (r:zd:17239/zd:14869) (q:draft)
phukhagawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:crash badly/smash into/pile up) (d:<phukha> and <gawp> written as one word: strike against with great damage; {ki phukhagawp}, of vehicles, is crash into one another) (j:phukha/gawp) (r:zd:15613/zd:12967/zd:20353) (q:draft)
phulna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature/health) (w:outbreak/springing up) (d:<phul>, gush out or spring up, with the noun suffix <na>: the springing up or breaking out of something; {phulna mun} is the place where a disease breaks out) (b:phul) (r:zd:24609/zd:24453) (q:draft, low confidence)
phulum = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (f:nature) (w:winged termite/flying termite) (d:an insect that swarms up out of the ground and flies high; the proverb {phulum phulna dingin leikha in petlet} says that it bursts out only because the <leikha> under the ground bites it; which insect is meant is not certain) (r:zd:11024/zd:24688) (q:draft, low confidence)
phulum = (i:2) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:ram to death/run down and kill) (d:<phu>, drive straight into, with <lum>, lie down, here to death, written as one word: kill by driving into) (r:zd:10855) (q:draft, low confidence)
phumna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/religion) (w:burial/burying/immersion) (d:<phum>, bury or immerse, with the noun suffix <na>: the putting of a body or a thing into the ground, {suang phumna} the setting of a stone, or immersion in water) (b:phum) (r:zd:25908/ts:3179) (q:draft)
phung = (i:2) (t:n) (f:social/family) (w:clan/family/lineage) (d:the family line a person belongs to) (s:beh) (q:draft)
phungvuh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/work) (w:nurture/foster/support/build up) (d:care for a person, a group or a gift so that it grows and stands firm; said of a church, a party, a people or a talent. The literal sense, heaping earth around the foot of a plant, is not attested in the articles) (r:zd:25172/zd:24003/zd:24381) (q:draft, literal sense to be confirmed)
phungzi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:Buddhist monk/monk) (d:a Buddhist monk; {phungzi sang} is a monastery, and the word is also used for a Christian monk) (o:Burmese, hpongyi) (r:zd:23113/ts:2189/ts:1657) (q:draft)
phunlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:not grumble/not complain/without complaining) (d:<phun>, grumble, and <lo>, not, written as one word; {phunlo in} is without grumbling, and {phunlo paulo in} is without complaint or a word) (j:phun/lo) (r:zd:24673/zd:20941/zd:15384) (q:draft)
phutkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/social) (w:establish/found/set up) (d:<phut>, set up, with <khia>, out, written as one word: found an organisation, a government or a country) (j:phut/khia) (r:zd:20673/ts:3289) (q:draft)
Physics = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:physics) (d:the science of matter and energy, as a subject of study) (o:English) (r:zd:15845/zd:22556) (q:draft)
Phyu = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua) (f:travel) (w:Phyu) (d:town in Bago Region of Myanmar; the same word, Burmese for white, is also part of Burmese personal and place names) (o:Burmese) (r:zd:17202) (q:draft, low confidence)
pi = (i:2) (t:n) (f:family) (w:grandmother) (d:grandmother, the mother of one's father or mother) (q:draft)
pia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:give/grant) (d:hand something over to someone or grant it; {thu pia} is give an order and <thupha pia> is bless) (a:ngah/lak)
piading = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:will give/to give) (d:<pia>, give, and <ding>, will, written as one word: will give, in order to give, to be given) (j:pia/ding) (r:zd:19249/zd:22704/zd:24331) (q:draft)
piakbeh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:give more/give in addition/pay extra) (d:<piak>, give, with the ending {-beh}, in addition: give or pay something more on top of what was given) (b:piak) (r:zd:12327/zd:22448/zd:20670) (q:draft)
piakding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:to give/to be given) (d:<piak> and <ding> written as one word: will give, to be given, or what is to be given; {sum piakding} is money to be paid) (j:piak/ding) (r:zd:15571/zd:24370) (q:draft)
piakei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not give/do not give) (d:<pia>, give, and the negative <kei>, written as one word: {piakei in} and {piakei un} are do not give, {piakei ning} is I would not give) (j:pia/kei) (r:zd:20263/zd:23733) (q:draft)
piakkhiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion/social) (w:giving/generosity/donation/dedication) (d:<piakkhiat>, give out, with the noun suffix <na>: the giving away of money, goods or oneself for others or for God) (b:piakkhiat) (r:zd:24119/zd:21561/zd:18107) (q:draft)
piakkul = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:must give/have to pay) (d:<piak> and <kul> written as one word: it is necessary to give or to pay; with <lo>, need not pay) (j:piak/kul) (r:zd:23863/zd:25824/zd:22581) (q:draft)
piakleh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:if one gives/when one gives) (d:<piak>, give, with <leh>, if or when, written as one word: if or when someone gives; {thupha na piakleh} is if you bless) (j:piak/leh) (r:zd:21044/zd:17481) (q:draft)
piakloh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not give) (d:<piak> and <loh> written as one word: not giving, not given; {piakloh phamawh} is must be given, and {piakloh omlo} is there is none who is not given) (j:piak/loh) (r:zd:23437/zd:21370) (q:draft)
piaksawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:try to give/offer/intend to give) (d:<piak>, give, with <sawm>, intend, written as one word: be about to give, offer or attempt to give) (j:piak/sawm) (r:zd:14701/zd:19814) (q:draft)
pialai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:give more/give in addition/also give) (d:<pia>, give, with the ending {-lai}, still or further: give something more, give as well) (b:pia) (r:zd:23136/zd:21590/zd:20587) (q:draft)
pialo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:not give/not provide/withhold) (d:<pia> and <lo> written as one word: does not give; in job notices {an pialo} means that food is not provided) (j:pia/lo) (r:zd:20577/zd:12336) (q:draft)
Piancit = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:travel/politics) (w:France) (d:France, in a name taken from Burmese; {Piancit pai} is the going of Zomi men to France in 1917, remembered at its hundredth year in 2017) (o:Burmese, pyinthit) (r:zd:11549/zd:18086) (q:draft)
pianga = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:arise and/come about and/be born and) (d:<piang> and the linking <a> written as one word: something comes about or is born, and the sentence goes on) (j:piang/a) (r:zd:19193/zd:21605/zd:11135) (q:draft)
piangding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:will happen/will come about) (d:<piang>, happen or come into being, and <ding>, will, written as one word) (j:piang/ding) (r:zd:20355/zd:23832) (q:draft)
pianggawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/social) (w:break out/erupt/happen violently) (d:<piang> happen with <gawp>, which shows that the action is severe, written as one word: of trouble, a fight or an accident, break out) (j:piang/gawp) (r:zd:15937/zd:16225/zd:13330) (q:draft)
pianghi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:happen/occur/arise) (d:<piang> and the sentence ending <hi> written as one word: it happens or happened, it comes about) (j:piang/hi) (r:zd:17848/zd:19562/zd:21323) (q:draft)
piangkhin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:have happened/have already occurred) (d:<piang>, happen, and <khin>, already, written as one word: have already happened or come about, often after a count of cases) (j:piang/khin) (r:zd:19662/zd:11715/zd:20682) (q:draft)
pianglo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not happen/not come about/not arise) (d:<piang>, come into being or happen, with <lo>, not, written as one word) (j:piang/lo) (r:zd:12337/zd:22140/zd:21050) (q:draft)
piangngei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:have happened before/once happened) (d:<piang> and <ngei> written as one word: have happened or taken place at an earlier time) (j:piang/ngei) (r:zd:20892/zd:15431/zd:19981) (q:draft)
piangpah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:happen at once/arise immediately) (d:<piang>, happen, and <pah>, at once, written as one word: come about straight away) (j:piang/pah) (r:zd:21110/zd:12136/zd:15201) (q:draft)
piangpiang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:keep happening/happen again and again/come about) (d:<piang>, happen, said twice: happen repeatedly or one after another; {piangpiang lel} is it simply comes about) (b:piang) (r:zd:22046/zd:23810/zd:20999) (q:draft)
piangthak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:religion) (w:be born again/born again) (d:<piang>, be born, with <thak>, new: be born again in the Christian sense, come to new faith; {mi piangthak} is a born-again person) (r:zd:20218/zd:8667/zd:23676) (q:draft)
piangthakte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:the born again/born-again believers) (d:<piangthak>, born again, with the plural {-te}: those who are born again, born-again Christians) (b:piangthak) (r:zd:23394/zd:23740/zd:22784) (q:draft)
piangtheilo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:impossible/cannot happen) (d:<piang>, happen, and <theilo>, unable, written as one word: cannot come about, not possible) (j:piang/theilo) (r:zd:17297/zd:19816) (q:draft)
pianist = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media) (w:pianist/piano player) (o:English) (r:zd:17634) (q:draft)
pianloh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:not happen/not arise/not come about) (d:<pian> and <loh> written as one word, before words such as <nading> and <hangin>: not come into being, not happen) (j:pian/loh) (r:zd:20004/zd:23487/zd:19875) (q:draft)
pianna nu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:birth mother/own mother/natural mother) (d:<pianna>, birth, and <nu>, mother: the mother who gave birth to someone, as against a stepmother or a woman addressed as mother; a possessive stands before it; {pianna nu leh pa} is one's own parents) (r:zd:19571/zd:24117/zd:26953) (q:draft)
piannop = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:want to become/wish to be) (d:<pian>, come to be, with <nop>, want: wish to be or to turn out a certain way; {na piannop dan} is what you want to become) (j:pian/nop) (r:zd:20917/zd:20725/zd:19731) (q:draft)
piano = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/religion) (w:piano) (d:the musical instrument; {piano tum} is play the piano) (o:English) (r:zd:23653/zd:9248/zd:9214) (q:draft)
pianpian = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:gradually/somewhat/more and more) (d:placed after a verb or describing word: the state is beginning to be so or is slowly becoming so, often followed by <ta>) (r:zd:22928/zd:15234/zd:19154) (q:draft)
pianta = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:rather/somewhat) (d:placed after a verb or describing word: it has by now become rather so, it seems to have come to that, as in {sawt pianta}, it has been rather long) (j:pian/ta) (r:zd:23890/zd:23014/zd:23603) (q:draft, low confidence)
pianthak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:religion) (w:be born again/be regenerated) (d:<pian>, be born, with <thak>, new: be born again in the Christian sense; also as a noun, the new birth) (r:zd:23394/zd:20281/zd:26664) (q:draft)
pianthakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:new birth/regeneration/conversion) (d:<pian>, be born, with <thak>, new, and the noun suffix <na>: being born again, the conversion of a person to faith) (r:zd:25288/zd:21052) (q:draft)
Piantit = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:politics/travel) (w:France/French) (d:France, often as {Piantit gam}; {Piantit pau} and {Piantit lai} are the French language) (o:Burmese, pyinthit) (r:zd:17437/zd:21978/zd:19571) (q:draft)
pianuamlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:be unwilling to give/refuse to give) (d:<pianuam>, want to give, with the negative <lo>, written as one word) (j:pianuam/lo) (r:zd:11454/zd:11182) (q:draft)
piapah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:give at once/give right away) (d:<pia>, give, and <pah>, at once, written as one word: give or grant without delay) (j:pia/pah) (r:zd:24069/zd:12304/zd:20176) (q:draft)
piapia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:keep giving/give repeatedly) (d:<pia>, give, said twice: give again and again or go on giving; with <ki>, be given one after another) (b:pia) (r:zd:14992/zd:24231/zd:21168) (q:draft)
piasa = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:have given/already given) (d:<pia>, give, with the ending {-sa}, already done: given; {hong piasa teng} are those who have given, in lists of donors) (b:pia) (r:zd:11011) (q:draft)
pibawl = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:honour/esteem/treat as important) (d:treat a person or an event as great and show it honour and attention) (r:zd:23466/zd:20264/ts:301) (q:draft)
picin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:mature/grow up/become complete) (d:form of <picing>, mature, used before <ding>, <nading>, <ma> and other endings: grow to maturity in body or in mind) (b:picing) (r:zd:21285/zd:24115/zd:23929) (q:draft)
picing takin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/social) (w:fully/maturely/properly/completely) (d:<picing>, mature or full-grown, and <takin>, which here makes an adverb of manner and does not mean while: in a full, mature and complete way; stands before the verb) (r:zd:21706/zd:17327) (q:draft)
picingtak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/work) (w:maturely/fully/properly/thoroughly) (d:<picing>, mature, with <tak> written as one word, usually followed by <in>: in a mature and complete way) (j:picing/tak) (r:zd:26565/zd:22810) (q:draft)
picingte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/family) (w:adults/mature people/grown-ups) (d:<picing>, mature, with the plural <te>: those who are full-grown or mature, said of people, minds, customs and nations) (b:picing) (r:zd:22757/zd:21081/zd:10938) (q:draft)
picinna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:maturity/growth/development) (d:<picin>, mature, with the noun ending {-na}: being or becoming full-grown in body, mind or faith; {lungsim picinna} is maturity of mind) (b:picing) (r:zd:21285/zd:10957/zd:16379) (q:draft)
Pickup = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:pickup truck/pickup) (d:a small truck with an open load bed; mostly {Pickup Truck} or {Pickup mawtaw}) (o:English) (r:zd:11992/zd:15974) (q:draft)
pihding = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:will do with/to do with) (d:the verb suffix <pih>, together with or for someone, and <ding> written as one word after a verb: will do it with or for someone, or someone to do it with) (j:pih/ding) (r:zd:19676/zd:15588/zd:17421) (q:draft)
pihpih = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:<pih> doubled after a verb: keep on doing the action with, to or for someone, as in {kiho pihpih}, kept talking with her) (b:pih) (r:zd:12992/zd:17070/zd:15570) (q:draft, low confidence)
pii = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/everyday) (j:pi) (r:zd:22203) (q:draft, low confidence)
piicing = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:social) (j:picing) (r:zd:25221/zd:25394) (q:draft)
pikhat = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:a great/a major/a big) (d:<pi> and <khat> written as one word after a noun: the ending for great belongs to the noun, so that {issue pikhat} is a big issue) (j:pi/khat) (r:zd:23432/zd:11662/zd:10687) (q:draft)
pikhat = (i:2) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:one foot) (d:<pi>, the measure foot, and <khat>, one, written as one word) (j:pi/khat) (r:zd:12264) (q:draft, low confidence)
pikkha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:nature/media) (w:gore/be gored) (d:<pik>, gore, with the particle <kha>, happen to: of a bull, strike and wound with the horn) (j:pik/kha) (r:zd:11870/zd:11927) (q:draft)
pilna sangpi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:higher education/advanced learning) (d:<pilna>, knowledge, and <sangpi>, very high: learning of a high level, such as a university education; the object of <nei>, have, <sin>, study, or <zo>, complete) (r:zd:11571/zd:10725) (q:draft)
pilna siamna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:knowledge and skill/learning/education) (d:<pilna>, knowledge, and <siamna>, skill, said together as one thing without <leh>: learning, what a person knows and is able to do) (r:zd:21120/zd:20979) (q:draft)
pilna sin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education) (w:study/get an education/go to school) (d:<pilna>, knowledge, and <sin>, learn: the usual expression for being at school or university, to study; the place stands before it with <ah>) (r:zd:9250/zd:11163/zd:16779) (q:draft)
pilna sinna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:education/schooling/study) (d:<pilna>, knowledge, and <sinna>, learning: the gaining of knowledge by study, education in general) (r:zd:23590/zd:24252/zd:21780) (q:draft)
Pilot = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/work) (w:pilot) (d:the person who flies an aircraft, in Zolai <vanlenghawl>, often written beside it) (s:vanlenghawl) (o:English) (r:zd:20680/zd:20248/zd:17846) (q:draft)
pilsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:education) (w:already wise/already educated) (d:<pil>, wise, with <sa>, already: wise or learned from the start or by now; {a pilsa a suak} is one born already wise) (b:pil) (r:zd:23554/zd:24303) (q:draft)
pilsin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education) (w:study/learn/pursue education) (d:<pil>, wise, with <sin>, learn: study in order to gain knowledge, go through schooling; {pilsin na}, also written <pilsinna>, is education) (r:zd:16245/zd:16457/zd:20443) (q:draft)
pilsinna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:education/learning/study) (d:<pil>, learned, with <sinna>, learning: schooling and study, and after a subject a field of study) (r:zd:22341/zd:16245/zd:12778) (q:draft)
pilvaang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (j:pilvang) (r:zd:17951/zd:20045/zd:25165) (q:draft)
pilvangtak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:alertly/watchfully/carefully/wisely) (d:<pilvang>, be alert, with <tak>, which makes an adverb, mostly followed by <in>: in a watchful and careful way) (b:pilvang) (j:pilvang/tak) (r:zd:23629/zd:20875) (q:draft)
pilvanhuai = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/social) (w:calling for caution/to be wary of) (d:<pilvang> be alert with <huai>, needing to be done: something about which one must be watchful and careful) (s:kidophuai) (b:pilvang) (r:zd:20060/zd:11135) (q:draft)
Pimpih = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua) (f:travel) (w:Pimpih) (d:a Zomi village in the Tedim area of Chin State; after a personal name it tells the home village) (r:zd:16139/zd:25189) (q:draft)
pimuh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:esteem/regard highly/look up to) (d:see someone as great, hold in high regard; {ki pimuh} is think highly of oneself) (a:simmawh) (r:zd:23257/zd:23830/zd:24202) (q:draft)
pin = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:although/even though) (d:in {na pin}, a way of writing {napi-in}, from <napi>, although: placed after a verb, even though this is so) (r:zd:22441/ts:7051) (q:draft, low confidence)
Pingpong = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media) (w:table tennis/ping-pong) (d:the game of table tennis; {pingpong sat} is play table tennis) (o:English, ping-pong) (r:zd:21302) (q:draft, low confidence)
Pinlong = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:politics) (w:Panglong) (d:town in Shan State of Myanmar where the agreement of 1947 between the Burmese leaders and the hill peoples was signed; {Pinlong thuciamna} is the Panglong Agreement and {Pinlong Conference} the Panglong Conference. Also the name of a quarter of Kalaymyo) (r:zd:24336/zd:22586) (q:draft)
pipe = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/work) (w:pipe/water pipe) (d:a pipe that carries water to a town or house; <tui pipe> is a water pipe) (o:English) (r:zd:17215/zd:15855) (q:draft)
pipeline = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:pipeline) (d:a long line of pipes that carries water, gas or oil) (o:English) (r:zd:17335/zd:16391) (q:draft)
pipen = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:main/chief/foremost/most) (d:<pi>, great or chief, and <pen>, most, written as one word and placed after a noun or describing word: the main one, the most; {a kisam pipen} is the most needed) (j:pi/pen) (r:zd:15493/zd:12177/zd:24354) (q:draft)
pipi mah = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:even though/in spite of) (d:<pipi>, very, and <mah>, emphasis: placed after a negated verb or describing word, often followed by <in>, even while not, in spite of not; {neilo pipi mah in} is even though having nothing) (r:zd:10761/zd:16376/zd:25932) (q:draft)
pipite = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:very/great) (d:<pipi>, very, with the plural <te>, placed after a describing word of several persons or things: {minthang pipite} is the very famous ones, {na lian pipite} is very great things) (b:pipi) (r:zd:9453/zd:25174/zd:21052) (q:draft)
Pistol = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:pistol/handgun) (d:a small gun held in one hand; also {pistol thau}) (o:English) (r:zd:12603/zd:11698) (q:draft)
