sabak = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food/social) (w:piece of meat/meat portion) (d:a cut piece or share of <sa>, meat; at a feast people put pieces into each other’s mouths as a sign of affection, and {sabak kituhna} is a scramble for the shares) (r:zd:25393/zd:24932/zd:21815) (q:draft)
