saikhat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/everyday) (w:a shop/a stall) (d:<sai>, shop, and <khat> written as one word: a shop, a stall or an eating place) (j:sai/khat) (r:zd:19398/zd:13181/zd:13048) (q:draft)
saimai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/travel) (w:shop front/front of the shop) (d:<sai>, shop, and <mai>, front, written as one word: the front of a shop or restaurant; {saimai ah} is in front of the shop) (j:sai/mai) (r:zd:17560/zd:12696/zd:14523) (q:draft)
Saimual = (i:1) (t:name) (c:mountain/place) (f:travel/nature) (w:Saimual) (d:hill about 6500 feet high at the entrance of Tedim town, with a view over the town and a place of prayer) (r:zd:18266/zd:10866) (q:draft)
sain = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:<sa> as the marker of a completed state and <in> written as one word after a verb or describing word: in that state, while being so or doing so) (r:zd:16379/zd:23170) (q:draft, low confidence)
