saisai = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:hurriedly/busily/in a rush) (d:placed after a verb: the action is done in haste or with bustle; {kizen saisai} is busy and energetic) (r:zd:12267/zd:15615) (q:draft, low confidence)
saisung = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:shop/inside of a shop) (d:<sai>, shop, with <sung>, inside, written as one word: the inside of a shop, the shop premises; {saisung ah} is in the shop) (j:sai/sung) (r:zd:22282/zd:21659/zd:12754) (q:draft)
saite = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:shops/stalls) (d:<sai>, shop, with the plural <te>: shops, stalls or businesses) (b:sai) (r:zd:25068/zd:16197) (q:draft)
saite = (i:2) (t:n) (f:work/politics/media) (w:department/agency/authorities) (d:<sai>, be in charge of, with the plural <te>, placed after the name of a matter: the people or offices that deal with it, as in {thuthak saite}, news agencies, and {cidamna lam saite}, the health authorities) (b:sai) (r:ts:9048/ts:12053/zd:21066) (q:draft)
sakding = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:<sak> and <ding> written as one word after a verb: will make it happen, will do it for someone) (j:sak/ding) (r:zd:17668/zd:21837) (q:draft)
sakgawp = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:the causative <sak>, make or cause, and <gawp>, severely, written as one word after a verb: cause it badly or do it to someone with violence, as in {lauthawng sakgawp}, frighten badly, and {suksiat sakgawp}, wreck) (j:sak/gawp) (r:zd:14901/zd:17517/zd:20013) (q:draft)
sakha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:suppose/assume/take to be) (d:<sa>, here think or consider a thing to be so, with <kha>: happen to think, suppose, often wrongly; {sakha kei ni} is let us not suppose) (j:sa/kha) (r:zd:22361/zd:12121/zd:25628) (q:draft)
sakkha = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:cause by accident/happen to make) (d:the causative <sak> with <kha>, happen to, written as one word after a verb: bring something about without meaning to, or happen to do it to someone) (j:sak/kha) (r:zd:19712/zd:20871) (q:draft)
sakkhin = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:the causative <sak> and <khin>, already, written as one word after a verb: has already been made to happen, has already been done to someone) (j:sak/khin) (r:zd:15205/zd:11778) (q:draft)
sakkhop = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/religion/social) (w:sing together) (d:sing, as in {la sak}, sing a song, with <khop>, together, written as one word: sing a song together) (j:sak/khop) (r:zd:19168/zd:24217/zd:9225) (q:draft)
sakleh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:if) (d:<sak> and <leh>, if, written as one word after a verb: if one lets or makes it happen; after <ka>, when I think it so) (j:sak/leh) (r:zd:13144/zd:17060) (q:draft, low confidence)
saklo = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:the causative <sak> and <lo>, not, written as one word after a verb: not make, not let, not allow to happen) (j:sak/lo) (r:zd:17409/zd:19262/zd:23977) (q:draft)
sakloh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not cause/not let/not consider) (d:<sak> and the negative <loh> written as one word after a verb: not cause or not let it happen, as in {nawngkai sakloh}, not to trouble; after a describing word it is the form of <sa>, deem, as in {kilawm i sakloh}, we do not think it fitting) (j:sak/loh) (r:zd:8668/zd:14946/zd:21049) (q:draft)
saklohna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:not feeling/not considering) (d:<sak>, here the form of <sa> in its sense feel or consider to be, with <lohna>: the fact of not finding something to be so, placed after a describing word; {nop saklohna} is not feeling happy, {dik saklohna} is not thinking something right) (r:zd:22474/zd:20956) (q:draft)
Sakollam = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel) (w:Sakollam) (d:a ward of the town of Tedim in Chin State) (r:zd:23205/zd:17530) (q:draft)
sakpah = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:the causative <sak> and <pah>, at once, written as one word after a verb: have it done at once; {kipuak sakpah} is was sent at once) (j:sak/pah) (r:zd:18036/zd:17856) (q:draft)
sakphot = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:the causative <sak> and <phot>, for the time being, written as one word after a verb: have something done for now, temporarily; {khakcip sakphot} is have it closed for the time being) (j:sak/phot) (r:zd:17622/zd:17707) (q:draft)
saksawm = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:intend to make/try to have done) (d:<sak> and <sawm> written as one word after a verb: intend or try to make someone do the action, or to have it done) (j:sak/sawm) (r:zd:15467/zd:12331/zd:20263) (q:draft)
sakthei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:can cause/be able to make) (d:causative <sak> and <thei>, able, written as one word after a verb: can make it happen, can cause to) (j:sak/thei) (r:zd:17262/zd:16415) (q:draft)
saktuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:each feel/each find) (d:<sak> and <tuak>, each, written as one word after a word of feeling: each of them feels or finds it so, {lamdang saktuak} is each finds it strange; after a verb of doing, each side does it to the other) (j:sak/tuak) (r:zd:15727/zd:16657/zd:11746) (q:draft, low confidence)
saktuam = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:the causative <sak> and <tuam> written as one word after a verb or describing word: make it so as a further result, cause it all the more; {ziakai saktuam} is cause yet more delay) (j:sak/tuam) (r:zd:15469/zd:20122/zd:23311) (q:draft, low confidence)
sakzo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be able to make/can cause) (d:<sak> and <zo> written as one word after a verb: be able to make that happen, as in {kikhel sakzo}, can make something change) (j:sak/zo) (r:zd:19947/zd:24276/zd:15275) (q:draft)
