sawl = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:send) (d:make someone go to a place or a person, with a task or a message) (s:puak/paisak) (r:55.4.12) (q:draft)
sawlsawl = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:keep telling/urge repeatedly/order again and again) (d:<sawl> said twice: tell or order someone to do something again and again) (b:sawl) (r:zd:24244/zd:23990/zd:19166) (q:draft)
sawm hamtang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:make a point of/try hard to/be determined to) (d:<sawm.2>, intend, and <hamtang>, insistently: placed after a verb, make a determined effort to do it; with <in> or <ni> at the end it is a strong advice, be sure to do it; <sawm> is here not the number ten) (r:zd:26252/zd:11702/zd:23886) (q:draft)
sawmleh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:if one intends to/if planning to) (d:<sawm>, intend, and <leh>, if, written as one word after a verb: if one means to do it) (j:sawm/leh) (r:zd:24135/zd:20747) (q:draft)
sawmleh = (i:2) (t:num) (f:everyday) (w:ten and) (d:<sawm>, ten, and <leh>, and, written as one word in the numbers eleven to nineteen: {sawmleh nih} is twelve) (j:sawm/leh) (r:zd:19679/zd:15274) (q:draft)
sawmlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not intend/not plan/not try) (d:<sawm>, intend, with <lo>, not, written as one word after a verb: not intend or not try to do it; {piak sawmlo} is not intend to give) (j:sawm/lo) (r:zd:12096/zd:14755) (q:draft)
